LC.course={"slug":"learnbangla","domain":"learnbangla.zyeemzia.com","title":"Learn Bangla","native":"সহজে বাংলা শিখি","tagline":"Easy Bangla for English speakers: read the script, speak with people, enjoy the culture.","lang":"Bangla","langNative":"বাংলা","voice":"bn-BD","htmlLang":"bn","cjk":false,"mark":"অ","greeting":"নমস্কার / আসসালামু আলাইকুম","greetingMeaning":"Hello (two common greetings)","alphabetTitle":"Bangla Script","alphabetShort":"Script","alphabetIntro":"Vowels, consonants, vowel signs and conjuncts. Tap any letter to hear it and see how it is used.","rootsLabel":"Word families","hanzi":false,"wish":{"t":"অভিনন্দন!","mean":"Congratulations!"},"pdf":"Learn-Bangla-Book.pdf","accent":"#0b7a4b","fontsCss":"family=Hind+Siliguri:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Figtree:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Reem+Kufi:wght@600;700","targetFont":"\"Hind Siliguri\", \"Noto Sans Bengali\", \"Nirmala UI\", sans-serif"};
LC.alphabet={"groups":[{"id":"vowels","label":"Vowels (স্বরবর্ণ)","note":"11 vowel letters. Inside a word each one (except অ) becomes a vowel sign, shown as its second form."},{"id":"consonants","label":"Consonants (ব্যঞ্জনবর্ণ)","note":"35 consonant letters in the standard order. The last four of the 39 (ৎ ং ঃ ঁ) are under Special signs."},{"id":"signs","label":"Special signs","note":"ৎ ং ঃ ঁ (the last four consonants) and the হসন্ত, which removes a vowel."},{"id":"numerals","label":"Numerals (সংখ্যা)","note":"The digits 0 to 9, used just like 0–9 in English."}],"items":[{"id":"o","ch":"অ","name":"shoro o","say":"অ","tr":"o","group":"vowels","sound":"A short, rounded o, like the 'o' in British 'hot' or the 'aw' in 'saw'. This sound also hides inside every consonant.","example":{"t":"অনেক","tr":"onek","mean":"many"},"tip":"অ has no vowel sign: it is the hidden vowel in ক (ko), খ (kho) and the rest."},{"id":"aa","ch":"আ","name":"shoro a","say":"আ","tr":"a","group":"vowels","sound":"An open a, like the 'a' in 'father', but short.","example":{"t":"আম","tr":"am","mean":"mango"},"tip":"আ is অ plus one straight line.","alt":"া"},{"id":"i","ch":"ই","name":"hrosho i","say":"ই","tr":"i","group":"vowels","sound":"Like the 'ee' in 'see', but short.","example":{"t":"ইঁদুর","tr":"indur","mean":"mouse"},"tip":"'hrosho' means short.","alt":"ি"},{"id":"ii","ch":"ঈ","name":"dirgho i","say":"ঈ","tr":"i","group":"vowels","sound":"The same sound as ই in everyday speech. Only the spelling is different.","example":{"t":"ঈগল","tr":"igol","mean":"eagle"},"tip":"'dirgho' means long.","alt":"ী"},{"id":"u","ch":"উ","name":"hrosho u","say":"উ","tr":"u","group":"vowels","sound":"Like the 'oo' in 'food', but short.","example":{"t":"উট","tr":"ut","mean":"camel"},"alt":"ু"},{"id":"uu","ch":"ঊ","name":"dirgho u","say":"ঊ","tr":"u","group":"vowels","sound":"The same sound as উ in everyday speech. Only the spelling is different.","example":{"t":"ঊষা","tr":"usha","mean":"dawn"},"alt":"ূ"},{"id":"ri","ch":"ঋ","name":"ri","say":"ঋ","tr":"ri","group":"vowels","sound":"Said 'ri', as in 'rich'. It is rare and mostly found in words from Sanskrit.","example":{"t":"ঋতু","tr":"ritu","mean":"season"},"alt":"ৃ"},{"id":"e","ch":"এ","name":"e","say":"এ","tr":"e","group":"vowels","sound":"Like the 'e' in 'bed', or the 'a' in 'say' without the glide. In some words it opens to the 'a' of 'cat'.","example":{"t":"এলাচ","tr":"elach","mean":"cardamom"},"alt":"ে"},{"id":"oi","ch":"ঐ","name":"oi","say":"ঐ","tr":"oi","group":"vowels","sound":"Like the 'oy' in 'boy'.","example":{"t":"ঐক্য","tr":"oikko","mean":"unity"},"alt":"ৈ"},{"id":"oh","ch":"ও","name":"o","say":"ও","tr":"o","group":"vowels","sound":"Like the 'o' in 'go', but pure, with no 'w' sound at the end.","example":{"t":"ওজন","tr":"ojon","mean":"weight"},"alt":"ো"},{"id":"ou","ch":"ঔ","name":"ou","say":"ঔ","tr":"ou","group":"vowels","sound":"o and u glided together, a bit like the 'ow' in 'show'.","example":{"t":"ঔষধ","tr":"oushodh","mean":"medicine"},"alt":"ৌ"},{"id":"ka","ch":"ক","name":"ko","say":"ক","tr":"ko","group":"consonants","sound":"An unaspirated k, with no puff of air, like the k in 'skin'.","example":{"t":"কলা","tr":"kola","mean":"banana"},"tip":"Hold a tissue in front of your lips: it stays still for ক and flutters for খ."},{"id":"kha","ch":"খ","name":"kho","say":"খ","tr":"kho","group":"consonants","sound":"k with a strong puff of air, like the k in 'kite' said with extra breath.","example":{"t":"খরগোশ","tr":"khorgosh","mean":"rabbit"}},{"id":"ga","ch":"গ","name":"go","say":"গ","tr":"go","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the g in 'go'.","example":{"t":"গরু","tr":"goru","mean":"cow"}},{"id":"gha","ch":"ঘ","name":"gho","say":"ঘ","tr":"gho","group":"consonants","sound":"A breathy g, like the 'g-h' in 'doghouse' said quickly.","example":{"t":"ঘর","tr":"ghor","mean":"room, house"}},{"id":"nga","ch":"ঙ","name":"umo","say":"ঙ","tr":"ng","group":"consonants","sound":"The 'ng' in 'sing'. It never starts a word.","example":{"t":"ব্যাঙ","tr":"bang","mean":"frog"},"tip":"Its traditional name is said 'umo' (some say 'ungo')."},{"id":"cha","ch":"চ","name":"cho","say":"চ","tr":"cho","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the ch in 'church', but with no puff of air.","example":{"t":"চা","tr":"cha","mean":"tea"}},{"id":"chha","ch":"ছ","name":"chho","say":"ছ","tr":"chho","group":"consonants","sound":"ch with a strong puff of air.","example":{"t":"ছাতা","tr":"chhata","mean":"umbrella"}},{"id":"ja","ch":"জ","name":"jo","say":"জ","tr":"jo","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the j in 'jam'.","example":{"t":"জাহাজ","tr":"jahaj","mean":"ship"}},{"id":"jha","ch":"ঝ","name":"jho","say":"ঝ","tr":"jho","group":"consonants","sound":"A breathy j, like the 'dg-h' in 'hedgehog' said quickly.","example":{"t":"ঝড়","tr":"jhor","mean":"storm"}},{"id":"nya","ch":"ঞ","name":"inyo","say":"ঞ","tr":"n","group":"consonants","sound":"A nasal n. On its own it is rare; it mostly joins চ or জ, as in পঞ্চাশ.","example":{"t":"পঞ্চাশ","tr":"ponchash","mean":"fifty"}},{"id":"tta","ch":"ট","name":"to","say":"ট","tr":"to","group":"consonants","sound":"A t with the tongue tip curled back to touch the roof of the mouth. English t is close to it.","example":{"t":"টাকা","tr":"taka","mean":"money (taka)"}},{"id":"ttha","ch":"ঠ","name":"tho","say":"ঠ","tr":"tho","group":"consonants","sound":"The curled-back t with a puff of air.","example":{"t":"ঠান্ডা","tr":"thanda","mean":"cold"}},{"id":"dda","ch":"ড","name":"do","say":"ড","tr":"do","group":"consonants","sound":"A d with the tongue tip curled back. English d is close to it.","example":{"t":"ডিম","tr":"dim","mean":"egg"}},{"id":"ddha","ch":"ঢ","name":"dho","say":"ঢ","tr":"dho","group":"consonants","sound":"The curled-back d with a breath of air.","example":{"t":"ঢাকা","tr":"dhaka","mean":"Dhaka (the capital)"}},{"id":"nna","ch":"ণ","name":"murdhonno no","say":"ণ","tr":"no","group":"consonants","sound":"Sounds the same as ন (n) in modern Bangla. It is a spelling letter.","example":{"t":"হরিণ","tr":"horin","mean":"deer"},"tip":"Spelling names: ণ is 'murdhonno no', ন is 'dontto no'."},{"id":"ta","ch":"ত","name":"to","say":"ত","tr":"to","group":"consonants","sound":"A soft t: the tongue tip touches the back of the top front teeth, like t in Spanish or French.","example":{"t":"তারা","tr":"tara","mean":"star"},"tip":"ত (tongue on teeth) and ট (tongue curled back) are different letters with different sounds."},{"id":"tha","ch":"থ","name":"tho","say":"থ","tr":"tho","group":"consonants","sound":"The soft teeth-t with a puff of air. It is not the 'th' of 'think'.","example":{"t":"থালা","tr":"thala","mean":"plate"}},{"id":"da","ch":"দ","name":"do","say":"দ","tr":"do","group":"consonants","sound":"A soft d with the tongue on the back of the top teeth, like d in Spanish.","example":{"t":"দরজা","tr":"dorja","mean":"door"}},{"id":"dha","ch":"ধ","name":"dho","say":"ধ","tr":"dho","group":"consonants","sound":"The soft teeth-d with a breath of air. It is not the 'th' of 'this'.","example":{"t":"ধান","tr":"dhan","mean":"rice plant"}},{"id":"na","ch":"ন","name":"dontto no","say":"ন","tr":"no","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the n in 'no'.","example":{"t":"নদী","tr":"nodi","mean":"river"}},{"id":"pa","ch":"প","name":"po","say":"প","tr":"po","group":"consonants","sound":"p with no puff of air, like the p in 'spin'.","example":{"t":"পাখি","tr":"pakhi","mean":"bird"}},{"id":"pha","ch":"ফ","name":"pho","say":"ফ","tr":"pho","group":"consonants","sound":"p with a puff of air. Many speakers say it like English f.","example":{"t":"ফুল","tr":"phul","mean":"flower"}},{"id":"ba","ch":"ব","name":"bo","say":"ব","tr":"bo","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the b in 'boy'.","example":{"t":"বই","tr":"boi","mean":"book"}},{"id":"bha","ch":"ভ","name":"bho","say":"ভ","tr":"bho","group":"consonants","sound":"A breathy b, like the 'b-h' in 'clubhouse' said quickly. Some speakers say it close to v.","example":{"t":"ভাত","tr":"bhat","mean":"cooked rice"}},{"id":"ma","ch":"ম","name":"mo","say":"ম","tr":"mo","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the m in 'mother'.","example":{"t":"মা","tr":"ma","mean":"mother"}},{"id":"ya","ch":"য","name":"ontostho jo","say":"য","tr":"jo","group":"consonants","sound":"Sounds like j in 'jam', just like জ.","example":{"t":"যখন","tr":"jokhon","mean":"when"}},{"id":"ra","ch":"র","name":"ro","say":"র","tr":"ro","group":"consonants","sound":"A quick tapped r: flick the tongue once against the ridge behind the top teeth.","example":{"t":"রুটি","tr":"ruti","mean":"flatbread"},"tip":"র is ব with a dot below."},{"id":"la","ch":"ল","name":"lo","say":"ল","tr":"lo","group":"consonants","sound":"A clear l, like the l in 'leaf'.","example":{"t":"লাল","tr":"lal","mean":"red"}},{"id":"sha","ch":"শ","name":"talobbo sho","say":"শ","tr":"sho","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the sh in 'shop'.","example":{"t":"শাপলা","tr":"shapla","mean":"water lily"}},{"id":"ssha","ch":"ষ","name":"murdhonno sho","say":"ষ","tr":"sho","group":"consonants","sound":"Also 'sh', just like শ. It appears mostly in formal or older words.","example":{"t":"ষাঁড়","tr":"shar","mean":"bull"}},{"id":"sa","ch":"স","name":"dontto sho","say":"স","tr":"sho","group":"consonants","sound":"Usually 'sh' too. It sounds like s in some clusters, such as স্ত, স্প and স্ক.","example":{"t":"সাপ","tr":"shap","mean":"snake"}},{"id":"ha","ch":"হ","name":"ho","say":"হ","tr":"ho","group":"consonants","sound":"Like the h in 'house'.","example":{"t":"হাতি","tr":"hati","mean":"elephant"}},{"id":"ra-dot","ch":"ড়","name":"doye shunno ro","say":"ড়","tr":"ro","group":"consonants","sound":"A flapped r: curl the tongue back, then flick it forward. It never starts a word.","example":{"t":"পাহাড়","tr":"pahar","mean":"hill"},"tip":"ড় is ড with a dot below."},{"id":"rha-dot","ch":"ঢ়","name":"dhoye shunno ro","say":"ঢ়","tr":"rho","group":"consonants","sound":"The flapped ড় with a little breath. Rare, and it never starts a word.","example":{"t":"আষাঢ়","tr":"ashar","mean":"Asharh (a month of the Bangla year)"}},{"id":"ya-dot","ch":"য়","name":"ontostho o","say":"য়","tr":"y","group":"consonants","sound":"A soft glide like the y in 'yes', or a vowel sound between vowels. It never starts a word.","example":{"t":"মেয়ে","tr":"meye","mean":"girl"},"tip":"য় is য with a dot below."},{"id":"khanda-ta","ch":"ৎ","name":"khondo to","say":"ৎ","tr":"t","group":"signs","sound":"A t with no vowel after it. It only comes at the end of a syllable.","example":{"t":"হঠাৎ","tr":"hothat","mean":"suddenly"},"tip":"Counted as one of the 39 consonants."},{"id":"anusvar","ch":"ং","name":"onushshar","say":"ং","tr":"ng","group":"signs","sound":"Adds 'ng' (as in 'sing') after a vowel.","example":{"t":"রং","tr":"rong","mean":"colour"},"tip":"Counted as one of the 39 consonants."},{"id":"bisarga","ch":"ঃ","name":"bisorgo","say":"ঃ","tr":"h","group":"signs","sound":"Inside a word it doubles the next consonant; at the end of a word it adds a light h.","example":{"t":"দুঃখ","tr":"dukkho","mean":"sadness"},"tip":"Counted as one of the 39 consonants. Do not mix it up with the colon (:)."},{"id":"chandrabindu","ch":"ঁ","name":"chondrobindu","say":"ঁ","tr":"nasal","group":"signs","sound":"Makes the vowel nasal: let air flow through your nose as you say it.","example":{"t":"চাঁদ","tr":"chand","mean":"moon"},"tip":"Its name means 'moon and dot', and that is how it looks."},{"id":"hasanta","ch":"্","name":"hoshonto","say":"্","tr":"no vowel","group":"signs","sound":"Removes the hidden o, so the consonant has no vowel. Usually the letters then join into a conjunct.","example":{"t":"শক্ত","tr":"shokto","mean":"hard, strong"},"tip":"In শক্ত the হসন্ত is hidden inside the joined letters ক্ত (ক্ + ত)."},{"id":"num-0","ch":"০","name":"shunno","say":"শূন্য","tr":"shunno","group":"numerals","sound":"Say শূন্য 'shunno'. The word also means 'empty'.","example":{"t":"শূন্য","tr":"shunno","mean":"zero"}},{"id":"num-1","ch":"১","name":"ek","say":"এক","tr":"ek","group":"numerals","sound":"Say এক 'ek'; the e is open, close to the 'a' in 'back'.","example":{"t":"একটি আম","tr":"ekti am","mean":"one mango"}},{"id":"num-2","ch":"২","name":"dui","say":"দুই","tr":"dui","group":"numerals","sound":"Say দুই 'dui', like 'doo-ee'.","example":{"t":"দুটি পাখি","tr":"duti pakhi","mean":"two birds"}},{"id":"num-3","ch":"৩","name":"tin","say":"তিন","tr":"tin","group":"numerals","sound":"Say তিন 'tin', with the soft teeth-t.","example":{"t":"তিনটি ফুল","tr":"tinti phul","mean":"three flowers"}},{"id":"num-4","ch":"৪","name":"char","say":"চার","tr":"char","group":"numerals","sound":"Say চার 'char'.","example":{"t":"চারটি কলা","tr":"charti kola","mean":"four bananas"},"tip":"It looks like an English 8, but it means 4!"},{"id":"num-5","ch":"৫","name":"panch","say":"পাঁচ","tr":"panch","group":"numerals","sound":"Say পাঁচ 'panch', with a nasal a.","example":{"t":"পাঁচ আঙুল","tr":"panch angul","mean":"five fingers"}},{"id":"num-6","ch":"৬","name":"chhoy","say":"ছয়","tr":"chhoy","group":"numerals","sound":"Say ছয় 'chhoy'.","example":{"t":"ছয় ঋতু","tr":"chhoy ritu","mean":"six seasons"},"tip":"Bangladesh has six seasons (ছয় ঋতু)."},{"id":"num-7","ch":"৭","name":"shat","say":"সাত","tr":"shat","group":"numerals","sound":"Say সাত 'shat'.","example":{"t":"সাত দিন","tr":"shat din","mean":"seven days"}},{"id":"num-8","ch":"৮","name":"at","say":"আট","tr":"at","group":"numerals","sound":"Say আট 'at', with the curled-back t.","example":{"t":"আট টাকা","tr":"at taka","mean":"eight taka"}},{"id":"num-9","ch":"৯","name":"noy","say":"নয়","tr":"noy","group":"numerals","sound":"Say নয় 'noy', rhyming with 'boy'.","example":{"t":"নয়টি ডিম","tr":"noyti dim","mean":"nine eggs"}}]};
LC.units.push({"id":"script","order":1,"icon":"অ","color":"teal","title":"Bangla Script","subtitle":"Vowels, consonants, vowel signs, conjuncts and numerals","lessons":[{"id":"u1-how-script-works","icon":"অ","title":"How Bangla Script Works","subtitle":"Direction, the headline and the hidden vowel","minutes":10,"goals":["Know which way Bangla is written","Spot the মাত্রা (headline)","Understand the hidden vowel অ"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Welcome! Bangla script looks beautiful and a little mysterious at first. Good news: it follows clear rules. Let's see how it works before learning single letters."},{"type":"text","text":"Bangla is written **left to right**, just like English. There are **no capital letters**, so each letter has only one form, even at the start of a name.","title":"Left to right, no capitals"},{"type":"text","text":"Most letters hang from a straight line on top called the {{মাত্রা}} (matra). When letters join into a word, their headlines join too, so the whole word sits under one long line.","title":"The headline"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"কলম","tr":"kolom","mean":"pen"},{"t":"বাবা","tr":"baba","mean":"father"},{"t":"আকাশ","tr":"akash","mean":"sky"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Think of the matra as a washing line: the letters are clothes hanging from it."},{"type":"text","text":"Every consonant carries a built-in vowel sound, {{অ}} (said 'o'). So {{ক}} on its own is 'ko', not just 'k'. For a different vowel you add a small **vowel sign** to the consonant.","title":"The hidden vowel"},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ক","label":"ko","desc":"The consonant alone has the hidden o sound."},{"t":"কা","label":"ka","desc":"Add the sign া and it says 'ka'."},{"t":"কি","label":"ki","desc":"Add the sign ি and it says 'ki'. This sign is written before ক!"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"The hidden o often goes quiet","color":"orange","desc":"At the end of a word the hidden o is usually silent. In some words it is said. You learn each word by hearing it.","how":"কলম ends in 'm', but বড় (big) ends in 'ro'.","examples":[{"t":"কলম","tr":"kolom","hl":"ম"},{"t":"আম","tr":"am","hl":"ম"},{"t":"বড়","tr":"boro","hl":"ড়"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Feature","English","Bangla"],"rows":[["Direction","Left to right","Left to right"],["Capital letters","Yes","No"],["Vowels in words","Full letters","Mostly small vowel signs"],["Line on top","No","Yes: the {{মাত্রা}}"],["Full stop","A dot (.)","An upright line ({{।}})"]]},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"The Bangla full stop is a small upright line {{।}} called {{দাঁড়ি}} (dari)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Tap each word, listen, and notice the headline running across the top.","lines":["কলম","বাবা","আকাশ","মা","আম"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Which way is Bangla written?","options":["Right to left","Left to right","Top to bottom only"],"answer":1},{"q":"What is the {{মাত্রা}} (matra)?","options":["A dot under a letter","The line on top","A capital letter","The full stop sign"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say {{ক}} on its own?","say":"ক","options":["k","ka","ki","ko"],"answer":3},{"q":"Does Bangla have capital letters?","options":["Yes, for names","Only at the start of a sentence","No, never"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which mark is the Bangla full stop?","options":["।",".","ঃ","-"],"answer":0},{"q":"In {{কলম}}, do you say the hidden o after the last letter ম?","options":["No, it is silent","Yes, we say 'kolomo'","Only in poems and songs"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u1-vowels","icon":"আ","title":"The 11 Vowels","subtitle":"স্বরবর্ণ: the vowel letters","minutes":12,"goals":["Recognise all 11 vowel letters","Say each vowel sound","Know when full vowel letters are used"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangla has **11 vowel letters** ({{স্বরবর্ণ}}). You use a full vowel letter when a word **starts** with a vowel, or when a vowel follows another vowel."},{"type":"letters","items":["o","aa","i","ii","u","uu","ri","e","oi","oh","ou"]},{"type":"text","text":"{{ই}} / {{ঈ}} and {{উ}} / {{ঊ}} are called 'short' and 'long', but in everyday speech each pair sounds the same. The difference is only in spelling.","title":"Short and long"},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ই","label":"hrosho i","desc":"Short i: sounds like 'ee'."},{"t":"ঈ","label":"dirgho i","desc":"Long i: the same sound today."},{"t":"উ","label":"hrosho u","desc":"Short u: sounds like 'oo'."},{"t":"ঊ","label":"dirgho u","desc":"Long u: the same sound today."}]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"অ","label":"o (open)","desc":"Like 'aw' in 'saw', but short."},{"t":"ও","label":"o (closed)","desc":"Like 'o' in 'go', with no 'w' at the end."}],"title":"Two kinds of o"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"অ and আ are twins: আ is অ plus one extra straight line."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"অনেক","tr":"onek","mean":"many","hl":"অ"},{"t":"আম","tr":"am","mean":"mango","hl":"আ"},{"t":"ইঁদুর","tr":"indur","mean":"mouse","hl":"ই"},{"t":"উট","tr":"ut","mean":"camel","hl":"উ"},{"t":"ঋতু","tr":"ritu","mean":"season","hl":"ঋ"},{"t":"এলাচ","tr":"elach","mean":"cardamom","hl":"এ"},{"t":"ওজন","tr":"ojon","mean":"weight","hl":"ও"},{"t":"ঔষধ","tr":"oushodh","mean":"medicine","hl":"ঔ"}],"title":"Words that start with a vowel"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"{{ঋ}} is said 'ri'. It is rare and mostly appears in words from Sanskrit, like {{ঋতু}} (season)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read each line aloud. Tap to check.","lines":["অ আ ই ঈ উ ঊ","ঋ এ ঐ ও ঔ","আম ইঁদুর উট","ঋতু এলাচ ওজন"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Listen. Which vowel do you hear?","say":"আ","options":["আ","অ","ও","এ"],"answer":0},{"q":"How many vowel letters does Bangla have?","options":["26","7","11","50"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which pair sounds the same in everyday speech?","options":["ই and ঈ","অ and আ","এ and ঐ","ও and ঔ"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which vowel is said 'oi', as in 'boy'?","say":"ঐ","options":["ঔ","ঐ","এ","ই"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which word starts with a vowel letter?","options":["উট","কলা","মা","বই"],"answer":0},{"q":"How is {{ঋ}} usually said?","options":["ri","oo","ee","ar"],"answer":0},{"q":"When do you use a full vowel letter like {{আ}}?","options":["After every consonant","Only in the names of people","Only at the end of a sentence","At the start of a word"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u1-ka-cha-rows","icon":"ক","title":"Consonants 1: ক-row and চ-row","subtitle":"Back of the mouth and roof of the mouth","minutes":14,"goals":["Learn the pattern of a consonant row","Read ক খ গ ঘ ঙ and চ ছ জ ঝ ঞ","Hear the puff of air in aspirated letters"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Consonants ({{ব্যঞ্জনবর্ণ}}) come in neat rows of five called {{বর্গ}} (borgo). Learn the pattern once and you can predict the sounds of a whole row."},{"type":"table","head":["Place","Sound type","ক-row","চ-row"],"rows":[["1","plain","{{ক}} ko","{{চ}} cho"],["2","plain + puff of air","{{খ}} kho","{{ছ}} chho"],["3","voiced","{{গ}} go","{{জ}} jo"],["4","voiced + breath","{{ঘ}} gho","{{ঝ}} jho"],["5","nasal","{{ঙ}} umo","{{ঞ}} inyo"]],"title":"The pattern of every row"},{"type":"text","text":"The {{ক}}-row ({{ক-বর্গ}}) is made at the back of the mouth, like English k and g.","title":"ক-বর্গ"},{"type":"letters","items":["ka","kha","ga","gha","nga"]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ক","label":"ko","desc":"No puff of air: like the k in 'skin'."},{"t":"খ","label":"kho","desc":"A strong puff: like the k in 'kite', with extra breath."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Hold a tissue in front of your lips. It should stay still for {{ক}} and flutter for {{খ}}."},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"{{ঙ}} never starts a word. You meet it in the middle or at the end, as in {{ব্যাঙ}} (frog)."},{"type":"text","text":"The {{চ}}-row ({{চ-বর্গ}}) is made with the tongue pressed against the roof of the mouth, close to English ch and j.","title":"চ-বর্গ"},{"type":"letters","items":["cha","chha","ja","jha","nya"]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{ঞ}} likes to hide in pairs such as {{ঞ্চ}} and {{ঞ্জ}}, as in {{পঞ্চাশ}} (fifty)."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"কলা","tr":"kola","mean":"banana","hl":"ক"},{"t":"খরগোশ","tr":"khorgosh","mean":"rabbit","hl":"খ"},{"t":"গরু","tr":"goru","mean":"cow","hl":"গ"},{"t":"ঘর","tr":"ghor","mean":"room, house","hl":"ঘ"},{"t":"চা","tr":"cha","mean":"tea","hl":"চ"},{"t":"ছাতা","tr":"chhata","mean":"umbrella","hl":"ছ"},{"t":"জাহাজ","tr":"jahaj","mean":"ship","hl":"জ"},{"t":"ঝড়","tr":"jhor","mean":"storm","hl":"ঝ"}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the rows, then the words.","lines":["ক খ গ ঘ ঙ","চ ছ জ ঝ ঞ","কলা খরগোশ গরু ঘর","চা ছাতা জাহাজ ঝড়"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Listen. Which letter is it?","say":"খ","options":["ক","গ","ঘ","খ"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which letter has a puff of air?","options":["ছ","চ","জ","ঙ"],"answer":0},{"q":"What does {{চা}} mean?","say":"চা","options":["water","tea","rice","milk"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which letter is the nasal of the ক-row?","options":["ঙ","ঞ","গ","ন"],"answer":0},{"q":"How many letters are in one {{বর্গ}} (row)?","options":["3","4","10","5"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{ঘ}} sounds like…","options":["g + breath, as in 'doghouse'","k with no puff of air, as in 'skin'","'ng' as in 'sing'","'j' as in 'jam'"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u1-ta-rows","icon":"ট","title":"Consonants 2: Two Kinds of T and D","subtitle":"ট-row (tongue curled back) and ত-row (tongue on teeth)","minutes":15,"goals":["Read ট ঠ ড ঢ ণ and ত থ দ ধ ন","Hear curled-back vs teeth sounds","Avoid the English 'th' trap"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"These two rows are the trickiest for English speakers, because Bangla has **two kinds of t and d**. Take it slowly; your ear will learn."},{"type":"text","text":"For the {{ট}}-row ({{ট-বর্গ}}), curl the tip of your tongue back and touch the roof of your mouth behind the gum ridge. English t and d are quite close to these.","title":"Tongue curled back"},{"type":"letters","items":["tta","ttha","dda","ddha","nna"]},{"type":"text","text":"For the {{ত}}-row ({{ত-বর্গ}}), touch the back of your top front teeth with the tip of your tongue. The sound is softer, like t and d in Spanish or French.","title":"Tongue on the teeth"},{"type":"letters","items":["ta","tha","da","dha","na"]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ট","label":"to (curled)","desc":"Tongue curled back. Close to English t."},{"t":"ত","label":"to (teeth)","desc":"Tongue on the teeth. Softer than English t."},{"t":"ড","label":"do (curled)","desc":"Tongue curled back. Close to English d."},{"t":"দ","label":"do (teeth)","desc":"Tongue on the teeth, like Spanish d."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"{{থ}} and {{ধ}} are **not** the 'th' of 'think' or 'this'. They are the soft teeth-t and teeth-d with a puff of breath."},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{ণ}} and {{ন}} sound the same today. {{ণ}} is just a spelling letter, as in {{হরিণ}} (deer)."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"টাকা","tr":"taka","mean":"money","hl":"ট"},{"t":"ঠান্ডা","tr":"thanda","mean":"cold","hl":"ঠ"},{"t":"ডিম","tr":"dim","mean":"egg","hl":"ড"},{"t":"ঢাকা","tr":"dhaka","mean":"Dhaka","hl":"ঢ"},{"t":"তারা","tr":"tara","mean":"star","hl":"ত"},{"t":"থালা","tr":"thala","mean":"plate","hl":"থ"},{"t":"দরজা","tr":"dorja","mean":"door","hl":"দ"},{"t":"ধান","tr":"dhan","mean":"rice plant","hl":"ধ"},{"t":"নদী","tr":"nodi","mean":"river","hl":"ন"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"The money of Bangladesh is the taka ({{টাকা}}). Its sign is {{৳}}. Dhaka ({{ঢাকা}}) is the capital."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read in pairs. Feel where your tongue goes.","lines":["ট ত","ড দ","ঠ থ","ঢ ধ","টাকা তারা ডিম দরজা"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Where does your tongue go for {{ত}}?","options":["On the back of the top teeth","Curled back to the roof of the mouth","Down behind the bottom teeth","Between the lips"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which letter is closest to English 'd'?","options":["দ","ড","ধ","ঢ"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Which word do you hear?","say":"ঢাকা","options":["ঢাকা","টাকা","ডাকা","থাকা"],"answer":0},{"q":"Is {{থ}} like the 'th' in 'think'?","options":["Yes, exactly the same","Yes, but a little longer","Only at the end of words","No: it is t with a puff"],"answer":3},{"q":"What does {{নদী}} mean?","say":"নদী","options":["river","door","money","plate"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which two letters sound the same today?","options":["ট and ত","ণ and ন","ড and দ","থ and ঠ"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u1-pa-row","icon":"প","title":"Consonants 3: প-row, য র ল","subtitle":"Lip sounds and three smooth letters","minutes":12,"goals":["Read প ফ ব ভ ম","Read য র ল","Tell ব and র apart"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"The {{প}}-row ({{প-বর্গ}}) is made with the lips, like English p, b and m. Then come three smooth letters: {{য}}, {{র}} and {{ল}}."},{"type":"letters","items":["pa","pha","ba","bha","ma"]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"প","label":"po","desc":"Lips together, no puff of air."},{"t":"ফ","label":"pho / fo","desc":"With a puff. Many people say it like English f."},{"t":"ব","label":"bo","desc":"Like English b."},{"t":"ভ","label":"bho","desc":"b + breath, like 'clubhouse' said fast."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"{{ফুল}} (flower) is said 'phul' or 'ful'. You will hear both in Bangladesh."},{"type":"text","text":"{{য}} sounds like {{জ}} (j). {{র}} is a quick tapped r: flick the tongue once, as in Spanish 'pero'. {{ল}} is like English l, light and clear.","title":"য, র and ল"},{"type":"letters","items":["ya","ra","la"]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{র}} is {{ব}} with a dot underneath. Same shape, different letter!"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"পাখি","tr":"pakhi","mean":"bird","hl":"প"},{"t":"ফুল","tr":"phul","mean":"flower","hl":"ফ"},{"t":"বই","tr":"boi","mean":"book","hl":"ব"},{"t":"ভাত","tr":"bhat","mean":"cooked rice","hl":"ভ"},{"t":"মা","tr":"ma","mean":"mother","hl":"ম"},{"t":"যখন","tr":"jokhon","mean":"when","hl":"য"},{"t":"রুটি","tr":"ruti","mean":"flatbread","hl":"র"},{"t":"লাল","tr":"lal","mean":"red","hl":"ল"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Rice ({{ভাত}}) is at the heart of most meals in Bangladesh. An old saying calls Bangalis {{মাছে ভাতে বাঙালি}}: 'fish-and-rice Bengalis'."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the letters, then the words.","lines":["প ফ ব ভ ম","য র ল","পাখি ফুল বই ভাত","মা যখন রুটি লাল"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Listen. Which word is it?","say":"ভাত","options":["ভাত","বাত","হাত","ভাই"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which letter is ব with a dot below?","options":["ড়","র","য়","ঢ়"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{য}} usually sounds like…","options":["y","z","j","r"],"answer":2},{"q":"What does {{পাখি}} mean?","say":"পাখি","options":["flower","book","rice","bird"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which letter is made with the lips?","options":["ক","ম","ত","চ"],"answer":1},{"q":"How is {{র}} made?","options":["One quick tap of the tongue","Rolled for a long time","Silent, like the r in British 'car'","Like a w, with round lips"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u1-sh-and-dots","icon":"শ","title":"Consonants 4: শ ষ স হ and the Dotted Letters","subtitle":"Three 'sh' letters, হ, ড় ঢ় য়","minutes":12,"goals":["Read শ ষ স হ","Know that স is usually 'sh'","Read the dotted letters ড় ঢ় য়"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Almost there! This lesson covers three 'sh' letters, {{হ}}, and three letters that wear a dot."},{"type":"text","text":"{{শ}}, {{ষ}} and {{স}} are usually all said **'sh'**. {{স}} sounds like 's' mainly in clusters such as {{স্ত}}, as in {{রাস্তা}} (road).","title":"Three letters, one sound"},{"type":"letters","items":["sha","ssha","sa","ha"]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"শ","label":"talobbo sho","desc":"The usual 'sh'. Very common."},{"t":"ষ","label":"murdhonno sho","desc":"Also 'sh'. Mostly in formal or older words."},{"t":"স","label":"dontto sho","desc":"Usually 'sh', but 's' in some clusters."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Bangla speakers use these names when they spell aloud, so learn them: 'talobbo sho', 'murdhonno sho', 'dontto sho'."},{"type":"text","text":"{{ড়}}, {{ঢ়}} and {{য়}} are {{ড}}, {{ঢ}} and {{য}} with a dot below. They never start a word.","title":"Letters with a dot"},{"type":"letters","items":["ra-dot","rha-dot","ya-dot"]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ড","label":"do","desc":"Tongue curled back, like English d."},{"t":"ড়","label":"ro (flap)","desc":"Curl the tongue back and flick it forward."},{"t":"য","label":"jo","desc":"Sounds like j."},{"t":"য়","label":"y / o","desc":"A soft glide like y, or a vowel sound."}]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"শাপলা","tr":"shapla","mean":"water lily","hl":"শ"},{"t":"ষাঁড়","tr":"shar","mean":"bull","hl":"ষ"},{"t":"সাপ","tr":"shap","mean":"snake","hl":"স"},{"t":"হাতি","tr":"hati","mean":"elephant","hl":"হ"},{"t":"পাহাড়","tr":"pahar","mean":"hill","hl":"ড়"},{"t":"মেয়ে","tr":"meye","mean":"girl","hl":"য়"},{"t":"নয়","tr":"noy","mean":"nine","hl":"য়"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"The {{শাপলা}} (water lily) is the national flower of Bangladesh."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Watch the dots!","lines":["শ ষ স হ","ড ড়  ঢ ঢ়  য য়","শাপলা সাপ হাতি","পাহাড় মেয়ে নয়"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"How is {{স}} said in {{সাপ}} (snake)?","say":"সাপ","options":["s","z","sh","ch"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which letter has a dot?","options":["য","য়","ব","ঢ"],"answer":1},{"q":"Can {{ড়}} start a word?","options":["No","Yes, often","Only in names"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"হাতি","options":["water lily","elephant","snake","girl"],"answer":1},{"q":"What is the national flower of Bangladesh?","options":["গোলাপ","শিমুল","শাপলা","কদম"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{য়}} in {{মেয়ে}} (girl) sounds like…","options":["a soft y","a hard j","a rolled r","a strong h"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u1-vowel-signs","icon":"কা","title":"Vowel Signs (কার)","subtitle":"How vowels attach to consonants","minutes":16,"goals":["Recognise the 10 vowel signs","Know where each sign sits","Read consonant + vowel sign pairs"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Inside a word, vowels change shape. They become small **vowel signs** called {{কার}} (kar), attached to a consonant. Every vowel except {{অ}} has one."},{"type":"table","head":["Vowel","Sign","Name","Where it goes","Example"],"rows":[["{{আ}}","{{া}}","{{আ-কার}}","after","{{কা}} ka"],["{{ই}}","{{ি}}","{{ই-কার}}","before","{{কি}} ki"],["{{ঈ}}","{{ী}}","{{ঈ-কার}}","after","{{কী}} ki"],["{{উ}}","{{ু}}","{{উ-কার}}","below","{{কু}} ku"],["{{ঊ}}","{{ূ}}","{{ঊ-কার}}","below","{{কূ}} ku"],["{{ঋ}}","{{ৃ}}","{{ঋ-কার}}","below","{{কৃ}} kri"],["{{এ}}","{{ে}}","{{এ-কার}}","before","{{কে}} ke"],["{{ঐ}}","{{ৈ}}","{{ঐ-কার}}","before","{{কৈ}} koi"],["{{ও}}","{{ো}}","{{ও-কার}}","both sides","{{কো}} ko"],["{{ঔ}}","{{ৌ}}","{{ঔ-কার}}","both sides","{{কৌ}} kou"]]},{"type":"build","base":["ক","ম","ল"],"marks":["া","ি","ী","ু","ূ","ৃ","ে","ৈ","ো","ৌ"],"labels":["a","i","i","u","u","ri","e","oi","o","ou"],"title":"Build the syllables"},{"type":"rule","name":"ি, ে and ৈ go first","color":"red","desc":"These three signs are written **before** the consonant, but you say them **after** it.","how":"Read the consonant first, then the vowel: {{নি}} = n + i = 'ni'.","examples":[{"t":"পানি","tr":"pani","hl":"নি"},{"t":"মেঘ","tr":"megh","hl":"মে"},{"t":"বৈশাখ","tr":"boishakh","hl":"বৈ"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{ো}} hugs the consonant: {{ে}} on the left, {{া}} on the right. {{কো}} = 'ko'."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"দুধ","tr":"dudh","mean":"milk","hl":"দু"},{"t":"ভূত","tr":"bhut","mean":"ghost","hl":"ভূ"},{"t":"কৃষক","tr":"krishok","mean":"farmer","hl":"কৃ"},{"t":"দোকান","tr":"dokan","mean":"shop","hl":"দো"},{"t":"মৌমাছি","tr":"moumachhi","mean":"bee","hl":"মৌ"},{"t":"নদী","tr":"nodi","mean":"river","hl":"দী"},{"t":"বিড়াল","tr":"biral","mean":"cat","hl":"বি"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"A few pairs change shape: {{রু}} (ru), {{রূ}} (ru), {{শু}} (shu), {{হু}} (hu), {{গু}} (gu) and {{হৃ}} (hri). Look carefully when you meet them.","title":"Special shapes"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read each line aloud.","lines":["কা কি কী কু কূ কৃ কে কৈ কো কৌ","মা মি মু মে মো","পানি দুধ মেঘ","দোকান মৌমাছি বিড়াল"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Where is {{ি}} written?","options":["Before the consonant","After the consonant, on the right","Under the consonant","Above the headline"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen and choose.","say":"মে","options":["মে","মা","মি","মো"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you read {{কু}}?","say":"কু","options":["ki","ku","ko","ke"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which sign is {{আ-কার}}?","options":["ি","ু","ে","া"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{কো}} is {{ক}} plus…","options":["two া signs, one each side","ু below it and া after it","ি and ী","ে and া around it"],"answer":3},{"q":"What does {{দোকান}} mean?","say":"দোকান","options":["milk","bee","shop","ghost"],"answer":2},{"q":"In {{পানি}}, which vowel sound comes last?","options":["a","o","e","i"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u1-special-signs","icon":"ং","title":"Special Signs: ্ ং ঃ ঁ ৎ","subtitle":"Five small signs with big jobs","minutes":12,"goals":["Recognise হসন্ত, অনুস্বার, বিসর্গ, চন্দ্রবিন্দু and খণ্ড ত","Know what sound each one makes"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Five small signs do big jobs. They are easy to spot once you know them."},{"type":"letters","items":["hasanta","anusvar","bisarga","chandrabindu","khanda-ta"]},{"type":"table","head":["Sign","Name","What it does","Example"],"rows":[["{{্}}","{{হসন্ত}} hoshonto","Removes the hidden vowel","{{ক্}} k (no o)"],["{{ং}}","{{অনুস্বার}} onushshar","Adds 'ng'","{{রং}} rong"],["{{ঃ}}","{{বিসর্গ}} bisorgo","Doubles the next consonant, or adds a light h","{{দুঃখ}} dukkho"],["{{ঁ}}","{{চন্দ্রবিন্দু}} chondrobindu","Makes the vowel nasal","{{চাঁদ}} chand"],["{{ৎ}}","{{খণ্ড ত}} khondo to","A t with no vowel after it","{{হঠাৎ}} hothat"]]},{"type":"text","text":"The {{হসন্ত}} is a small slanted stroke under a letter. It says: 'no vowel here'. Usually the two letters **join** into a conjunct instead, so you rarely see the হসন্ত itself.","title":"হসন্ত and joining"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"ক্ + ত = ক্ত","tr":"k + to = kto"},{"t":"শক্ত","tr":"shokto","mean":"hard, strong","hl":"ক্ত"}]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ং","label":"ng (sign)","desc":"Adds 'ng' after a vowel: রং, বাংলা."},{"t":"ঙ","label":"ng (letter)","desc":"A full letter that can join others: ব্যাঙ, সঙ্গে."}],"title":"Same sound, two shapes"},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"কাদা","label":"kada","desc":"mud"},{"t":"কাঁদা","label":"kanda","desc":"to cry: the ঁ makes the 'a' nasal"}],"title":"One small sign, a new word"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{চন্দ্রবিন্দু}} means 'moon and dot'. Look: {{ঁ}} is a little moon with a dot!"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"বাংলা","tr":"bangla","mean":"Bangla","hl":"ং"},{"t":"সংখ্যা","tr":"shongkha","mean":"number","hl":"ং"},{"t":"দুঃখ","tr":"dukkho","mean":"sadness","hl":"ঃ"},{"t":"চাঁদ","tr":"chand","mean":"moon","hl":"ঁ"},{"t":"হঠাৎ","tr":"hothat","mean":"suddenly","hl":"ৎ"},{"t":"উৎসব","tr":"utshob","mean":"festival","hl":"ৎ"}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Find the special sign in each word, then read it.","lines":["রং বাংলা সংখ্যা","দুঃখ চাঁদ","হঠাৎ উৎসব","কাদা কাঁদা"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Which sign makes a vowel nasal?","options":["ং","ঃ","্","ঁ"],"answer":3},{"q":"What does {{ং}} add?","options":["h","t","ng","a nasal vowel"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. Which word is it?","say":"চাঁদ","options":["ছাদ","চাঁপা","চাঁদ","চাল"],"answer":2},{"q":"What does {{ৎ}} stand for?","options":["a long a sound","t with no vowel after it","the letter ত with a hidden o","a nasal sound"],"answer":1},{"q":"In {{দুঃখ}} (dukkho), what does {{ঃ}} do?","options":["Adds a strong 'h' sound","Doubles the k sound","Makes the u nasal","Ends the sentence"],"answer":1},{"q":"What does {{কাঁদা}} mean?","say":"কাঁদা","options":["mud","to cry","moon","to laugh"],"answer":1},{"q":"What is {{্}} called?","options":["হসন্ত","মাত্রা","কার","দাঁড়ি"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u1-conjuncts","icon":"ক্ষ","title":"Conjuncts (যুক্তবর্ণ)","subtitle":"When consonants join together","minutes":18,"goals":["Read common conjuncts","Recognise র-ফলা, য-ফলা and রেফ","Know that some conjuncts change their sound"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"When two consonants meet with **no vowel between them**, Bangla often joins them into one shape: a {{যুক্তবর্ণ}} (conjunct). Some are easy to see through; some are new shapes to learn."},{"type":"table","head":["Conjunct","Made of","Example","Meaning"],"rows":[["{{ক্ষ}}","{{ক}} + {{ষ}}","{{শিক্ষা}} shikkha","education"],["{{জ্ঞ}}","{{জ}} + {{ঞ}}","{{জ্ঞান}} gyan","knowledge"],["{{ঙ্গ}}","{{ঙ}} + {{গ}}","{{সঙ্গে}} shonge","with"],["{{ন্ত}}","{{ন}} + {{ত}}","{{শান্ত}} shanto","calm"],["{{স্ত}}","{{স}} + {{ত}}","{{রাস্তা}} rasta","road"],["{{ন্দ}}","{{ন}} + {{দ}}","{{সুন্দর}} shundor","beautiful"],["{{ক্ত}}","{{ক}} + {{ত}}","{{রক্ত}} rokto","blood"],["{{ষ্ট}}","{{ষ}} + {{ট}}","{{মিষ্টি}} mishti","sweet"],["{{ল্প}}","{{ল}} + {{প}}","{{গল্প}} golpo","story"],["{{চ্চ}}","{{চ}} + {{চ}}","{{বাচ্চা}} bachcha","child"]],"title":"Common conjuncts"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"{{ক্ষ}} is said 'kh' at the start of a word ({{ক্ষমা}}, khoma, forgiveness) and 'kkh' in the middle ({{শিক্ষা}}). {{জ্ঞ}} is said 'gy' at the start ({{জ্ঞান}}) and 'gg' in the middle ({{বিজ্ঞান}}, biggan, science)."},{"type":"text","text":"Three letters turn into small marks when they join others.","title":"Three special helpers"},{"type":"rule","name":"র-ফলা ( ্র )","color":"blue","desc":"An r **after** a consonant becomes a small slanted stroke at its foot.","how":"প্রথম = প + র + থ + ম: 'prothom' (first).","examples":[{"t":"প্রথম","tr":"prothom","hl":"প্র"},{"t":"গ্রাম","tr":"gram","hl":"গ্র"},{"t":"ট্রেন","tr":"tren","hl":"ট্রে"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"য-ফলা ( ্য )","color":"purple","desc":"A য **after** a consonant becomes a small zigzag on the right. After the first letter with া it makes the 'a' of 'bag'; in the middle of a word it doubles the consonant.","examples":[{"t":"ব্যাগ","tr":"bag","hl":"ব্যা"},{"t":"সত্য","tr":"shotto","hl":"ত্য"},{"t":"বিদ্যা","tr":"biddya","hl":"দ্যা"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"রেফ ( র্ )","color":"green","desc":"An r **before** a consonant becomes a small hook on top of the next letter, above the headline. Say the r first.","examples":[{"t":"সূর্য","tr":"shurjo","hl":"র্য"},{"t":"বর্ষা","tr":"borsha","hl":"র্ষ"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"The great river {{পদ্মা}} is said 'podda', not 'podma'. Some conjuncts change their sound, so listen to every new word."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"ক্ষমা","tr":"khoma","mean":"forgiveness","hl":"ক্ষ"},{"t":"বিজ্ঞান","tr":"biggan","mean":"science","hl":"জ্ঞ"},{"t":"বন্ধু","tr":"bondhu","mean":"friend","hl":"ন্ধ"},{"t":"ছাত্র","tr":"chhatro","mean":"student","hl":"ত্র"},{"t":"বিশ্ব","tr":"bishsho","mean":"world","hl":"শ্ব"}],"title":"More words"},{"type":"practice","text":"Find the conjunct, then read the word.","lines":["শিক্ষা জ্ঞান সঙ্গে","শান্ত রাস্তা সুন্দর","প্রথম গ্রাম ট্রেন","ব্যাগ সত্য সূর্য বর্ষা"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"What is a {{যুক্তবর্ণ}}?","options":["A vowel sign","A letter with a dot","Two consonants joined","A word with no vowels at all"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{ক্ষ}} is made of…","options":["ক + স","খ + ষ","ক + শ","ক + ষ"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Which word is it?","say":"প্রথম","options":["পরথম","প্রথা","প্রথম","পথম"],"answer":2},{"q":"Where does রেফ ( র্ ) appear?","options":["At the bottom, as a slanted stroke","On the right, as a zigzag","Before the word","On top, above the headline"],"answer":3},{"q":"How is {{পদ্মা}} said?","say":"পদ্মা","options":["podma","padma","podda","pomda"],"answer":2},{"q":"What does {{বন্ধু}} mean?","say":"বন্ধু","options":["friend","student","road","story"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which word has a য-ফলা?","options":["ব্যাগ","গ্রাম","শিক্ষা","গল্প"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u1-numerals","icon":"১","title":"Bangla Numerals","subtitle":"০ ১ ২ ৩ ৪ ৫ ৬ ৭ ৮ ৯","minutes":10,"goals":["Read the digits ০ to ৯","Say the numbers 0 to 10","Read prices and dates"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangladesh uses its own digits on signs, prices, calendars and buses. They work exactly like 0–9: same place values, new shapes."},{"type":"letters","items":["num-0","num-1","num-2","num-3","num-4","num-5","num-6","num-7","num-8","num-9"]},{"type":"table","head":["Digit","Word","Say","Value"],"rows":[["{{০}}","{{শূন্য}}","shunno","0"],["{{১}}","{{এক}}","ek","1"],["{{২}}","{{দুই}}","dui","2"],["{{৩}}","{{তিন}}","tin","3"],["{{৪}}","{{চার}}","char","4"],["{{৫}}","{{পাঁচ}}","panch","5"],["{{৬}}","{{ছয়}}","chhoy","6"],["{{৭}}","{{সাত}}","shat","7"],["{{৮}}","{{আট}}","at","8"],["{{৯}}","{{নয়}}","noy","9"],["{{১০}}","{{দশ}}","dosh","10"]]},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"৪","label":"4, not 8!","desc":"Looks like an English 8 but means four."},{"t":"৮","label":"8","desc":"This is the Bangla eight."}],"title":"Don't be fooled"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"৫০ টাকা","tr":"ponchash taka","mean":"50 taka"},{"t":"১৯৭১","tr":"unish sho ekattor","mean":"1971, the year of Bangladesh's independence"},{"t":"২১ ফেব্রুয়ারি","tr":"ekushe februari","mean":"21 February","note":"Read aloud as একুশে ফেব্রুয়ারি."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"21 February ({{একুশে ফেব্রুয়ারি}}) honours the people who gave their lives for the Bangla language in 1952. UNESCO made it International Mother Language Day."},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"From 11 to 99, Bangla has a separate word for every number (21 is {{একুশ}}). Learn 1–10 first; the rest come step by step."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the digits and numbers aloud.","lines":["০ ১ ২ ৩ ৪","৫ ৬ ৭ ৮ ৯","১০ ২০ ৫০ ১০০"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"What is {{৪}}?","options":["8","7","9","4"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Which digit is it?","say":"সাত","options":["৯","৭","১","৬"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say {{৫}}?","options":["চার","ছয়","পাঁচ","পঞ্চাশ"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which is 10?","options":["১","১০","০১","১০০"],"answer":1},{"q":"Read: {{৩}} + {{২}} = ?","options":["৬","৪","৮","৫"],"answer":3},{"q":"What price is {{৮০ টাকা}}?","options":["40 taka","8 taka","800 taka","80 taka"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u1-reading-lab","icon":"পড়","title":"Reading Lab","subtitle":"Put it all together: words and short sentences","minutes":15,"goals":["Read new words step by step","Read two short sentences","Meet some famous Bangladeshi words"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Time to put it all together! Read slowly: consonant, vowel sign, next consonant. Tap any word to check yourself."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Find the consonants","desc":"Spot each consonant or conjunct from left to right."},{"title":"Add the vowel signs","desc":"Remember: ি, ে and ৈ sit in front but are said after."},{"title":"Check the small signs","desc":"Look for ং, ঃ, ঁ, ৎ and dots."},{"title":"Say it smoothly","t":"বিড়াল","tr":"biral","mean":"cat","desc":"Blend the syllables into one word."}],"title":"How to read a new word"},{"type":"practice","text":"Word ladders: each line grows one step.","lines":["ক কা কাক","ম মা মাছ","ব বা বাঘ","প পা পাখি"]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"বাংলাদেশ","tr":"bangladesh","mean":"Bangladesh"},{"t":"ঢাকা","tr":"dhaka","mean":"Dhaka"},{"t":"পদ্মা","tr":"podda","mean":"the Padma river"},{"t":"ইলিশ","tr":"ilish","mean":"hilsa fish"},{"t":"রিকশা","tr":"riksha","mean":"rickshaw"},{"t":"বৈশাখ","tr":"boishakh","mean":"Boishakh, the first month of the Bangla year"}],"title":"Famous words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"The {{ইলিশ}} (hilsa) is the national fish of Bangladesh, and the Royal Bengal tiger ({{বাঘ}}) is the national animal."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি বাংলা শিখি।","tr":"ami bangla shikhi","mean":"I learn Bangla.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"বাংলা","mean":"Bangla"},{"t":"শিখি","mean":"learn"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"এটা আমার বই।","tr":"eta amar boi","mean":"This is my book.","words":[{"t":"এটা","mean":"this"},{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"বই","mean":"book"}],"note":"Bangla needs no word for 'is' in a sentence like this one."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read these short sentences.","lines":["আমি বাংলা শিখি।","এটা আমার বই।","পাখি গান গায়।","মা ভাত রান্না করে।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Listen. Which word is it?","say":"বাঘ","options":["বাঘ","বাগ","ভাগ","বাঁশ"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you read {{মাছ}}?","say":"মাছ","options":["machh","moch","michh","mach-o"],"answer":0},{"q":"What does {{আমি}} mean?","say":"আমি","options":["you","we","I","my"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which word means 'cat'?","options":["মৌমাছি","কাক","বিড়াল","পাখি"],"answer":2},{"q":"In {{পদ্মা}}, how is {{দ্ম}} said?","options":["dm","md","dd","m"],"answer":2},{"q":"How do you read {{রিকশা}}?","say":"রিকশা","options":["rikosha","rekasha","roksha","riksha"],"answer":3},{"q":"What is the national fish of Bangladesh?","options":["রুই","চিংড়ি","কই","ইলিশ"],"answer":3}]}]}]});
LC.units.push({"id":"writing","order":2,"icon":"ক","color":"cyan","title":"Writing Bangla","subtitle":"Pen grip, letters, vowel signs, conjuncts and numerals by hand","lessons":[{"id":"u2-pen-and-matra","icon":"মা","title":"Pen Grip & the Headline","subtitle":"Good habits before the first letter","minutes":10,"goals":["Hold the pen comfortably","Know where letters sit","Know which letters have a full, half or no headline"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing Bangla by hand helps you read faster and remember letters. Start relaxed: good habits now save time later."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Hold the pen lightly","desc":"Grip it a little above the tip, between thumb and first finger, resting on the middle finger."},{"title":"Use lined paper","desc":"Use one line as the headline. Letter bodies hang just below it."},{"title":"Relax your wrist","desc":"Tilt the paper slightly and let your hand glide."},{"title":"Go slowly","desc":"Neat and slow beats fast and messy."}],"title":"Getting ready"},{"type":"text","text":"Most of a letter **hangs below the headline**. A few parts rise above it (like the curl on {{ই}}), and some signs, like {{ু}}, sit below the letter.","title":"Where letters sit"},{"type":"rule","name":"Body first, headline last","color":"blue","desc":"Many writers draw the body of each letter first, then pull the {{মাত্রা}} across the top from left to right. In a word, one long headline covers all the letters.","how":"Some people draw the headline first. Either way works; just stay consistent.","examples":[{"t":"কলম","tr":"kolom"},{"t":"বাবা","tr":"baba"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Headline","Letters"],"rows":[["Full (32)","{{অ আ ই ঈ উ ঊ ক ঘ চ ছ জ ঝ ট ঠ ড ঢ ত দ ন ফ ব ভ ম য র ল ষ স হ ড় ঢ় য়}}"],["Half (8)","{{ঋ খ গ ণ থ ধ প শ}}"],["None (10)","{{এ ঐ ও ঔ ঙ ঞ ৎ ং ঃ ঁ}}"]],"title":"Which letters have a headline?"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"10 letters have no headline, 8 have half a headline, and the other 32 have a full one."},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["অ","আ","ব","র"],"note":"Trace slowly. Draw the headline last.","title":"Warm-up"},{"type":"selfcheck","items":["My pen grip is relaxed","My headlines are straight and level","My letters hang from the headline instead of floating below it"]},{"type":"practice","text":"Say each word, then trace it in the air with your finger, headline last.","lines":["কলম","বাবা","মামা"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Where does most of a Bangla letter sit?","options":["Above the headline","On top of the matra, like a hat","Across two lines","Below the headline"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which letter has **no** headline?","options":["ক","অ","ব","এ"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which letter has a half headline?","options":["ক","ম","ল","প"],"answer":3},{"q":"When do many writers draw the headline of a word?","options":["Before anything else","After the letters","Never","Only for words of five letters or more"],"answer":1},{"q":"How should you hold the pen?","options":["Tightly, at the very tip","Lightly, a little above the tip","In a fist, like a spoon","Lightly, but at the very top end of the pen"],"answer":1},{"q":"How many letters have a full headline?","options":["10","8","50","32"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u2-writing-vowels","icon":"অ","title":"Writing the Vowels","subtitle":"অ to ঔ, step by step","minutes":20,"goals":["Write all 11 vowel letters","Know where each vowel starts","Know which vowels have no headline"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Let's write the 11 vowels. Watch the pen demo first, then trace, then write on your own."},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"General rules: start at the top left, move down and to the right, and draw straight posts from top to bottom. Draw the headline last, from left to right.","title":"Before you start"},{"type":"howto","char":"অ","name":"shoro o","steps":["Start just under the headline on the left. Draw a small curve out to the right and back, like the top of a 3.","Keep going into a bigger lower curve, then join it to the right with a short line.","Draw a straight post on the right, from the headline down.","Draw the headline across the top, left to right."],"tip":"The left part looks like a 3; the right part is a straight post."},{"type":"howto","char":"আ","name":"shoro a","steps":["Write অ exactly as before.","Add one more straight post on the right, from the headline down: this is the আ-kar.","Stretch the headline over both posts."],"tip":"আ = অ + া"},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["অ","আ"]},{"type":"howto","char":"ই","name":"hrosho i","steps":["Start just under the headline and draw the body: a curve out to the right and down, like a soft 2.","Finish the bottom with a small loop and a short tail.","Draw the headline.","Add the little curl that stands above the headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"ঈ","name":"dirgho i","steps":["Start under the headline, as for ই.","Draw the curved body; it has one extra loop that ই does not have.","Draw the headline.","Add the curl above the headline."],"tip":"Write ই and ঈ side by side and compare them with the demo."},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["ই","ঈ"]},{"type":"howto","char":"উ","name":"hrosho u","steps":["Start just under the headline.","Draw the main curve down and round, like a hook.","Finish with a tail curling out to the right.","Draw the headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"ঊ","name":"dirgho u","steps":["Write উ.","Add an extra small curl on its tail.","Draw the headline."],"tip":"ঊ is উ with one more curl."},{"type":"howto","char":"ঋ","name":"ri","steps":["Start at the top left and draw the curvy body down.","Add the small hook on the right side.","Draw a short headline: ঋ has only half a headline."]},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["উ","ঊ","ঋ"]},{"type":"howto","char":"এ","name":"e","steps":["Start at the top with a short slanted stroke.","Bring the line down in one smooth curve.","Stop. এ has **no** headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"ঐ","name":"oi","steps":["Write এ.","Add the extra curl on top.","No headline."],"tip":"ঐ is এ wearing a little hat."},{"type":"howto","char":"ও","name":"o","steps":["Start with the small hook at the top.","Below it, draw a curve like the number 3.","No headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"ঔ","name":"ou","steps":["Write ও.","Add the extra curl at the top right.","No headline."],"tip":"ঔ is ও with one more curl."},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["এ","ঐ","ও","ঔ"]},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["আম","উট","এক","ওজন"],"note":"Now write whole words that start with a vowel.","title":"Vowels in words"},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Which vowel letters have no headline?","options":["অ আ ই ঈ","এ ঐ ও ঔ","উ ঊ ঋ","ই ঈ উ ঊ"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you make {{আ}} from {{অ}}?","options":["Add a straight post","Add a dot below it","Add a curl on top","Remove the headline"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which letter has a curl above the headline?","options":["অ","উ","আ","ই"],"answer":3},{"q":"When do you draw the headline on {{অ}}?","options":["First of all","Before the post","At the end","Never"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{ঊ}} looks like {{উ}} plus…","options":["a dot below","an extra curl","a straight post","a headline"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which vowel has a half headline?","options":["ঋ","এ","অ","উ"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u2-consonant-families","icon":"ব","title":"Consonants by Shape Families","subtitle":"Learn one shape, write several letters","minutes":20,"goals":["Group consonants by shared shapes","Write the dot letters correctly","Write ক, ব, র, ষ and প"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Many consonants share parts. Learn a family and you learn several letters at once."},{"type":"table","head":["Family","Letters","What they share"],"rows":[["Dot letters","{{ব র}} · {{ড ড়}} · {{ঢ ঢ়}} · {{য য়}}","The second letter is the first plus a dot below"],["Triangle","{{ব র ষ}}","A triangle hanging from the headline"],["Post on the right","{{খ গ ঘ ধ ন প ব ম য ষ}}","A straight post down the right side"],["Look-alikes","{{প ফ}}","{{ফ}} is {{প}} with an extra curl"],["No headline","{{ঙ ঞ}}","Leave the headline off"]]},{"type":"howto","char":"ব","name":"bo","steps":["Draw the straight post on the right, from the headline down.","From the top of the post, slide a slanting line down to the left.","Curve along the bottom back to the right to meet the foot of the post. You now have a triangle.","Draw the headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"র","name":"ro","steps":["Write ব.","Put a dot just below the middle of it."],"tip":"No dot, no র!"},{"type":"howto","char":"ষ","name":"murdhonno sho","steps":["Write the triangle body, as for ব.","Add a short slanting stroke across the inside.","Draw the headline."]},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["ব","র","ষ"]},{"type":"howto","char":"ক","name":"ko","steps":["Draw the straight post down from the headline.","Starting on the left, make a small loop that crosses the post.","Finish with the tail curving out on the right.","Draw the headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"প","name":"po","steps":["Start at the top left with a small inward hook.","Bring the line down and curve it right along the bottom.","Draw the post on the right to meet it.","Add a short headline over the post: প has only half a headline."]},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["ক","খ","গ","ঘ","প","ফ"]},{"type":"text","text":"Write the base letter fully, then add the dot **last**.","title":"The dot family"},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"ড / ড়","label":"do / ro","desc":"Same shape; ড় has a dot."},{"t":"ঢ / ঢ়","label":"dho / rho","desc":"Same shape; ঢ় has a dot."},{"t":"য / য়","label":"jo / y","desc":"Same shape; য় has a dot."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"A missing dot changes the letter. {{বড়}} (big) must have its dot, or it is misspelled."},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["ড","ড়","ঢ","ঢ়","য","য়"]},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["বড়","পাহাড়","মেয়ে","রুটি","কলা"],"note":"Check every dot when you finish.","title":"Words with family letters"},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"How do you turn {{ব}} into {{র}}?","options":["Add a dot below","Add a line above it","Add a curl on the right side","Remove the headline"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which letter is {{ড}} with a dot?","options":["ঢ","দ","ট","ড়"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which letter has a straight post on the right?","options":["এ","ঙ","ও","ন"],"answer":3},{"q":"What does {{ফ}} add to {{প}}?","options":["A dot below","An extra curl","A second headline above","A long tail on the left side"],"answer":1},{"q":"When do you add the dot?","options":["Last","First","Before the headline","Never"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which letter has no headline?","options":["ঙ","ক","প","গ"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u2-placing-vowel-signs","icon":"কি","title":"Placing Vowel Signs","subtitle":"Before, after, below and both sides","minutes":16,"goals":["Put each vowel sign in the right place","Write ি before its consonant","Write words with vowel signs"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Now attach the vowel signs. Each sign has a fixed place: before, after, below, or on both sides of the consonant."},{"type":"table","head":["Position","Signs","Example"],"rows":[["Before","{{ি ে ৈ}}","{{কি কে কৈ}}"],["After","{{া ী}}","{{কা কী}}"],["Below","{{ু ূ ৃ}}","{{কু কূ কৃ}}"],["Both sides","{{ো ৌ}}","{{কো কৌ}}"]]},{"type":"howto","char":"কি","name":"ki","steps":["Draw the ই-kar first: a straight post with a curved top.","Let the curve bend over to the right, above the headline.","Write ক tucked under the curve.","Join the headline across both."],"tip":"Written first, said second: k + i."},{"type":"howto","char":"কী","name":"ki","steps":["Write ক first.","Draw the ঈ-kar post on its right.","Let its curved top bend back over ক to the left.","Join the headline across both."]},{"type":"howto","char":"কো","name":"ko","steps":["Write the এ-kar ে before the consonant.","Write ক.","Add the আ-kar া after it.","Join the headline over ক and া."],"tip":"ো is ে + া wrapped around the consonant."},{"type":"howto","char":"কু","name":"ku","steps":["Write ক.","Hang the উ-kar from the bottom: a small hook."]},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Some pairs have joined shapes: {{রু}}, {{রূ}}, {{শু}}, {{হু}}, {{গু}} and {{হৃ}}. Copy them from the demo.","title":"Special shapes"},{"type":"build","base":["ব","দ","স"],"marks":["া","ি","ী","ু","ূ","ৃ","ে","ৈ","ো","ৌ"],"labels":["a","i","i","u","u","ri","e","oi","o","ou"],"title":"Practise every sign"},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["কা","কি","কী","কু","কূ","কৃ","কে","কৈ","কো","কৌ"]},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["পানি","দুধ","মেঘ","দোকান","নদী","কৃষক"],"note":"Say each word as you write it."},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Which sign goes on both sides?","options":["ো","ি","ু","ী"],"answer":0},{"q":"Where does {{ী}} go?","options":["After the consonant","Before the consonant","Under the consonant","Above the headline only"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which signs go below?","options":["ি ে ৈ","ু ূ ৃ","া ী","ো ৌ"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{মৌ}} has which sign?","say":"মৌ","options":["ো","ৌ","ৈ","ে"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which of these has a special joined shape?","options":["রু","কু","মু","দু"],"answer":0},{"q":"In {{কি}}, which sound do you say first?","options":["i","k","both at once"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u2-writing-conjuncts","icon":"ক্ষ","title":"Writing Conjuncts","subtitle":"Joined letters, ফলা and রেফ","minutes":18,"goals":["Write common conjuncts","Add র-ফলা, য-ফলা and রেফ","Write words with conjuncts"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Conjuncts look hard, but most follow a simple idea: two letters squeezed into one space."},{"type":"text","text":"Some conjuncts keep both letters easy to see, like {{ল্প}} in {{গল্প}}. Others are new shapes you simply learn, like {{ক্ষ}} and {{জ্ঞ}}. Watch the demo for each one.","title":"Two kinds"},{"type":"howto","char":"প্র","name":"র-ফলা","steps":["Write the consonant (here প).","Add a short slanting stroke at its foot: this is র-ফলা."],"tip":"Read it p + r: প্রথম = 'prothom'."},{"type":"howto","char":"ব্য","name":"য-ফলা","steps":["Write the consonant (here ব).","Add the য-ফলা on its right: a small zigzag joined to the headline."]},{"type":"howto","char":"র্য","name":"রেফ","steps":["Write the second letter (here য) with its headline.","Add a small curved hook standing on the headline above it: this is রেফ.","Remember to read the r **first**: সূর্য = 'shurjo'."]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Typing is different from handwriting: on a keyboard you type {{ক}} + {{্}} + {{ষ}} and the computer builds {{ক্ষ}} for you."},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["ক্ষ","জ্ঞ","ঙ্গ","ন্ত","স্ত","ন্দ"]},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["শিক্ষা","জ্ঞান","সঙ্গে","শান্ত","রাস্তা","সুন্দর","প্রথম","ব্যাগ","সূর্য"],"note":"Copy each word twice."},{"type":"selfcheck","items":["রেফ sits above the headline","র-ফলা is at the foot of the letter","য-ফলা is on the right","The headline joins the whole word"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"In {{সূর্য}}, where is the r written?","options":["As a dot under the letter","As a slanted stroke at the foot of a letter","As a hook above the headline","As a separate letter র at the end"],"answer":2},{"q":"What is the slanted stroke at the foot of {{প্র}}?","options":["য-ফলা","রেফ","হসন্ত","র-ফলা"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which word has a রেফ?","options":["প্রথম","সূর্য","ব্যাগ","গ্রাম"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which conjunct is ক + ষ?","options":["ক্ত","ক্ষ","ষ্ট","জ্ঞ"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you type {{ক্ষ}} on a keyboard?","options":["ক + ষ + া","ষ + ক","ক + ্ + ষ","ক + ং + ষ"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which word means 'road'?","options":["শান্ত","সুন্দর","সঙ্গে","রাস্তা"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u2-writing-numerals","icon":"৫","title":"Writing Numerals","subtitle":"Digits for prices, buses and dates","minutes":12,"goals":["Write the digits ০ to ৯","Write numbers with several digits","Write the words for 1 to 5"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangla digits are quick to write, and you will see them everywhere: on prices, buses and dates."},{"type":"howto","char":"০","name":"shunno","steps":["Start at the top.","Draw a small oval round to the left and back up to close it.","Keep it small: smaller than an English 0."]},{"type":"howto","char":"৪","name":"char","steps":["Start at the top.","Draw the small top loop.","Sweep down into the bigger bottom loop and close it."],"tip":"It looks like an English 8, but it means 4!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Use the tracing pads and the pen demo for every digit. Write each one five times."},{"type":"write","level":"letter","items":["০","১","২","৩","৪","৫","৬","৭","৮","৯"]},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["১০","২৫","৫০","১০০","১৯৭১"],"note":"Numbers with several digits work just like English."},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["এক","দুই","তিন","চার","পাঁচ"],"note":"Now the number words.","title":"Number words"},{"type":"dictation","items":[{"t":"৩","tr":"tin","mean":"three"},{"t":"৮","tr":"at","mean":"eight"},{"t":"১২","tr":"baro","mean":"twelve"},{"t":"৫০","tr":"ponchash","mean":"fifty"}],"title":"Listen and write the digits"},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"Which Bangla digit looks like an English 8?","options":["৪","৮","৬","৩"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. Which digit is it?","say":"নয়","options":["৯","৬","৭","২"],"answer":0},{"q":"Write 25 in Bangla digits.","options":["৫২","২৪","২০","২৫"],"answer":3},{"q":"What number is {{১০০}}?","options":["10","1000","100","110"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which is the word for 3?","options":["চার","দুই","দশ","তিন"],"answer":3},{"q":"What is {{১৯৭১}}?","options":["1971","1791","1917","1871"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u2-copywork-dictation","icon":"✍","title":"Copywork & Dictation","subtitle":"Copy, listen, write and check","minutes":18,"goals":["Copy words and sentences neatly","Write words you hear","Check your own writing"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Final practice! Copy, listen, write, then check your own work like a teacher."},{"type":"write","level":"word","items":["আম","বই","মা","বাবা","ফুল","পাখি","নদী","আকাশ"],"note":"Copy each word three times. Headline last.","title":"Copy words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Leave a small gap between words, and break the headline at each gap."},{"type":"write","level":"line","items":["আমি বাংলা শিখি।","এটা আমার বই।","পাখি গান গায়।","মা ভাত রান্না করে।"],"note":"End each sentence with a দাঁড়ি (।).","title":"Copy sentences"},{"type":"dictation","items":[{"t":"কলম","tr":"kolom","mean":"pen"},{"t":"মাছ","tr":"machh","mean":"fish"},{"t":"চাঁদ","tr":"chand","mean":"moon"},{"t":"সুন্দর","tr":"shundor","mean":"beautiful"},{"t":"বাংলাদেশ","tr":"bangladesh","mean":"Bangladesh"},{"t":"আমি বাংলা শিখি।","tr":"ami bangla shikhi","mean":"I learn Bangla."}],"title":"Dictation"},{"type":"selfcheck","items":["Every letter hangs from a straight headline","The headline breaks between words","ি, ে and ৈ come before their consonant","The dots under র, ড়, ঢ় and য় are in place","ঁ and ং are not mixed up","Each sentence ends with ।"]},{"type":"practice","text":"Read your own writing aloud. If you can read it easily, so can others.","lines":["আমি বাংলা শিখি।","এটা আমার বই।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick check","items":[{"q":"What ends a sentence in Bangla?","options":[".","ঃ","।","্"],"answer":2},{"q":"Between words, the headline should…","options":["continue without a break","get thicker","break","be drawn twice, once above and once below"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which spelling is correct for 'moon'?","say":"চাঁদ","options":["চাদ","চাঁদ","চাংদ","চাঃদ"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which word means 'fish'?","options":["মা","মাঠ","মাছ","মামা"],"answer":2},{"q":"What should you do after writing?","options":["Read it back aloud","Erase the headlines","Add capital letters at the start","Nothing at all"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which is spelled correctly for 'I learn Bangla'?","options":["আমি বাংলা শিখি।","আমি বাংলা শিকি।","আমী বাংলা শিখি।","আমি বাংলা শিখী।"],"answer":0}]}]}]});
LC.units.push({"id":"words","order":3,"icon":"শব্দ","color":"emerald","title":"First Words & Phrases","subtitle":"Greetings, numbers, money, family, food and getting around","lessons":[{"id":"u3-greetings","icon":"সালাম","title":"Hello, How Are You?","subtitle":"Greetings, replies and goodbyes","minutes":12,"goals":["Greet people respectfully in Bangla","Ask and answer “How are you?”","Say thank you, sorry and goodbye"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Your very first Bangla words! In Bangladesh, the greeting you choose can show a little about you and the person you meet. Don't worry: people are delighted whenever a learner tries."},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম","label":"Muslim greeting","desc":"Means “peace be upon you”. Most people in Bangladesh are Muslim, so you will hear this greeting everywhere. The reply is {{ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম}}."},{"t":"নমস্কার","label":"Hindu greeting","desc":"Often said with palms pressed together. Used by Hindu Bangladeshis and very widely in West Bengal (India). The reply is the same word."},{"t":"আদাব","label":"Polite, neutral","desc":"An older respectful greeting, sometimes used between people of different faiths. You will hear it less often today."}],"title":"Three ways to say hello"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম","tr":"assalamu alaikum","mean":"hello (peace be upon you)","example":{"t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম, চাচা।","tr":"assalamu alaikum, chacha","mean":"Hello, uncle."}},{"t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম","tr":"walaikum assalam","mean":"reply: and peace be upon you"},{"t":"নমস্কার","tr":"nomoshkar","mean":"hello (Hindu greeting)","example":{"t":"নমস্কার, দিদি।","tr":"nomoshkar, didi","mean":"Hello, sister."}}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Not sure which one to use? Simply greet back with the same words the other person used. With Muslim friends, {{আসসালামু আলাইকুম}} is natural; with Hindu friends and neighbours, {{নমস্কার}} is warm and respectful. A smile and {{কেমন আছেন?}} works with everyone."},{"type":"text","text":"Bangla has different words for “you”, depending on respect (more in Unit 4). For now: use {{কেমন আছেন?}} with adults and strangers, and {{কেমন আছ?}} with friends and children.","title":"How are you?"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"কেমন আছেন?","tr":"kemon achhen?","mean":"How are you? (polite)","note":"for elders, strangers, teachers","hl":"আছেন"},{"t":"কেমন আছ?","tr":"kemon achho?","mean":"How are you? (friendly)","note":"for friends, younger people","hl":"আছ"},{"t":"ভালো আছি।","tr":"bhalo achhi","mean":"I'm fine."},{"t":"আলহামদুলিল্লাহ, ভালো আছি।","tr":"alhamdulillah, bhalo achhi","mean":"Thank God, I'm fine.","note":"very common in Bangladesh"},{"t":"মোটামুটি।","tr":"motamuti","mean":"So-so."},{"t":"আপনি কেমন আছেন?","tr":"apni kemon achhen?","mean":"And how are you?"}]},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Rafi","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম, খালা।","tr":"assalamu alaikum, khala","mean":"Hello, auntie."},{"who":"Khala","t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম। কেমন আছ, বাবা?","tr":"walaikum assalam. kemon achho, baba?","mean":"Hello. How are you, dear?"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"ভালো আছি। আপনি কেমন আছেন?","tr":"bhalo achhi. apni kemon achhen?","mean":"I'm fine. How are you?"},{"who":"Khala","t":"আলহামদুলিল্লাহ, ভালো।","tr":"alhamdulillah, bhalo","mean":"Thank God, fine."}],"title":"Meeting an aunt"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"Elders often call a young boy {{বাবা}} (“dad”) and a young girl {{মা}} (“mum”) as a sweet word of affection. It isn't a mistake. It's love!"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"ধন্যবাদ","tr":"dhonnobad","mean":"thank you"},{"t":"জি","tr":"ji","mean":"yes (respectful)"},{"t":"হ্যাঁ","tr":"hya","mean":"yes"},{"t":"না","tr":"na","mean":"no"},{"t":"ঠিক আছে","tr":"thik achhe","mean":"OK, all right"},{"t":"দুঃখিত","tr":"dukkhito","mean":"sorry"},{"t":"মাফ করবেন","tr":"maf korben","mean":"excuse me / please forgive me"}],"title":"Little polite words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"{{জি}} is the respectful “yes” in Bangladesh. Answering an elder or a teacher with {{জি}} sounds very polite. You can also say {{জি না}} for a polite “no”."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আল্লাহ হাফেজ।","tr":"allah hafez","mean":"Goodbye (God protect you).","note":"common among Muslims in Bangladesh"},{"t":"আসি তাহলে।","tr":"ashi tahole","mean":"I'll be off then.","note":"literally “I come then”"},{"t":"আবার দেখা হবে।","tr":"abar dekha hobe","mean":"See you again."},{"t":"ভালো থাকবেন।","tr":"bhalo thakben","mean":"Take care. (polite)"},{"t":"ভালো থেকো।","tr":"bhalo theko","mean":"Take care. (friendly)"}],"title":"Saying goodbye"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"When leaving, people often say {{আসি}}, literally “I come”. It means “I'm going now, and I'll come again.” A friendly way to leave the door open!"},{"type":"practice","text":"Say each line aloud. Tap any word to hear it.","lines":["আসসালামু আলাইকুম।","নমস্কার।","কেমন আছেন?","ভালো আছি, ধন্যবাদ।","আপনি কেমন আছেন?","আবার দেখা হবে। ভালো থাকবেন।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"What is the usual reply to {{আসসালামু আলাইকুম}}?","options":["নমস্কার","আলহামদুলিল্লাহ, ভালো আছি","ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম","আবার দেখা হবে"],"answer":2,"explain":"The reply turns the words around: “and upon you, peace”."},{"q":"Listen. What is the person asking?","say":"কেমন আছেন?","options":["How are you? (polite)","What is your name?","Where are you going now?","Are you hungry?"],"answer":0,"explain":"{{কেমন আছেন?}} is the polite “How are you?”."},{"q":"Which greeting is used by Hindu Bangladeshis, often with palms together?","options":["আল্লাহ হাফেজ","নমস্কার","আসসালামু আলাইকুম","ধন্যবাদ"],"answer":1},{"q":"You meet your friend's grandmother. How do you ask how she is?","options":["কেমন আছ?","ভালো থেকো।","ঠিক আছে?","কেমন আছেন?"],"answer":3,"explain":"With elders, use the polite form ending in {{-েন}}."},{"q":"What does {{ভালো থাকবেন}} mean?","options":["Good morning","Thank you very much","I'm fine, thanks","Take care"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"দুঃখিত","options":["Thank you","Sorry","Hello","Yes, please"],"answer":1},{"q":"In Bangladesh, {{জি}} usually means…","options":["no, thank you (polite)","goodbye","yes (respectful)","maybe later"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u3-introductions","icon":"নাম","title":"Introducing Yourself","subtitle":"Name, home, age and “I speak a little Bangla”","minutes":12,"goals":["Say your name and ask someone's name","Say where you are from and where you live","Ask people to repeat or speak slowly"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let's introduce ourselves. Good news: Bangla has no word for “am / is / are” in sentences like “I am Sara”. You just say “I Sara”!"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার নাম সারা।","tr":"amar nam sara","mean":"My name is Sara.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"নাম","mean":"name"},{"t":"সারা","mean":"Sara"}],"note":"No “is” needed: “my name Sara”."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আপনার নাম কী?","tr":"apnar nam ki?","mean":"What is your name? (polite)","hl":"আপনার"},{"t":"তোমার নাম কী?","tr":"tomar nam ki?","mean":"What is your name? (friendly)","hl":"তোমার"},{"t":"আমার নাম রাফি।","tr":"amar nam rafi","mean":"My name is Rafi."},{"t":"আমি সারা।","tr":"ami sara","mean":"I'm Sara."}],"title":"Names"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{কী}} = “what”. Think of the English word “key”: it's the key question word!"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আমি লন্ডন থেকে এসেছি।","tr":"ami london theke eshechhi","mean":"I've come from London.","hl":"থেকে"},{"t":"আমি বাংলাদেশি।","tr":"ami bangladeshi","mean":"I'm Bangladeshi."},{"t":"আমি ব্রিটিশ বাংলাদেশি।","tr":"ami british bangladeshi","mean":"I'm British Bangladeshi."},{"t":"আমি নিউ ইয়র্কে থাকি।","tr":"ami niu iyorke thaki","mean":"I live in New York.","note":"{{-এ}} = in","hl":"থাকি"},{"t":"আমার বাড়ি সিলেটে।","tr":"amar bari shilete","mean":"My family home is in Sylhet."}],"title":"Where are you from?"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{আপনার বাড়ি কোথায়?}} (“Where is your home?”) usually means “Which district is your family from?”, not your street address. Bangladeshis love to find a home town in common!"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আমি ছাত্র।","tr":"ami chhatro","mean":"I'm a student. (male)"},{"t":"আমি ছাত্রী।","tr":"ami chhatri","mean":"I'm a student. (female)"},{"t":"আমার বয়স বারো বছর।","tr":"amar boyosh baro bochhor","mean":"I'm twelve years old.","note":"literally “my age twelve years”"},{"t":"আমি একটু একটু বাংলা বলতে পারি।","tr":"ami ektu ektu bangla bolte pari","mean":"I can speak a little Bangla."}],"title":"More about you"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"A few job and role words change for girls and women: {{ছাত্র}} / {{ছাত্রী}} (student). Most words, and all verbs, stay the same for everyone."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আবার বলবেন?","tr":"abar bolben?","mean":"Could you say that again?"},{"t":"একটু আস্তে বলবেন?","tr":"ektu aste bolben?","mean":"Could you speak a little slowly?"},{"t":"আমি বুঝতে পারিনি।","tr":"ami bujhte parini","mean":"I didn't understand."},{"t":"এটা বাংলায় কী বলে?","tr":"eta banglay ki bole?","mean":"What is this called in Bangla?"}],"title":"Life-saving phrases"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Nadia","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম। আমার নাম নাদিয়া। আপনার নাম কী?","tr":"assalamu alaikum. amar nam nadia. apnar nam ki?","mean":"Hello. My name is Nadia. What's your name?"},{"who":"Mr Karim","t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম। আমার নাম করিম। তুমি কোথা থেকে এসেছ?","tr":"walaikum assalam. amar nam korim. tumi kotha theke eshechho?","mean":"Hello. My name is Karim. Where have you come from?"},{"who":"Nadia","t":"আমি লন্ডন থেকে এসেছি। আমি একটু একটু বাংলা বলতে পারি।","tr":"ami london theke eshechhi. ami ektu ektu bangla bolte pari","mean":"I've come from London. I can speak a little Bangla."},{"who":"Mr Karim","t":"খুব ভালো! তোমার সাথে পরিচিত হয়ে ভালো লাগল।","tr":"khub bhalo! tomar shathe porichito hoye bhalo laglo","mean":"Very good! Nice to meet you."}],"title":"Nice to meet you"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"{{পরিচিত হয়ে ভালো লাগল}} means “it felt good to get to know you”. With adults, use {{আপনার সাথে}} (with you, polite)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Introduce yourself out loud. Swap in your own name and city.","lines":["আমার নাম …।","আমি … থেকে এসেছি।","আমি … থাকি।","আমি একটু একটু বাংলা বলতে পারি।","আপনার নাম কী?"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “My name is Sara”?","options":["আমি নাম সারা।","সারা কী নাম?","আমার নাম সারা।","তোমার নাম সারা।"],"answer":2,"explain":"{{আমার}} = my, {{নাম}} = name. No word for “is”."},{"q":"Listen. What is being asked?","say":"আপনার নাম কী?","options":["What is your name?","Where do you live?","How old are you?","How are you today?"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{আমি ঢাকায় থাকি}} means…","options":["I am from London.","I live in Dhaka.","I am going to Dhaka.","Dhaka is my name."],"answer":1},{"q":"A girl says she is a student. Which word does she use?","options":["ছাত্র","বছর","বয়স","ছাত্রী"],"answer":3},{"q":"You didn't catch what someone said. What do you say?","options":["আবার বলবেন?","ভালো থাকবেন।","আমার নাম কী?","ঠিক আছে।"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আমি একটু একটু বাংলা বলতে পারি।","options":["I don't understand Bangla at all.","Please speak Bangla slowly.","I can speak a little Bangla.","My mother speaks good Bangla."],"answer":2},{"q":"Which word means “what”?","options":["কে","কেন","কোথায়","কী"],"answer":3,"explain":"{{কে}} = who, {{কেন}} = why, {{কোথায়}} = where."}]}]},{"id":"u3-numbers","icon":"১২৩","title":"Numbers 1–20","subtitle":"Bangla digits and number words","minutes":14,"goals":["Read the Bangla digits ০–৯","Count from 1 to 20","Use numbers with {{টা}} to count things"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangla has its own digits! They work just like 0–9: same system, different shapes. Once you know ten little shapes, you can read any number on a price tag, a bus or a clock."},{"type":"table","head":["Digit","Bangla digit","Word","Say it"],"rows":[["1","{{১}}","{{এক}}","ek"],["2","{{২}}","{{দুই}}","dui"],["3","{{৩}}","{{তিন}}","tin"],["4","{{৪}}","{{চার}}","char"],["5","{{৫}}","{{পাঁচ}}","panch"],["6","{{৬}}","{{ছয়}}","chhoy"],["7","{{৭}}","{{সাত}}","shat"],["8","{{৮}}","{{আট}}","at"],["9","{{৯}}","{{নয়}}","noy"],["10","{{১০}}","{{দশ}}","dosh"],["0","{{০}}","{{শূন্য}}","shunno"]],"title":"0 to 10"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Careful: {{৪}} (4) looks like an English 8, and {{৭}} (7) looks a bit like a 9. Bangla {{৮}} is 8. Take your time with these!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"{{নয়}} means “nine”, but it is also a word for “is not”. Context always makes it clear."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"এগারো","tr":"egaro","mean":"11 (১১)"},{"t":"বারো","tr":"baro","mean":"12 (১২)"},{"t":"তেরো","tr":"tero","mean":"13 (১৩)"},{"t":"চৌদ্দ","tr":"choddo","mean":"14 (১৪)"},{"t":"পনেরো","tr":"ponero","mean":"15 (১৫)"},{"t":"ষোলো","tr":"sholo","mean":"16 (১৬)"},{"t":"সতেরো","tr":"shotero","mean":"17 (১৭)"},{"t":"আঠারো","tr":"atharo","mean":"18 (১৮)"},{"t":"উনিশ","tr":"unish","mean":"19 (১৯)"},{"t":"বিশ","tr":"bish","mean":"20 (২০)"}],"title":"11 to 20"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"11 to 18 mostly end in {{-রো}} (-ro): {{এগারো}}, {{বারো}}, {{তেরো}}, {{পনেরো}}, {{ষোলো}}, {{সতেরো}}, {{আঠারো}}. Then {{উনিশ}} (19) means “one short of {{বিশ}} (20)”."},{"type":"text","text":"To count things, add {{টা}} to the number: {{একটা}} (one), {{দুইটা}} (two), {{তিনটা}} (three). The noun stays singular, so there is no -s.","title":"Counting things"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"একটা কলম","tr":"ekta kolom","mean":"one pen / a pen","hl":"একটা"},{"t":"দুইটা বই","tr":"duita boi","mean":"two books","hl":"দুইটা"},{"t":"পাঁচটা আম","tr":"panchta am","mean":"five mangoes","hl":"পাঁচটা"},{"t":"দশটা ডিম","tr":"doshta dim","mean":"ten eggs","hl":"দশটা"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"In West Bengal you'll hear {{দুটো}} (two) and {{তিনটে}} (three). In Bangladesh, {{দুইটা}} and {{তিনটা}} are normal. Both are correct Bangla."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{বিশ}} (20) has an old partner word, {{কুড়ি}}, still used in villages and markets to count things in twenties."},{"type":"practice","text":"Count aloud from 1 to 20, then read the digits.","lines":["এক দুই তিন চার পাঁচ","ছয় সাত আট নয় দশ","এগারো বারো তেরো চৌদ্দ পনেরো","ষোলো সতেরো আঠারো উনিশ বিশ","১ ৫ ৮ ১২ ১৭ ২০"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Which number is {{৭}}?","options":["9","7","4","1"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which Bangla digit is 4?","options":["৮","৯","৭","৪"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Which number do you hear?","say":"বারো","options":["11","12","20","2"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say 15?","options":["পাঁচ","এগারো","পনেরো","উনিশ"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. Which number do you hear?","say":"ছয়","options":["6","16","9","7"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you say “three books”?","options":["তিনটা বই","তিন বইগুলো","বই তিন","তিনটা বইরা"],"answer":0,"explain":"Number + {{টা}} + noun. No plural ending."},{"q":"What does {{উনিশ}} mean?","options":["9","90","11","19"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u3-money","icon":"৳","title":"Numbers & Money","subtitle":"Big numbers, taka and shopping","minutes":14,"goals":["Say tens, hundreds and thousands","Understand prices in taka","Ask “How much?” and bargain politely"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangladesh's money is the {{টাকা}} (taka), written ৳. Let's learn the numbers you need for shopping, and a few phrases for the market."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"ত্রিশ","tr":"trish","mean":"30"},{"t":"চল্লিশ","tr":"chollish","mean":"40"},{"t":"পঞ্চাশ","tr":"ponchash","mean":"50"},{"t":"ষাট","tr":"shat","mean":"60"},{"t":"সত্তর","tr":"shottor","mean":"70"},{"t":"আশি","tr":"ashi","mean":"80"},{"t":"নব্বই","tr":"nobboi","mean":"90"},{"t":"একশো","tr":"eksho","mean":"100"},{"t":"এক হাজার","tr":"ek hajar","mean":"1,000"},{"t":"এক লাখ","tr":"ek lakh","mean":"100,000"},{"t":"এক কোটি","tr":"ek koti","mean":"10,000,000"}],"title":"Tens and big numbers"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Numbers 21 to 99 each have their own word (like {{পঁচিশ}} = 25, {{পঞ্চাশ}} = 50). Don't try to learn them all at once! Learn the tens first, and the prices you use most."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"দুইশো","tr":"duisho","mean":"200"},{"t":"পাঁচশো","tr":"panchsho","mean":"500"},{"t":"দুই হাজার","tr":"dui hajar","mean":"2,000"},{"t":"পঁচিশ","tr":"pochish","mean":"25"},{"t":"সাড়ে তিনশো","tr":"sare tinsho","mean":"350","note":"{{সাড়ে}} = and a half"}],"title":"Building big numbers"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"South Asia counts big numbers in lakhs and crores. {{এক লাখ}} = 1,00,000 (one hundred thousand) and {{এক কোটি}} = 1,00,00,000 (ten million). Notice where the commas go!"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"টাকা","tr":"taka","mean":"taka (money)","example":{"t":"পঞ্চাশ টাকা","tr":"ponchash taka","mean":"fifty taka"}},{"t":"পয়সা","tr":"poysha","mean":"paisa (100 = 1 taka)"},{"t":"দাম","tr":"dam","mean":"price"},{"t":"কত?","tr":"koto?","mean":"how much? how many?"},{"t":"সস্তা","tr":"shosta","mean":"cheap"},{"t":"বেশি","tr":"beshi","mean":"too much, a lot"},{"t":"ভাংতি","tr":"bhangti","mean":"small change"}],"title":"Money words"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"এটার দাম কত?","tr":"etar dam koto?","mean":"How much is this?","note":"literally “this one's price how much?”","hl":"কত"},{"t":"এটা কত টাকা?","tr":"eta koto taka?","mean":"How many taka is this?"},{"t":"একশো বিশ টাকা।","tr":"eksho bish taka","mean":"120 taka."},{"t":"অনেক দাম!","tr":"onek dam!","mean":"That's very expensive!"},{"t":"একটু কম রাখেন।","tr":"ektu kom rakhen","mean":"Please make it a bit cheaper.","note":"used when bargaining"},{"t":"ভাংতি আছে?","tr":"bhangti achhe?","mean":"Do you have change?"}],"title":"At the shop"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Customer","t":"ভাই, এই আমগুলোর দাম কত?","tr":"bhai, ei amgulor dam koto?","mean":"Brother, how much are these mangoes?"},{"who":"Seller","t":"এক কেজি একশো বিশ টাকা।","tr":"ek keji eksho bish taka","mean":"120 taka a kilo."},{"who":"Customer","t":"অনেক দাম! একটু কম রাখেন।","tr":"onek dam! ektu kom rakhen","mean":"That's a lot! Make it a bit less."},{"who":"Seller","t":"ঠিক আছে, একশো টাকা দেন।","tr":"thik achhe, eksho taka den","mean":"OK, give me 100 taka."},{"who":"Customer","t":"দুই কেজি দেন। ধন্যবাদ।","tr":"dui keji den. dhonnobad","mean":"Give me two kilos. Thanks."}],"title":"Buying mangoes"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"In markets, bargaining is normal and friendly. In shops with fixed prices ({{একদাম}}, “one price”), people don't bargain. Calling the seller {{ভাই}} (brother) or {{আপা}} (sister) keeps it warm."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the prices aloud.","lines":["১০ টাকা","৫০ টাকা","১০০ টাকা","৫০০ টাকা","এটার দাম কত?","একটু কম রাখেন।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you ask “How much is this?”","options":["এটা কী?","আপনার নাম কী?","এটার দাম কত?","আপনি কোথায় থাকেন?"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. How much does it cost?","say":"পঞ্চাশ টাকা","options":["15 taka","500 taka","50 taka","5 taka"],"answer":2},{"q":"What is {{একশো}}?","options":["100","1,000","10","100,000"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{এক লাখ}} is…","options":["1,000","100,000","1,000,000","10,000,000"],"answer":1},{"q":"The price is too high. What can you say?","options":["একটু কম রাখেন।","অনেক সস্তা!","আরও বেশি দেন।","ভালো থাকবেন।"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What is the person asking for?","say":"ভাংতি আছে?","options":["a receipt","a bigger bag","small change","the price list"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which number is {{চল্লিশ}}?","options":["4","40","14","400"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u3-time","icon":"সময়","title":"Days & Time","subtitle":"Days of the week, parts of the day, telling the time","minutes":14,"goals":["Name the days of the week","Use today, yesterday and tomorrow","Ask and tell the time"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Every Bangla day name ends in {{বার}} (bar), which means “day of the week”. Several come from the planets, just like the English names."},{"type":"table","head":["English","Bangla","Say it"],"rows":[["Sunday","{{রবিবার}}","robibar"],["Monday","{{সোমবার}}","shombar"],["Tuesday","{{মঙ্গলবার}}","mongolbar"],["Wednesday","{{বুধবার}}","budhbar"],["Thursday","{{বৃহস্পতিবার}}","brihoshpotibar"],["Friday","{{শুক্রবার}}","shukrobar"],["Saturday","{{শনিবার}}","shonibar"]],"title":"Days of the week"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{রবি}} = the Sun, so {{রবিবার}} is Sun-day. {{সোম}} = the Moon: Mon-day. {{শনি}} = Saturn: Satur-day. Same idea as English!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"In Bangladesh the weekend is **Friday and Saturday**. Friday ({{শুক্রবার}}) is the day of the big midday prayer, and families often share a special lunch."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"আজ","tr":"aj","mean":"today"},{"t":"কাল","tr":"kal","mean":"yesterday OR tomorrow"},{"t":"পরশু","tr":"porshu","mean":"the day after tomorrow / before yesterday"},{"t":"এখন","tr":"ekhon","mean":"now"},{"t":"দিন","tr":"din","mean":"day"},{"t":"সপ্তাহ","tr":"shoptaho","mean":"week"},{"t":"মাস","tr":"mash","mean":"month"},{"t":"বছর","tr":"bochhor","mean":"year"}],"title":"Time words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"{{কাল}} means both “yesterday” and “tomorrow”! The verb tells you which: {{কাল এসেছিলাম}} (I came yesterday) vs {{কাল আসব}} (I'll come tomorrow)."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"সকাল","tr":"shokal","mean":"morning"},{"t":"দুপুর","tr":"dupur","mean":"midday, early afternoon"},{"t":"বিকাল","tr":"bikal","mean":"late afternoon"},{"t":"সন্ধ্যা","tr":"shondhya","mean":"evening (around sunset)"},{"t":"রাত","tr":"rat","mean":"night"}],"title":"Parts of the day"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"In Bangladesh people say {{বিকাল}}; in West Bengal and in books you'll also see {{বিকেল}}. Same word, same meaning."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"কয়টা বাজে?","tr":"koyta baje?","mean":"What time is it?","note":"literally “how many has it struck?”"},{"t":"এখন তিনটা বাজে।","tr":"ekhon tinta baje","mean":"It's three o'clock now.","hl":"তিনটা"},{"t":"সাড়ে চারটা","tr":"sare charta","mean":"half past four","hl":"সাড়ে"},{"t":"সোয়া পাঁচটা","tr":"shoa panchta","mean":"quarter past five","hl":"সোয়া"},{"t":"পৌনে ছয়টা","tr":"poune chhoyta","mean":"quarter to six","hl":"পৌনে"},{"t":"সকাল আটটায়","tr":"shokal atay","mean":"at eight in the morning","note":"{{-য়}} = at"}],"title":"Telling the time"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Two special times: 1:30 is {{দেড়টা}} (derta) and 2:30 is {{আড়াইটা}} (araita). Not “sare-one” or “sare-two”!"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি শুক্রবার সকালে আসব।","tr":"ami shukrobar shokale ashbo","mean":"I'll come on Friday morning.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"শুক্রবার","mean":"Friday"},{"t":"সকালে","mean":"in the morning"},{"t":"আসব","mean":"will come"}],"note":"Time words come early in the sentence. The verb comes last."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["আজ সোমবার।","কাল শুক্রবার।","কয়টা বাজে?","এখন সাড়ে চারটা বাজে।","সকাল আটটায় স্কুল।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Which day is {{শুক্রবার}}?","options":["Thursday","Saturday","Sunday","Friday"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Which day is it?","say":"সোমবার","options":["Tuesday","Sunday","Wednesday","Monday"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{কাল}} can mean…","options":["only today","yesterday or tomorrow","only next week","now"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you ask “What time is it?”","options":["আজ কী বার?","কয়টা বাজে?","কত টাকা?","কখন আসবে?"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{সাড়ে চারটা}} is…","options":["4:30","4:15","3:45","4:00"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What time is it?","say":"দেড়টা","options":["2:30","1:15","1:30","12:30"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which word means “evening”?","options":["সকাল","দুপুর","সন্ধ্যা","রাত"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u3-family","icon":"মা","title":"Family & Kinship","subtitle":"Rich Bangla words for every relative","minutes":16,"goals":["Name close family members","Tell father's side from mother's side","Use family words politely with strangers"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"English has one word, “uncle”. Bangla has several! Each relative has a special word that shows **whose side** of the family they are on. It sounds like a lot, but it's very logical."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"পরিবার","tr":"poribar","mean":"family"},{"t":"বাবা","tr":"baba","mean":"father","example":{"t":"আমার বাবা ডাক্তার।","tr":"amar baba daktar","mean":"My father is a doctor."}},{"t":"মা","tr":"ma","mean":"mother"},{"t":"ভাই","tr":"bhai","mean":"brother"},{"t":"বোন","tr":"bon","mean":"sister"},{"t":"ছেলে","tr":"chhele","mean":"son, boy"},{"t":"মেয়ে","tr":"meye","mean":"daughter, girl"},{"t":"স্বামী","tr":"shami","mean":"husband"},{"t":"স্ত্রী","tr":"stri","mean":"wife"}],"title":"Close family"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Many Muslim families in Bangladesh say {{আব্বু}} (dad) and {{আম্মু}} (mum). Older siblings are called {{ভাইয়া}} (big brother) and {{আপু}} (big sister). Using a name alone for an older sibling sounds rude!"},{"type":"table","head":["Relative","Father's side","Mother's side"],"rows":[["grandfather","{{দাদা}} (dada)","{{নানা}} (nana)"],["grandmother","{{দাদি}} (dadi)","{{নানি}} (nani)"],["uncle (parent's brother)","{{চাচা}} (chacha)","{{মামা}} (mama)"],["aunt (uncle's wife)","{{চাচি}} (chachi)","{{মামি}} (mami)"],["aunt (parent's sister)","{{ফুফু}} (fufu)","{{খালা}} (khala)"],["uncle (aunt's husband)","{{ফুফা}} (fufa)","{{খালু}} (khalu)"]],"title":"Two sides of the family"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Mother's side words often start with M or Kh: {{মামা}}, {{মামি}}, {{খালা}}, {{খালু}}. And {{নানা}}/{{নানি}} sound like English “nana”, which also means grandma for many people!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"In Hindu families and in West Bengal, some words change: {{দাদা}} means **elder brother**, grandfather is {{ঠাকুরদা}} or {{দাদু}}, father's brother is {{কাকা}}, father's sister is {{পিসি}}, and mother's sister is {{মাসি}}. Listen to what each family uses."},{"type":"text","text":"Cousins are easy: add {{-তো}} to the uncle or aunt word, then say brother or sister.","title":"Cousins"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"চাচাতো ভাই","tr":"chachato bhai","mean":"cousin (son of father's brother)","hl":"চাচাতো"},{"t":"মামাতো বোন","tr":"mamato bon","mean":"cousin (daughter of mother's brother)","hl":"মামাতো"},{"t":"খালাতো ভাই","tr":"khalato bhai","mean":"cousin (son of mother's sister)","hl":"খালাতো"},{"t":"ফুফাতো বোন","tr":"fufato bon","mean":"cousin (daughter of father's sister)","hl":"ফুফাতো"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Cousins are often as close as brothers and sisters, and people may simply call them {{ভাই}} or {{বোন}}."},{"type":"sentence","t":"উনি আমার মামা।","tr":"uni amar mama","mean":"He is my uncle (mother's brother).","words":[{"t":"উনি","mean":"he/she (respectful)"},{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"মামা","mean":"mother's brother"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Bangladeshis use family words with strangers too. Call an older man {{চাচা}}, an older woman {{খালা}}, a young man {{ভাই}} and a young woman {{আপা}}. In Dhaka, people even call rickshaw drivers and tea sellers {{মামা}}. It's friendly and respectful."},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Tania","t":"এটা কার ছবি?","tr":"eta kar chhobi?","mean":"Whose photo is this?"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"এটা আমার নানা আর নানি।","tr":"eta amar nana ar nani","mean":"These are my grandparents (mum's side)."},{"who":"Tania","t":"আর ইনি কে?","tr":"ar ini ke?","mean":"And who is this?"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"ইনি আমার খালা। আর ও আমার খালাতো বোন।","tr":"ini amar khala. ar o amar khalato bon","mean":"This is my aunt (mum's sister). And that's my cousin."}],"title":"Looking at photos"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud, then say who each person is in your family.","lines":["আমার বাবা","আমার মা","আমার দাদা আর দাদি","আমার নানা আর নানি","আমার চাচা","আমার খালা","আমার মামাতো ভাই"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Your mother's brother is your…","options":["মামা","চাচা","খালু","দাদা"],"answer":0},{"q":"Your father's father (in most Bangladeshi Muslim families) is your…","options":["দাদা","নানা","মামা","ভাই"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. Who is this relative?","say":"খালা","options":["father's sister","mother's brother","grandmother","mother's sister"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{ফুফু}} is…","options":["mother's sister","father's sister","father's brother","older sister"],"answer":1},{"q":"What is a {{চাচাতো ভাই}}?","options":["an older brother","a grandfather","an uncle","a cousin"],"answer":3,"explain":"The son of your {{চাচা}} (father's brother)."},{"q":"In West Bengal, {{দাদা}} usually means…","options":["grandfather (mum's side)","elder brother","uncle","father"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Who is it?","say":"নানি","options":["paternal grandmother","an aunt","an older sister","maternal grandmother"],"answer":3},{"q":"How might you politely call an older woman you don't know?","options":["আম্মু","বোন","খালা","মেয়ে"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u3-food","icon":"ভাত","title":"Food & Drink","subtitle":"Rice, fish, dal and table talk","minutes":14,"goals":["Name everyday Bangladeshi foods","Say what you like and what you want","Use the verb {{খাওয়া}} for eating and drinking"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Food is love in Bangladesh! A guest is always offered something to eat. Let's learn the words you will need at the table."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"An old saying: {{মাছে-ভাতে বাঙালি}} (“fish and rice make a Bengali”). Rice and fish are at the heart of the meal, and {{ইলিশ}} (hilsa) is the national fish."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"ভাত","tr":"bhat","mean":"cooked rice, a meal","example":{"t":"আমি ভাত খাই।","tr":"ami bhat khai","mean":"I eat rice."}},{"t":"মাছ","tr":"machh","mean":"fish"},{"t":"ডাল","tr":"dal","mean":"lentil soup, dal"},{"t":"মাংস","tr":"mangsho","mean":"meat"},{"t":"মুরগি","tr":"murgi","mean":"chicken"},{"t":"ডিম","tr":"dim","mean":"egg"},{"t":"রুটি","tr":"ruti","mean":"flatbread"},{"t":"সবজি","tr":"shobji","mean":"vegetables"},{"t":"ফল","tr":"fol","mean":"fruit"},{"t":"আম","tr":"am","mean":"mango"}],"title":"At the table"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"পানি","tr":"pani","mean":"water"},{"t":"চা","tr":"cha","mean":"tea"},{"t":"দুধ","tr":"dudh","mean":"milk"},{"t":"চিনি","tr":"chini","mean":"sugar"},{"t":"লবণ","tr":"lobon","mean":"salt"},{"t":"ঝাল","tr":"jhal","mean":"spicy (hot)"},{"t":"মিষ্টি","tr":"mishti","mean":"sweet; sweets"}],"title":"Drinks and tastes"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"In Bangladesh water is {{পানি}}. In West Bengal and in many Hindu families it is {{জল}}. Both mean water."},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"Bangla uses one verb, {{খাওয়া}} (to eat), for food **and** drinks: {{পানি খাই}} (I drink water), {{চা খাই}} (I drink tea)."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আমার ক্ষুধা লেগেছে।","tr":"amar khudha legechhe","mean":"I'm hungry.","note":"literally “hunger has struck me”"},{"t":"আমি মাছ পছন্দ করি।","tr":"ami machh pochhondo kori","mean":"I like fish."},{"t":"আমি ঝাল খাই না।","tr":"ami jhal khai na","mean":"I don't eat spicy food."},{"t":"এক গ্লাস পানি দেন।","tr":"ek glash pani den","mean":"Please give me a glass of water."},{"t":"আরেকটু দেন।","tr":"arektu den","mean":"A little more, please."},{"t":"খুব মজা হয়েছে!","tr":"khub moja hoyechhe!","mean":"It's delicious!","note":"{{মজা}} = tasty, in Bangladesh"}],"title":"Useful phrases"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি ভাত আর ডাল খাই।","tr":"ami bhat ar dal khai","mean":"I eat rice and dal.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"ভাত","mean":"rice"},{"t":"আর","mean":"and"},{"t":"ডাল","mean":"dal"},{"t":"খাই","mean":"eat"}],"note":"The verb {{খাই}} goes at the end."},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Nani","t":"খেয়েছ, বাবা?","tr":"kheyechho, baba?","mean":"Have you eaten, dear?"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"না, নানি। আমার ক্ষুধা লেগেছে।","tr":"na, nani. amar khudha legechhe","mean":"No, Grandma. I'm hungry."},{"who":"Nani","t":"বসো। ভাত, মাছ আর ডাল আছে।","tr":"bosho. bhat, machh ar dal achhe","mean":"Sit down. There's rice, fish and dal."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"খুব মজা হয়েছে! আরেকটু দেন।","tr":"khub moja hoyechhe! arektu den","mean":"It's delicious! A little more, please."}],"title":"At Nani's house"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{খেয়েছেন?}} (“Have you eaten?”) is a caring everyday greeting, like “How are you?”. And traditionally, many people eat rice with the right hand."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["ভাত, মাছ, ডাল","এক কাপ চা","আমি আম পছন্দ করি।","আমার ক্ষুধা লেগেছে।","খুব মজা হয়েছে!"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"What is {{ভাত}}?","options":["bread","cooked rice","fish curry","tea"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is it?","say":"মাছ","options":["meat","egg","fish","milk"],"answer":2},{"q":"In Bangladesh, “water” is…","options":["পানি","দুধ","চা","ডাল"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you say “I'm hungry”?","options":["আমি মাছ খাই।","আরেকটু দেন।","খুব মজা হয়েছে!","আমার ক্ষুধা লেগেছে।"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which verb do you use for “drink tea”?","options":["খাওয়া","করা","যাওয়া","দেখা"],"answer":0,"explain":"Bangla says {{চা খাই}}: “I eat tea”."},{"q":"Listen. What does the speaker mean?","say":"খুব মজা হয়েছে!","options":["It's delicious!","It's too spicy!","I'm not hungry.","Where's the water?"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{ঝাল}} means…","options":["sweet","salty","spicy","sour"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u3-colours","icon":"রং","title":"Colours & Clothes","subtitle":"Describe what people wear","minutes":12,"goals":["Name the main colours","Name everyday and traditional clothes","Put a colour before a noun"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangladesh is full of colour: bright saris, green rice fields, red-and-green flags. Colour is {{রং}} (rong)."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"লাল","tr":"lal","mean":"red"},{"t":"নীল","tr":"nil","mean":"blue"},{"t":"সবুজ","tr":"shobuj","mean":"green"},{"t":"হলুদ","tr":"holud","mean":"yellow"},{"t":"সাদা","tr":"shada","mean":"white"},{"t":"কালো","tr":"kalo","mean":"black"},{"t":"কমলা","tr":"komola","mean":"orange"},{"t":"গোলাপি","tr":"golapi","mean":"pink"},{"t":"বেগুনি","tr":"beguni","mean":"purple"},{"t":"বাদামি","tr":"badami","mean":"brown"},{"t":"আকাশি","tr":"akashi","mean":"sky blue"}],"title":"Colours"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Many colours are named after things: {{গোলাপি}} from {{গোলাপ}} (rose), {{বেগুনি}} from {{বেগুন}} (aubergine), {{কমলা}} = an orange, {{আকাশি}} from {{আকাশ}} (sky). {{হলুদ}} is also turmeric!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"The flag of Bangladesh is a red circle on green. People call it {{লাল-সবুজ}} (red-green). Green for the land, red for the sun and for those who gave their lives in 1971."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"জামা","tr":"jama","mean":"top, shirt, dress (general word)"},{"t":"শার্ট","tr":"shart","mean":"shirt"},{"t":"প্যান্ট","tr":"pyant","mean":"trousers"},{"t":"শাড়ি","tr":"shari","mean":"sari"},{"t":"সালোয়ার কামিজ","tr":"shaloar kamij","mean":"shalwar kameez"},{"t":"ওড়না","tr":"orna","mean":"long scarf"},{"t":"পাঞ্জাবি","tr":"panjabi","mean":"long tunic for men"},{"t":"লুঙ্গি","tr":"lungi","mean":"wrap-around lungi"},{"t":"জুতা","tr":"juta","mean":"shoes"},{"t":"টুপি","tr":"tupi","mean":"cap, prayer cap"}],"title":"Clothes"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"On Eid, many men wear a new {{পাঞ্জাবি}}, and on {{পহেলা বৈশাখ}} (Bangla New Year, 14 April) people wear red and white."},{"type":"rule","name":"Colour before noun","color":"green","desc":"Like English, the colour comes before the thing. It never changes its ending.","examples":[{"t":"লাল শাড়ি","tr":"lal shari","mean":"a red sari","hl":"লাল"},{"t":"সাদা পাঞ্জাবি","tr":"shada panjabi","mean":"a white panjabi","hl":"সাদা"},{"t":"কালো জুতা","tr":"kalo juta","mean":"black shoes","hl":"কালো"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার জামাটা নীল।","tr":"amar jamata nil","mean":"My shirt is blue.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"জামাটা","mean":"the shirt"},{"t":"নীল","mean":"blue"}],"note":"No verb “is”: “my shirt blue”."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"তোমার প্রিয় রং কী?","tr":"tomar priyo rong ki?","mean":"What's your favourite colour?"},{"t":"আমার প্রিয় রং সবুজ।","tr":"amar priyo rong shobuj","mean":"My favourite colour is green."},{"t":"লাল শাড়িটা খুব সুন্দর।","tr":"lal sharita khub shundor","mean":"The red sari is very beautiful."}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Describe what you are wearing today.","lines":["আমার জামাটা …।","আমার জুতা কালো।","লাল শাড়ি","সাদা পাঞ্জাবি","আমার প্রিয় রং …।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"{{সবুজ}} is…","options":["blue","yellow","grey","green"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Which colour?","say":"লাল","options":["black","red","white","pink"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say “white shirt”?","options":["শার্ট সাদাটা","শার্টের সাদা","সাদার শার্ট","সাদা শার্ট"],"answer":3},{"q":"A {{পাঞ্জাবি}} is…","options":["a pair of shoes","a long tunic","a long scarf","a cap"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which colour is named after the aubergine?","options":["গোলাপি","কমলা","হলুদ","বেগুনি"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আমার প্রিয় রং সবুজ।","options":["Green is a bad colour.","My shirt is not green.","My favourite colour is green.","I have a green sari at home."],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u3-home","icon":"ঘর","title":"Home & Objects","subtitle":"Rooms, things, and where they are","minutes":12,"goals":["Name rooms and everyday objects","Say where something is","Ask “Where is…?”"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Let's walk around a Bangladeshi home and learn the words for the things we see. We will also learn how to say where things are."},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"{{বাড়ি}} is a house or your family home; {{বাসা}} is the place you live now, often a flat in the city. A Dhaka family may say: “our {{বাসা}} is in Dhaka, but our {{বাড়ি}} is in Barishal.”"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"বাড়ি","tr":"bari","mean":"house, family home"},{"t":"বাসা","tr":"basha","mean":"flat, place where you live"},{"t":"ঘর","tr":"ghor","mean":"room; home"},{"t":"রান্নাঘর","tr":"rannaghor","mean":"kitchen"},{"t":"বাথরুম","tr":"bathrum","mean":"bathroom"},{"t":"দরজা","tr":"dorja","mean":"door"},{"t":"জানালা","tr":"janala","mean":"window"},{"t":"ছাদ","tr":"chhad","mean":"roof, flat rooftop"}],"title":"Rooms"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"{{রান্নাঘর}} = {{রান্না}} (cooking) + {{ঘর}} (room). Many Bangla words snap together like this."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"টেবিল","tr":"tebil","mean":"table"},{"t":"চেয়ার","tr":"cheyar","mean":"chair"},{"t":"খাট","tr":"khat","mean":"bed (frame)"},{"t":"পাখা","tr":"pakha","mean":"fan"},{"t":"বাতি","tr":"bati","mean":"light, lamp"},{"t":"বই","tr":"boi","mean":"book"},{"t":"কলম","tr":"kolom","mean":"pen"},{"t":"ফোন","tr":"fon","mean":"phone"},{"t":"চাবি","tr":"chabi","mean":"key"},{"t":"ব্যাগ","tr":"byag","mean":"bag"}],"title":"Things"},{"type":"rule","name":"Where is it?","color":"blue","desc":"Bangla puts the place word **after** the thing it relates to, joined by {{-র / -এর}} (of): “table-of on” = on the table.","examples":[{"t":"টেবিলের উপর","tr":"tebiler upor","mean":"on the table","hl":"উপর"},{"t":"খাটের নিচে","tr":"khater niche","mean":"under the bed","hl":"নিচে"},{"t":"ব্যাগের ভিতরে","tr":"byager bhitore","mean":"inside the bag","hl":"ভিতরে"},{"t":"দরজার পাশে","tr":"dorjar pashe","mean":"next to the door","hl":"পাশে"},{"t":"ঘরের বাইরে","tr":"ghorer baire","mean":"outside the room","hl":"বাইরে"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"চাবিটা টেবিলের উপর আছে।","tr":"chabita tebiler upor achhe","mean":"The key is on the table.","words":[{"t":"চাবিটা","mean":"the key"},{"t":"টেবিলের","mean":"table's"},{"t":"উপর","mean":"on"},{"t":"আছে","mean":"is (there)"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"English says “on the table”. Bangla says “the table's top”. Think of it as describing the **spot**: the table's top, the bed's underneath, the bag's inside."},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Sara","t":"আম্মু, আমার চাবিটা কোথায়?","tr":"ammu, amar chabita kothay?","mean":"Mum, where's my key?"},{"who":"Ammu","t":"দেখো, টেবিলের উপর।","tr":"dekho, tebiler upor","mean":"Look, on the table."},{"who":"Sara","t":"না, এখানে নেই।","tr":"na, ekhane nei","mean":"No, it isn't here."},{"who":"Ammu","t":"তাহলে তোমার ব্যাগের ভিতরে দেখো।","tr":"tahole tomar byager bhitore dekho","mean":"Then look inside your bag."},{"who":"Sara","t":"পেয়েছি! ধন্যবাদ।","tr":"peyechhi! dhonnobad","mean":"Found it! Thanks."}],"title":"The lost key"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["বইটা টেবিলের উপর।","জুতা খাটের নিচে।","ফোনটা ব্যাগের ভিতরে।","পাখাটা চালাও।","আমার কলম কোথায়?"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"{{রান্নাঘর}} is the…","options":["kitchen","bathroom","bedroom","rooftop"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What object is it?","say":"চাবি","options":["key","pen","book","fan"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you say “under the bed”?","options":["নিচে খাট","খাটের উপর","খাটের নিচে","খাট নিচের"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{জানালা}} is a…","options":["door","window","table","lamp"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Where is the phone?","say":"ফোনটা ব্যাগের ভিতরে।","options":["inside the bag","on the table","under the chair","next to the door"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which word is the place you live now, often a city flat?","options":["ছাদ","দরজা","রান্নাঘর","বাসা"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u3-places","icon":"পথ","title":"Places & Transport","subtitle":"Getting around town by rickshaw, bus and boat","minutes":14,"goals":["Name places in town","Name ways to travel","Ask the way and take a rickshaw"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Time to go out! Bangladesh has busy markets, colourful rickshaws and big rivers. Let's learn how to get around."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"বাজার","tr":"bajar","mean":"market"},{"t":"দোকান","tr":"dokan","mean":"shop"},{"t":"স্কুল","tr":"skul","mean":"school"},{"t":"হাসপাতাল","tr":"hashpatal","mean":"hospital"},{"t":"মসজিদ","tr":"moshjid","mean":"mosque"},{"t":"মন্দির","tr":"mondir","mean":"temple"},{"t":"ব্যাংক","tr":"byangk","mean":"bank"},{"t":"রাস্তা","tr":"rasta","mean":"road, street"},{"t":"শহর","tr":"shohor","mean":"town, city"},{"t":"গ্রাম","tr":"gram","mean":"village"}],"title":"Places"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"In Bangladesh a {{হোটেল}} is often a simple **restaurant**, not a place to sleep. A sign saying “hotel” may just mean great rice and curry!"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"রিকশা","tr":"riksha","mean":"cycle rickshaw"},{"t":"সিএনজি","tr":"si-en-ji","mean":"auto-rickshaw (CNG)"},{"t":"বাস","tr":"bas","mean":"bus"},{"t":"ট্রেন","tr":"tren","mean":"train"},{"t":"গাড়ি","tr":"gari","mean":"car"},{"t":"নৌকা","tr":"nouka","mean":"boat"},{"t":"লঞ্চ","tr":"lonch","mean":"river ferry"},{"t":"প্লেন","tr":"plen","mean":"plane"},{"t":"হেঁটে","tr":"hente","mean":"on foot"}],"title":"Transport"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Green auto-rickshaws are called {{সিএনজি}} after the gas they run on. Long river journeys are often made by {{লঞ্চ}}, big ferries that travel overnight."},{"type":"rule","name":"Travel “by” something","color":"purple","desc":"To say how you travel, add {{-এ}} to the vehicle (or {{-তে}} after some vowels).","examples":[{"t":"বাসে","tr":"bashe","mean":"by bus","hl":"বাসে"},{"t":"ট্রেনে","tr":"trene","mean":"by train","hl":"ট্রেনে"},{"t":"রিকশায়","tr":"rikshay","mean":"by rickshaw","hl":"রিকশায়"},{"t":"নৌকায়","tr":"noukay","mean":"by boat","hl":"নৌকায়"}]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"বাজারটা কোথায়?","tr":"bajarta kothay?","mean":"Where is the market?"},{"t":"সোজা যান।","tr":"shoja jan","mean":"Go straight on."},{"t":"ডানে যান।","tr":"dane jan","mean":"Go right."},{"t":"বামে যান।","tr":"bame jan","mean":"Go left."},{"t":"কাছে","tr":"kachhe","mean":"near"},{"t":"দূরে","tr":"dure","mean":"far"}],"title":"Asking the way"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Rafi","t":"মামা, ধানমন্ডি যাবেন?","tr":"mama, dhanmondi jaben?","mean":"Driver, will you go to Dhanmondi?"},{"who":"Driver","t":"যাব। আশি টাকা।","tr":"jabo. ashi taka","mean":"I'll go. 80 taka."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"ষাট টাকায় চলেন।","tr":"shat takay cholen","mean":"Let's go for 60."},{"who":"Driver","t":"ঠিক আছে, উঠেন।","tr":"thik achhe, uthen","mean":"OK, get on."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"মামা, এখানে রাখেন। ধন্যবাদ।","tr":"mama, ekhane rakhen. dhonnobad","mean":"Driver, stop here please. Thanks."}],"title":"Taking a rickshaw"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"In everyday Bangladeshi speech, polite commands often end in {{-েন}}: {{চলেন}}, {{উঠেন}}, {{রাখেন}}. In books you will see the formal {{-ুন}}: {{চলুন}}, {{উঠুন}}, {{রাখুন}}. More in Unit 4!"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি বাসে স্কুলে যাই।","tr":"ami bashe skule jai","mean":"I go to school by bus.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"বাসে","mean":"by bus"},{"t":"স্কুলে","mean":"to school"},{"t":"যাই","mean":"go"}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["বাজারটা কোথায়?","সোজা যান, তারপর ডানে।","মামা, যাবেন?","ভাড়া কত?","এখানে রাখেন।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"{{হাসপাতাল}} is a…","options":["hotel","hospital","school","market"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Which direction?","say":"বামে যান।","options":["left","right","straight on","back"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you ask a rickshaw driver if he'll take you?","options":["মামা, কেমন আছ?","মামা, খেয়েছেন?","মামা, যাবেন?","মামা, নাম কী?"],"answer":2},{"q":"How do you say “by train”?","options":["ট্রেনের","ট্রেনকে","ট্রেনে","ট্রেনটা"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is the person asking?","say":"ভাড়া কত?","options":["Where is the bus?","How much is the fare?","Is it far from here?","Which way to the market?"],"answer":1},{"q":"In Bangladesh, a small {{হোটেল}} is often…","options":["a bank","a bus station","a school","a place to eat"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{গ্রাম}} means…","options":["town","road","village","shop"],"answer":2}]}]}]});
LC.units.push({"id":"grammar","order":4,"icon":"আমি","color":"indigo","title":"Grammar Made Easy","subtitle":"Word order, respect, tenses, questions and the little endings that hold Bangla together","lessons":[{"id":"u4-word-order","icon":"ক্রিয়া","title":"Word Order: Verb Last","subtitle":"Subject, object, verb","minutes":12,"goals":["Put the verb at the end of a sentence","Use “after-words” (postpositions) instead of prepositions","Build simple sentences of your own"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the biggest secret of Bangla grammar: **the verb goes last**. English says “I eat rice”. Bangla says “I rice eat”. Once this clicks, everything else is easier!"},{"type":"rule","name":"Subject + Object + Verb","color":"green","desc":"Who does it, then what, then the action at the very end.","examples":[{"t":"আমি ভাত খাই।","tr":"ami bhat khai","mean":"I eat rice.","hl":"খাই"},{"t":"সারা বই পড়ে।","tr":"shara boi pore","mean":"Sara reads books.","hl":"পড়ে"},{"t":"রাফি ফুটবল খেলে।","tr":"rafi futbol khele","mean":"Rafi plays football.","hl":"খেলে"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি ভাত খাই।","tr":"ami bhat khai","mean":"I eat rice.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"ভাত","mean":"rice"},{"t":"খাই","mean":"eat"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Imagine every Bangla sentence as a little train: the **verb is the last carriage**. Who? What? Where? When? can join in the middle, but the verb always pulls in at the back."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Start with who","t":"আমি","tr":"ami","mean":"I"},{"title":"Add when","t":"আমি প্রতিদিন","tr":"ami protidin","mean":"I every day"},{"title":"Add where","t":"আমি প্রতিদিন স্কুলে","tr":"ami protidin skule","mean":"I every day to school"},{"title":"Finish with the verb","t":"আমি প্রতিদিন স্কুলে যাই।","tr":"ami protidin skule jai","mean":"I go to school every day."}],"title":"Build a sentence step by step"},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাফি তার বোনকে একটা বই দিল।","tr":"rafi tar bonke ekta boi dilo","mean":"Rafi gave his sister a book.","words":[{"t":"রাফি","mean":"Rafi"},{"t":"তার","mean":"his"},{"t":"বোনকে","mean":"to sister"},{"t":"একটা","mean":"a"},{"t":"বই","mean":"book"},{"t":"দিল","mean":"gave"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"After-words, not before-words","color":"blue","desc":"English has prepositions (**in** Dhaka, **with** me). Bangla puts these words **after** the noun: postpositions.","examples":[{"t":"ঢাকা থেকে","tr":"dhaka theke","mean":"from Dhaka","hl":"থেকে"},{"t":"আমার সাথে","tr":"amar shathe","mean":"with me","hl":"সাথে"},{"t":"বাড়ির দিকে","tr":"barir dike","mean":"towards the house","hl":"দিকে"},{"t":"স্কুলের পরে","tr":"skuler pore","mean":"after school","hl":"পরে"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Bangla word order is quite flexible because the endings show who does what. But a beginner can never go wrong with: **who + when + where + what + verb**."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"তুমি কী খাও?","tr":"tumi ki khao?","mean":"What do you eat?","note":"question word stays in the middle"},{"t":"আমি আমার নানির সাথে থাকি।","tr":"ami amar nanir shathe thaki","mean":"I live with my grandmother."},{"t":"বাবা সকালে অফিসে যান।","tr":"baba shokale ofishe jan","mean":"Dad goes to the office in the morning."}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Notice that each sentence ends with the verb.","lines":["আমি ভাত খাই।","সারা বই পড়ে।","আমি প্রতিদিন স্কুলে যাই।","বাবা সকালে অফিসে যান।","আমি ঢাকা থেকে এসেছি।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Where does the verb usually go in a Bangla sentence?","options":["at the start","after the subject","at the end","anywhere at all"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which is the correct way to say “I eat rice”?","options":["আমি ভাত খাই।","আমি খাই ভাত।","খাই আমি ভাত।","ভাত খাই আমি না।"],"answer":0},{"q":"“From Dhaka” in Bangla is…","options":["থেকে ঢাকা","ঢাকা থেকে","ঢাকার থেকেই","থেকে ঢাকার"],"answer":1,"explain":"{{থেকে}} comes after the place."},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"সারা বই পড়ে।","options":["Sara buys books.","The book is Sara's.","Sara doesn't read.","Sara reads books."],"answer":3},{"q":"Which word is the verb in {{রাফি ফুটবল খেলে}}?","options":["রাফি","ফুটবল","none of them","খেলে"],"answer":3},{"q":"How do you say “with me”?","options":["সাথে আমি","আমার সাথে","আমি সাথে","সাথে আমার"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Where does Dad go in the morning?","say":"বাবা সকালে অফিসে যান।","options":["to the market","to school","to the office","to the mosque"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u4-pronouns","icon":"তুমি","title":"Pronouns & Three Levels of Respect","subtitle":"তুই, তুমি and আপনি","minutes":15,"goals":["Know the Bangla pronouns","Choose between তুই, তুমি and আপনি","Match the verb ending to the level of respect"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"English has just one “you”. Bangla has **three**, from very close to very polite. Choosing the right one shows respect, and Bangladeshis notice!"},{"type":"table","head":["","One person","More than one"],"rows":[["I / we","{{আমি}} ami","{{আমরা}} amra"],["you (intimate)","{{তুই}} tui","{{তোরা}} tora"],["you (familiar)","{{তুমি}} tumi","{{তোমরা}} tomra"],["you (polite)","{{আপনি}} apni","{{আপনারা}} apnara"],["he / she","{{সে}} she","{{তারা}} tara"],["he / she (respectful)","{{তিনি}} tini, {{উনি}} uni","{{তাঁরা}} tara, {{ওনারা}} onara"]],"title":"The pronouns"},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"তুই","label":"Very close","desc":"Best friends of the same age, little children, sometimes brothers and sisters. With anyone else it sounds rude!"},{"t":"তুমি","label":"Friendly","desc":"Friends, classmates, younger people, and in many families, parents. Warm and normal."},{"t":"আপনি","label":"Polite","desc":"Strangers, elders, teachers, shopkeepers, anyone you are not sure about."}],"title":"Which “you”?"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"When in doubt, use {{আপনি}}. Being too polite is never a problem. Calling a stranger {{তুই}} can cause real offence."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"In many families children say {{তুমি}} to their parents; in some more traditional families they use {{আপনি}}, especially with the father. Grandparents often call grandchildren {{তুই}} with love."},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"Bangla pronouns have **no gender**. {{সে}} means “he” **or** “she”. Easy!"},{"type":"text","text":"Each “you” has its own verb ending. Here is the verb {{করা}} (to do) in the present:","title":"Verb endings follow respect"},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","Verb","Say it","Ending"],"rows":[["{{আমি}} / {{আমরা}}","{{করি}}","kori","-i"],["{{তুই}} / {{তোরা}}","{{করিস}}","koris","-is"],["{{তুমি}} / {{তোমরা}}","{{করো}}","koro","-o"],["{{আপনি}} / {{আপনারা}}","{{করেন}}","koren","-en"],["{{সে}} / {{তারা}}","{{করে}}","kore","-e"],["{{তিনি}} / {{উনি}}","{{করেন}}","koren","-en"]]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Plural doesn't change the verb: {{আমি করি}}, {{আমরা করি}}. And the respectful {{-েন}} ending is the same for “you” ({{আপনি}}) and “he/she” ({{তিনি}}): **-en = respect**."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"তুই কী করিস?","tr":"tui ki koris?","mean":"What do you do? (to a best friend)","hl":"করিস"},{"t":"তুমি কী করো?","tr":"tumi ki koro?","mean":"What do you do? (friendly)","hl":"করো"},{"t":"আপনি কী করেন?","tr":"apni ki koren?","mean":"What do you do? (polite)","hl":"করেন"}],"title":"One question, three levels"},{"type":"table","head":["","Ordinary","Respectful"],"rows":[["this person (near)","{{এ}} e","{{ইনি}} ini"],["that person (there)","{{ও}} o","{{উনি}} uni"],["he / she (not here)","{{সে}} she","{{তিনি}} tini"]],"title":"Near and far"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"{{তিনি}} is mostly used in writing and formal speech. In conversation people say {{উনি}} for someone they respect: {{উনি আমার শিক্ষক}} (He/She is my teacher)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Ask “How are you?” at each level.","lines":["কেমন আছিস?","কেমন আছ?","কেমন আছেন?","আপনি কী করেন?","উনি আমার শিক্ষক।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Which “you” should you use with a shopkeeper you don't know?","options":["তুই","তুমি","আপনি","সে"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{সে}} can mean…","options":["he or she","only he","only she","they"],"answer":0},{"q":"Choose the verb: {{আপনি কী ___?}}","options":["করিস","করেন","করো","করি"],"answer":1,"explain":"{{আপনি}} takes the {{-েন}} ending."},{"q":"Listen. Who is the speaker most likely talking to?","say":"তুই কী করিস?","options":["a teacher","a stranger","a grandfather","a close friend"],"answer":3},{"q":"Choose the verb: {{আমরা বাংলা ___}} (study)","options":["পড়ি","পড়িস","পড়েন","পড়ো"],"answer":0,"explain":"{{আমরা}} uses the same ending as {{আমি}}."},{"q":"Which pronoun is respectful “he/she” in conversation?","options":["ও","এ","উনি","তুই"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. Which level of respect is this?","say":"কেমন আছেন?","options":["intimate (তুই)","friendly (তুমি)","it isn't a question","polite (আপনি)"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u4-to-be","icon":"আছে","title":"“To Be”: আছে, হয় and No Verb","subtitle":"Three ways to say am, is, are","minutes":15,"goals":["Make “X is Y” sentences with no verb","Use {{আছে}} for being somewhere and for “have”","Use {{হওয়া}} for “become” and general facts"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"English uses “to be” for everything. Bangla splits it into three jobs. Let's take them one at a time."},{"type":"rule","name":"Job 1: “X is Y”: no verb at all!","color":"green","desc":"When you say what or who something is, or describe it, just put the two words side by side.","examples":[{"t":"আমি ছাত্র।","tr":"ami chhatro","mean":"I am a student.","hl":"ছাত্র"},{"t":"সে আমার বন্ধু।","tr":"she amar bondhu","mean":"He/She is my friend.","hl":"বন্ধু"},{"t":"বাড়িটা বড়।","tr":"barita boro","mean":"The house is big.","hl":"বড়"},{"t":"এটা আমার বই।","tr":"eta amar boi","mean":"This is my book.","hl":"বই"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Talk like a newspaper headline: “I student.” “House big.” That's perfect Bangla!"},{"type":"rule","name":"Job 2: আছে: is there / is somewhere / have","color":"blue","desc":"Use {{আছে}} when something **exists** or **is in a place**, for how someone **is**, and for **having** things.","examples":[{"t":"বইটা টেবিলে আছে।","tr":"boita tebile achhe","mean":"The book is on the table.","hl":"আছে"},{"t":"আমি ভালো আছি।","tr":"ami bhalo achhi","mean":"I am well.","hl":"আছি"},{"t":"বাসায় কেউ আছে?","tr":"bashay keu achhe?","mean":"Is anyone at home?","hl":"আছে"},{"t":"আমার একটা বোন আছে।","tr":"amar ekta bon achhe","mean":"I have a sister.","hl":"আছে"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","is / are (now)","was / were"],"rows":[["{{আমি}}","{{আছি}} achhi","{{ছিলাম}} chhilam"],["{{তুই}}","{{আছিস}} achhis","{{ছিলি}} chhili"],["{{তুমি}}","{{আছ}} achho","{{ছিলে}} chhile"],["{{আপনি}} / {{তিনি}}","{{আছেন}} achhen","{{ছিলেন}} chhilen"],["{{সে}} / it","{{আছে}} achhe","{{ছিল}} chhilo"]],"title":"আছে: present and past"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"In the past, Job 1 also uses these forms: {{আমি ছাত্র}} (I am a student) → {{আমি ছাত্র ছিলাম}} (I was a student)."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার দুইটা ভাই আছে।","tr":"amar duita bhai achhe","mean":"I have two brothers.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"দুইটা","mean":"two"},{"t":"ভাই","mean":"brother(s)"},{"t":"আছে","mean":"exist"}],"note":"There is no verb “to have”. Bangla says “my two brothers exist”."},{"type":"rule","name":"Job 3: হওয়া: to be, to become","color":"orange","desc":"Use {{হওয়া}} for becoming something, for the future of “to be”, and for things that usually happen.","examples":[{"t":"আমি ডাক্তার হব।","tr":"ami daktar hobo","mean":"I will be a doctor.","hl":"হব"},{"t":"শীতকালে খুব ঠান্ডা হয়।","tr":"shitkale khub thanda hoy","mean":"It gets very cold in winter.","hl":"হয়"},{"t":"উনি আমার মামা হন।","tr":"uni amar mama hon","mean":"He is my uncle (by relation).","hl":"হন"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"To ask how someone is related to you, people say {{উনি তোমার কী হন?}}, literally “What does he/she become to you?”. A very common family question!"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud and spot the job: no verb, আছে, or হওয়া.","lines":["আমি ছাত্র।","আমি ভালো আছি।","আমার একটা বোন আছে।","বাড়িটা বড়।","আমি ডাক্তার হব।","আমি তখন ছোট ছিলাম।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “I am a student”?","options":["আমি ছাত্র আছি।","আমি ছাত্র।","আমার ছাত্র আছে।","আমি ছাত্র হয়।"],"answer":1,"explain":"Job 1: no verb at all."},{"q":"How do you say “I have a sister”?","options":["আমি একটা বোন।","আমি বোন আছি।","আমার বোন হয়।","আমার একটা বোন আছে।"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Where is the book?","say":"বইটা টেবিলে আছে।","options":["in the bag","on the table","at school","under the bed"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which word means “was” with {{আমি}}?","options":["ছিল","আছি","ছিলাম","হব"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{আমি ডাক্তার হব}} means…","options":["I will be a doctor.","I am a doctor.","I was a doctor.","I have a doctor."],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"বাসায় কেউ আছে?","options":["Is anyone at home?","Who is at school?","The house is big.","I'm at home now."],"answer":0},{"q":"Choose: {{আপনি কেমন ___?}}","options":["আছি","আছিস","ছিলাম","আছেন"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u4-present-simple","icon":"করি","title":"Present Simple","subtitle":"I do, you go, she eats","minutes":15,"goals":["Find the root of a verb","Add the right present ending","Talk about habits and facts"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"The present simple is for habits and facts: “I drink tea”, “She lives in Sylhet”. You already know the endings from the pronouns lesson. Now let's use them with real verbs."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Take the dictionary form","t":"করা","tr":"kora","mean":"to do"},{"title":"Drop the -া to find the root","t":"কর্","tr":"kor","mean":"do-"},{"title":"Add the ending for the person","t":"করি","tr":"kori","mean":"I do"}],"title":"How to build it"},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","করা (do)","খাওয়া (eat)","যাওয়া (go)","থাকা (live)"],"rows":[["{{আমি}} / {{আমরা}}","{{করি}}","{{খাই}}","{{যাই}}","{{থাকি}}"],["{{তুই}} / {{তোরা}}","{{করিস}}","{{খাস}}","{{যাস}}","{{থাকিস}}"],["{{তুমি}} / {{তোমরা}}","{{করো}}","{{খাও}}","{{যাও}}","{{থাকো}}"],["{{আপনি}} / {{তিনি}}","{{করেন}}","{{খান}}","{{যান}}","{{থাকেন}}"],["{{সে}} / {{তারা}}","{{করে}}","{{খায়}}","{{যায়}}","{{থাকে}}"]],"title":"Present simple"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"The five endings: **-i, -is, -o, -en, -e**. Say them like a little song: “ee, is, oh, en, eh”!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Verbs whose root ends in a vowel, like {{খা}} (eat) and {{যা}} (go), squeeze the endings a little: {{খাই}}, {{খাও}}, {{খান}}, {{খায়}}. Listen and copy."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আমি প্রতিদিন চা খাই।","tr":"ami protidin cha khai","mean":"I drink tea every day.","hl":"খাই"},{"t":"সে স্কুলে যায়।","tr":"she skule jay","mean":"He/She goes to school.","hl":"যায়"},{"t":"আপনি কোথায় থাকেন?","tr":"apni kothay thaken?","mean":"Where do you live?","hl":"থাকেন"},{"t":"তুমি কী করো?","tr":"tumi ki koro?","mean":"What do you do?","hl":"করো"},{"t":"আমরা বাংলা শিখি।","tr":"amra bangla shikhi","mean":"We learn Bangla.","hl":"শিখি"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার মা রোজ সকালে নামাজ পড়েন।","tr":"amar ma roj shokale namaj poren","mean":"My mother prays every morning.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"মা","mean":"mother"},{"t":"রোজ","mean":"every day"},{"t":"সকালে","mean":"in the morning"},{"t":"নামাজ","mean":"prayer"},{"t":"পড়েন","mean":"says (respectful)"}],"note":"We use the respectful {{-েন}} for parents and elders, even when talking **about** them."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Talking about your parents, grandparents or teachers, use the respectful ending: {{বাবা অফিসে যান}}, {{দাদি গল্প বলেন}}. Using {{যায়}} for your father can sound disrespectful."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Then change each sentence to talk about yourself.","lines":["সে স্কুলে যায়।","আপনি কোথায় থাকেন?","বাবা অফিসে যান।","আমরা বাংলা শিখি।","আমি প্রতিদিন চা খাই।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Choose: {{আমি ভাত ___}}","options":["খায়","খান","খাই","খাস"],"answer":2},{"q":"Choose: {{সে স্কুলে ___}}","options":["যাই","যান","যায়","যাও"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. Who is the sentence about?","say":"আপনি কোথায় থাকেন?","options":["you (polite)","I","he (ordinary)","we"],"answer":0},{"q":"What is the root of {{করা}}?","options":["করি","কর্","কা","রা"],"answer":1},{"q":"Talking about your grandmother, which is best?","options":["দাদি গল্প বলেন।","দাদি গল্প বলে।","দাদি গল্প বলিস।","দাদি গল্প বলি।"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আমরা বাংলা শিখি।","options":["I teach Bangla.","They speak Bangla.","We learn Bangla.","We don't know Bangla."],"answer":2},{"q":"Choose: {{তুমি কোথায় ___?}} (live)","options":["থাকি","থাকো","থাকেন","থাকিস"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u4-present-continuous","icon":"করছি","title":"Present Continuous","subtitle":"I am doing, she is eating","minutes":12,"goals":["Say what is happening right now","Add the {{-ছ-}} / {{-চ্ছ-}} endings","Use it for plans in the near future"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"“I'm reading”, “It's raining”, “What are you doing?”. For actions happening right now, Bangla adds a little {{ছ}} sound to the verb."},{"type":"rule","name":"Root + ছ + ending","color":"green","desc":"Add {{ছি, ছিস, ছ, ছেন, ছে}} to the root. For roots ending in a vowel ({{খা}}, {{যা}}), it becomes {{চ্ছ}}.","examples":[{"t":"আমি পড়ছি।","tr":"ami porchhi","mean":"I'm reading / studying.","hl":"পড়ছি"},{"t":"সে খাচ্ছে।","tr":"she khachchhe","mean":"He/She is eating.","hl":"খাচ্ছে"},{"t":"বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","tr":"brishti hochchhe","mean":"It's raining.","hl":"হচ্ছে"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","করা (do)","খাওয়া (eat)","যাওয়া (go)"],"rows":[["{{আমি}} / {{আমরা}}","{{করছি}} korchhi","{{খাচ্ছি}} khachchhi","{{যাচ্ছি}} jachchhi"],["{{তুই}} / {{তোরা}}","{{করছিস}} korchhis","{{খাচ্ছিস}} khachchhis","{{যাচ্ছিস}} jachchhis"],["{{তুমি}} / {{তোমরা}}","{{করছ}} korchho","{{খাচ্ছ}} khachchho","{{যাচ্ছ}} jachchho"],["{{আপনি}} / {{তিনি}}","{{করছেন}} korchhen","{{খাচ্ছেন}} khachchhen","{{যাচ্ছেন}} jachchhen"],["{{সে}} / {{তারা}}","{{করছে}} korchhe","{{খাচ্ছে}} khachchhe","{{যাচ্ছে}} jachchhe"]],"title":"Present continuous"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Same five endings as before: **-i, -is, -o, -en, -e**. Just slip {{ছ}} (chh) in front. {{করি}} → {{করছি}}."},{"type":"sentence","t":"তুমি এখন কী করছ?","tr":"tumi ekhon ki korchho?","mean":"What are you doing now?","words":[{"t":"তুমি","mean":"you"},{"t":"এখন","mean":"now"},{"t":"কী","mean":"what"},{"t":"করছ","mean":"are doing"}]},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Nadia","t":"হ্যালো, কী করছ?","tr":"hyalo, ki korchho?","mean":"Hello, what are you doing?"},{"who":"Tania","t":"টিভি দেখছি। তুমি?","tr":"tivi dekhchhi. tumi?","mean":"Watching TV. You?"},{"who":"Nadia","t":"আমি বাজারে যাচ্ছি। আসবে?","tr":"ami bajare jachchhi. ashbe?","mean":"I'm going to the market. Will you come?"},{"who":"Tania","t":"হ্যাঁ, আসছি!","tr":"hya, ashchhi!","mean":"Yes, I'm coming!"}],"title":"On the phone"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Like English, the continuous can talk about plans: {{আমি কাল ঢাকা যাচ্ছি}} = I'm going to Dhaka tomorrow."},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"{{আসছি!}} (“I'm coming!”) is what everyone shouts when Mum calls them for dinner."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["আমি পড়ছি।","সে ঘুমাচ্ছে।","বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","তুমি কী করছ?","আমরা খাচ্ছি।","আসছি!"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “I am reading”?","options":["আমি পড়ি।","আমি পড়লাম।","আমি পড়ব।","আমি পড়ছি।"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. What is happening?","say":"বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","options":["It's very hot.","The wind is blowing.","It will rain later.","It's raining."],"answer":3},{"q":"Choose: {{আপনি কী ___?}} (are doing)","options":["করছি","করছেন","করছিস","করছে"],"answer":1},{"q":"Choose: {{সে ভাত ___}} (is eating)","options":["খাচ্ছি","খাচ্ছে","খাই","খাচ্ছেন না"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What does the speaker mean?","say":"আসছি!","options":["I'm coming!","I came yesterday.","Don't come here!","Are you coming?"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{আমি কাল ঢাকা যাচ্ছি}} talks about…","options":["something from yesterday","a daily habit","a plan for tomorrow","something impossible"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u4-past","icon":"করলাম","title":"Past Simple","subtitle":"I did, she went, we ate","minutes":15,"goals":["Form the past simple with {{-ল-}}","Learn the irregular {{গেলাম}} and {{এলাম}}","Recognise the “have done” form"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"To talk about the past, Bangla adds an {{ল}} (l) sound. Think of the English “-ed”: Bangla's past marker is “-l-”."},{"type":"rule","name":"Root + ল + ending","color":"green","desc":"The endings are {{লাম, লি, লে, লেন, ল}}.","examples":[{"t":"আমি কাজটা করলাম।","tr":"ami kajta korlam","mean":"I did the work.","hl":"করলাম"},{"t":"সে আমাকে দেখল।","tr":"she amake dekhlo","mean":"He/She saw me.","hl":"দেখল"},{"t":"আপনি কখন এলেন?","tr":"apni kokhon elen?","mean":"When did you arrive?","hl":"এলেন"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","করা (do)","দেখা (see)","খাওয়া (eat)","যাওয়া (go)"],"rows":[["{{আমি}} / {{আমরা}}","{{করলাম}}","{{দেখলাম}}","{{খেলাম}}","{{গেলাম}}"],["{{তুই}} / {{তোরা}}","{{করলি}}","{{দেখলি}}","{{খেলি}}","{{গেলি}}"],["{{তুমি}} / {{তোমরা}}","{{করলে}}","{{দেখলে}}","{{খেলে}}","{{গেলে}}"],["{{আপনি}} / {{তিনি}}","{{করলেন}}","{{দেখলেন}}","{{খেলেন}}","{{গেলেন}}"],["{{সে}} / {{তারা}}","{{করল}}","{{দেখল}}","{{খেল}}","{{গেল}}"]],"title":"Past simple"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"**L for “last time”**: {{করলাম}} korlam, {{খেলাম}} khelam, {{গেলাম}} gelam. Hear the “l”? That's the past."},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Watch the changes: {{খাওয়া}} → {{খেলাম}} (a becomes e), {{যাওয়া}} → {{গেলাম}} (a new start!), {{আসা}} → {{এলাম}} (I came). In Bangladesh you'll also hear {{আসলাম}} for “I came” in casual talk."},{"type":"sentence","t":"কাল আমি একটা সিনেমা দেখলাম।","tr":"kal ami ekta shinema dekhlam","mean":"Yesterday I watched a film.","words":[{"t":"কাল","mean":"yesterday"},{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"একটা","mean":"a"},{"t":"সিনেমা","mean":"film"},{"t":"দেখলাম","mean":"watched"}]},{"type":"text","text":"Bangla also has a “have done” form, very common in daily talk. It uses {{-েছ-}}.","title":"“I have eaten”"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"আমি খেয়েছি।","tr":"ami kheyechhi","mean":"I have eaten.","hl":"খেয়েছি"},{"t":"তুমি কী করেছ?","tr":"tumi ki korechho?","mean":"What have you done?","hl":"করেছ"},{"t":"সে বাড়ি গেছে।","tr":"she bari gechhe","mean":"He/She has gone home.","hl":"গেছে"},{"t":"আমি ঢাকা থেকে এসেছি।","tr":"ami dhaka theke eshechhi","mean":"I have come from Dhaka.","hl":"এসেছি"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Remember {{খেয়েছেন?}} (Have you eaten?) from the food lesson? That's this form! Answer with {{জি, খেয়েছি}} (Yes, I have)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["আমি ভাত খেলাম।","সে বাজারে গেল।","আপনি কখন এলেন?","আমরা অনেক মজা করলাম।","আমি খেয়েছি।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “I went”?","options":["আমি যাই।","আমি যাব।","আমি গেলাম।","আমি যাচ্ছি।"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. When is this happening?","say":"সে বাজারে গেল।","options":["in the past","right now","tomorrow","every day"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which sound marks the past simple?","options":["ল (l)","ছ (chh)","ব (b)","ন (n)"],"answer":0},{"q":"Choose: {{আপনি কখন ___?}} (came)","options":["এলাম","এলি","আসব","এলেন"],"answer":3},{"q":"The past of {{খাওয়া}} with {{আমি}} is…","options":["খালাম","খেলাম","খাইলাম","খাবলাম"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আমি খেয়েছি।","options":["I will eat.","I'm eating now.","I don't eat that.","I have eaten."],"answer":3},{"q":"Choose: {{কাল আমরা অনেক মজা ___}}","options":["করি","করলাম","করব","করছি"],"answer":1,"explain":"{{কাল}} + past ending = yesterday."}]}]},{"id":"u4-future","icon":"করব","title":"Future","subtitle":"I will do, will you come?","minutes":12,"goals":["Form the future with {{-ব-}}","Make offers and plans","Use “will be” with {{হব}}"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"The future is easy: add a {{ব}} (b) sound. “B for be-going-to”!"},{"type":"rule","name":"Root + ব + ending","color":"green","desc":"The endings are {{ব, বি, বে, বেন, বে}}.","examples":[{"t":"আমি কাল আসব।","tr":"ami kal ashbo","mean":"I'll come tomorrow.","hl":"আসব"},{"t":"তুমি কী খাবে?","tr":"tumi ki khabe?","mean":"What will you eat?","hl":"খাবে"},{"t":"বৃষ্টি হবে।","tr":"brishti hobe","mean":"It will rain.","hl":"হবে"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","করা (do)","খাওয়া (eat)","যাওয়া (go)","হওয়া (be)"],"rows":[["{{আমি}} / {{আমরা}}","{{করব}} korbo","{{খাব}} khabo","{{যাব}} jabo","{{হব}} hobo"],["{{তুই}} / {{তোরা}}","{{করবি}} korbi","{{খাবি}} khabi","{{যাবি}} jabi","{{হবি}} hobi"],["{{তুমি}} / {{তোমরা}}","{{করবে}} korbe","{{খাবে}} khabe","{{যাবে}} jabe","{{হবে}} hobe"],["{{আপনি}} / {{তিনি}}","{{করবেন}} korben","{{খাবেন}} khaben","{{যাবেন}} jaben","{{হবেন}} hoben"],["{{সে}} / {{তারা}}","{{করবে}} korbe","{{খাবে}} khabe","{{যাবে}} jabe","{{হবে}} hobe"]],"title":"Future"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"{{তুমি}} and {{সে}} share the same future form: {{তুমি যাবে}} (you will go), {{সে যাবে}} (he/she will go). The pronoun tells you who."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি আগামী মাসে বাংলাদেশে যাব।","tr":"ami agami mashe bangladeshe jabo","mean":"I'll go to Bangladesh next month.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"আগামী","mean":"next"},{"t":"মাসে","mean":"in month"},{"t":"বাংলাদেশে","mean":"to Bangladesh"},{"t":"যাব","mean":"will go"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"When talking about plans, many Muslims add {{ইনশাআল্লাহ}} (“if God wills”): {{কাল দেখা হবে, ইনশাআল্লাহ}}."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"চা খাবেন?","tr":"cha khaben?","mean":"Would you like some tea?","note":"a future question = a polite offer","hl":"খাবেন"},{"t":"আপনি কি আসবেন?","tr":"apni ki ashben?","mean":"Will you come?"},{"t":"আমি ডাক্তার হব।","tr":"ami daktar hobo","mean":"I will be a doctor."},{"t":"আমরা ঈদে গ্রামে যাব।","tr":"amra ide grame jabo","mean":"We'll go to the village for Eid."}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"At Eid, millions of people leave the cities to visit their family village. Buses, trains and ferries are packed!"},{"type":"practice","text":"Say three plans for next week.","lines":["আমি কাল আসব।","আমরা ঈদে গ্রামে যাব।","তুমি কী খাবে?","চা খাবেন?","আমি ডাক্তার হব।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “I will go”?","options":["আমি গেলাম।","আমি যাচ্ছি না।","আমি যাই।","আমি যাব।"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which sound marks the future?","options":["ল (l)","ছ (chh)","ব (b)","ত (t)"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is the person doing?","say":"চা খাবেন?","options":["asking for the bill","offering tea","refusing tea","making tea now"],"answer":1},{"q":"Choose: {{আপনি কখন ___?}} (will come)","options":["আসব","আসবি","আসবেন","এলেন"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{বৃষ্টি হবে}} means…","options":["It will rain.","It's raining.","It rained.","It never rains."],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. Where will they go?","say":"আমরা ঈদে গ্রামে যাব।","options":["to the market","to Dhaka","to school","to the village"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u4-negation","icon":"না","title":"Saying No: না, নেই, নয়","subtitle":"Three kinds of “not”","minutes":15,"goals":["Put {{না}} after the verb","Use {{-নি}} for the past","Choose {{নেই}} or {{নয়}} for “isn't”"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangla has three little “no” words, each with its own job. Good news: they mostly go **after** the verb, at the very end."},{"type":"rule","name":"না after the verb","color":"red","desc":"For present, continuous and future, just add {{না}} at the end.","examples":[{"t":"আমি মাছ খাই না।","tr":"ami machh khai na","mean":"I don't eat fish.","hl":"না"},{"t":"সে আসবে না।","tr":"she ashbe na","mean":"He/She won't come.","hl":"না"},{"t":"আমি এখন পড়ছি না।","tr":"ami ekhon porchhi na","mean":"I'm not studying now.","hl":"না"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"English puts “not” in the middle. Bangla saves it for the end, like a surprise twist: “I fish eat… **not**!”"},{"type":"rule","name":"Past: add -নি","color":"orange","desc":"For “didn't” or “haven't”, take the **present** form and stick {{নি}} on the end.","examples":[{"t":"আমি খাইনি।","tr":"ami khaini","mean":"I didn't eat / I haven't eaten.","hl":"নি"},{"t":"সে আসেনি।","tr":"she asheni","mean":"He/She didn't come.","hl":"নি"},{"t":"আমরা দেখিনি।","tr":"amra dekhini","mean":"We didn't see (it).","hl":"নি"},{"t":"তুমি করোনি?","tr":"tumi koroni?","mean":"Didn't you do it?","hl":"নি"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Don't negate the {{ল}} past form in normal speech. “I didn't go” is {{আমি যাইনি}}, built from {{যাই}} + {{নি}}."},{"type":"rule","name":"নেই: “there isn't / don't have”","color":"purple","desc":"{{নেই}} is the opposite of {{আছে}}.","examples":[{"t":"আমার গাড়ি নেই।","tr":"amar gari nei","mean":"I don't have a car.","hl":"নেই"},{"t":"বাবা বাসায় নেই।","tr":"baba bashay nei","mean":"Dad isn't at home.","hl":"নেই"},{"t":"সময় নেই!","tr":"shomoy nei!","mean":"There's no time!","hl":"নেই"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"নয়: “is not” (Job 1 sentences)","color":"blue","desc":"For “X is not Y”, use {{নয়}} and its family. In everyday speech, {{না}} is also fine here.","examples":[{"t":"আমি ডাক্তার নই।","tr":"ami daktar noi","mean":"I'm not a doctor.","hl":"নই"},{"t":"উনি শিক্ষক নন।","tr":"uni shikkhok non","mean":"He/She is not a teacher.","hl":"নন"},{"t":"এটা আমার নয়।","tr":"eta amar noy","mean":"This isn't mine.","hl":"নয়"},{"t":"এটা আমার না।","tr":"eta amar na","mean":"This isn't mine. (casual)","hl":"না"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","is not"],"rows":[["{{আমি}}","{{নই}} noi"],["{{তুই}}","{{নস}} nosh"],["{{তুমি}}","{{নও}} no"],["{{আপনি}} / {{তিনি}}","{{নন}} non"],["{{সে}} / it","{{নয়}} noy"]],"title":"নয় family"},{"type":"table","head":["Yes","No"],"rows":[["{{আমি যাই।}} I go.","{{আমি যাই না।}} I don't go."],["{{আমি যাব।}} I'll go.","{{আমি যাব না।}} I won't go."],["{{আমি গেলাম।}} I went.","{{আমি যাইনি।}} I didn't go."],["{{টাকা আছে।}} There's money.","{{টাকা নেই।}} There's no money."],["{{আমি ছাত্র।}} I'm a student.","{{আমি ছাত্র নই।}} I'm not a student."]],"title":"Summary"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud, then make each sentence true for you.","lines":["আমি মাছ খাই না।","আমি খাইনি।","আমার গাড়ি নেই।","আমি ডাক্তার নই।","সে আসবে না।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “I don't eat fish”?","options":["আমি মাছ খাই না।","আমি না মাছ খাই।","আমি মাছ খাইনি।","আমি মাছ নেই।"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you say “I didn't go”?","options":["আমি যাইনি।","আমি যাব না।","আমি নেই।","আমি যাই না।"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"বাবা বাসায় নেই।","options":["Dad is at home.","Dad won't come home.","Dad isn't at home.","Dad has no house."],"answer":2},{"q":"Which word is the opposite of {{আছে}}?","options":["নয়","নি","হবে","নেই"],"answer":3},{"q":"Choose: {{আমি ডাক্তার ___}}","options":["নেই","নই","নন","নি"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What does the speaker say?","say":"সে আসবে না।","options":["He came yesterday.","He's coming now.","He didn't eat.","He won't come."],"answer":3},{"q":"Where does {{না}} usually go?","options":["before the subject","after the verb","before the verb","at the start"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u4-questions","icon":"কী?","title":"Asking Questions","subtitle":"কী, কে, কোথায়, কখন, কেন, কত and কি","minutes":15,"goals":["Learn the main question words","Keep normal word order in questions","Tell {{কী}} (what) from {{কি}} (yes/no)"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Asking questions in Bangla is easy: you **don't change the word order**. Just put the question word where the answer would be."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"কী","tr":"ki","mean":"what"},{"t":"কে","tr":"ke","mean":"who"},{"t":"কোথায়","tr":"kothay","mean":"where"},{"t":"কখন","tr":"kokhon","mean":"when"},{"t":"কেন","tr":"keno","mean":"why"},{"t":"কত","tr":"koto","mean":"how much / how many"},{"t":"কেমন","tr":"kemon","mean":"how (what like)"},{"t":"কোন","tr":"kon","mean":"which"},{"t":"কার","tr":"kar","mean":"whose"},{"t":"কয়টা","tr":"koyta","mean":"how many (things)"}],"title":"Question words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Almost every question word starts with **k-**: {{কী}}, {{কে}}, {{কোথায়}}, {{কখন}}, {{কেন}}, {{কত}}. English has the “wh-” words; Bangla has the “k-” words!"},{"type":"rule","name":"The question word sits where the answer goes","color":"green","desc":"Ask and answer with the same order.","examples":[{"t":"তুমি কী খাচ্ছ? → আমি ভাত খাচ্ছি।","tr":"tumi ki khachchho? → ami bhat khachchhi","mean":"What are you eating? → I'm eating rice.","hl":"কী"},{"t":"সে কোথায় থাকে? → সে সিলেটে থাকে।","tr":"she kothay thake? → she shilete thake","mean":"Where does he live? → He lives in Sylhet.","hl":"কোথায়"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আপনি কোথায় থাকেন?","tr":"apni kothay thaken?","mean":"Where do you live?","words":[{"t":"আপনি","mean":"you"},{"t":"কোথায়","mean":"where"},{"t":"থাকেন","mean":"live"}]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"কে এসেছে?","tr":"ke eshechhe?","mean":"Who has come?"},{"t":"ট্রেন কখন ছাড়বে?","tr":"tren kokhon charbe?","mean":"When will the train leave?"},{"t":"তুমি কেন কাঁদছ?","tr":"tumi keno kandchho?","mean":"Why are you crying?"},{"t":"তোমার বয়স কত?","tr":"tomar boyosh koto?","mean":"How old are you?"},{"t":"তুমি কোন ক্লাসে পড়ো?","tr":"tumi kon klashe poro?","mean":"Which class (year) are you in?"},{"t":"তোমরা কয় ভাই-বোন?","tr":"tomra koy bhai-bon?","mean":"How many brothers and sisters are you?"}],"title":"More questions"},{"type":"compare","items":[{"t":"কী","label":"what","desc":"With the long vowel sign ী. A real question word: {{তোমার নাম কী?}} (What is your name?)"},{"t":"কি","label":"yes/no marker","desc":"With the short sign ি. It turns a sentence into a yes/no question: {{তুমি কি চা খাবে?}} (Will you have tea?)"}],"title":"কী or কি?"},{"type":"rule","name":"Yes/no questions with কি","color":"blue","desc":"Put {{কি}} after the subject (or early in the sentence). Your voice goes up at the end.","examples":[{"t":"আপনি কি বাংলা বলেন?","tr":"apni ki bangla bolen?","mean":"Do you speak Bangla?","hl":"কি"},{"t":"এটা কি তোমার?","tr":"eta ki tomar?","mean":"Is this yours?","hl":"কি"},{"t":"তুমি আসবে?","tr":"tumi ashbe?","mean":"Will you come? (no কি, rising voice)"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"To answer yes, just repeat the verb: “{{আসবে?}}” “{{আসব।}}” (Will you come? I will.) To answer no, add {{না}}: “{{আসব না।}}”"},{"type":"practice","text":"Ask these questions aloud with a rising voice for yes/no.","lines":["তোমার নাম কী?","আপনি কোথায় থাকেন?","কয়টা বাজে?","আপনি কি বাংলা বলেন?","তুমি কেন কাঁদছ?"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Which word means “where”?","options":["কখন","কেন","কে","কোথায়"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which word means “why”?","options":["কেমন","কত","কেন","কী"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is the person asking?","say":"ট্রেন কখন ছাড়বে?","options":["When will the train leave?","Where is the train?","How much is the ticket?","Who is on the train?"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which sentence is a yes/no question?","options":["তুমি কি চা খাবে?","তুমি কী খাবে?","তুমি কোথায় যাবে?","তুমি কখন খাবে?"],"answer":0,"explain":"{{কি}} with the short sign makes a yes/no question."},{"q":"“Who has come?” is…","options":["কী এসেছে?","কেন এসেছে?","কে এসেছে?","কার এসেছে?"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"তোমার বয়স কত?","options":["What's your name?","How old are you?","Where are you from?","How much is it?"],"answer":1},{"q":"Someone asks {{যাবে?}}. How do you say “Yes, I will”?","options":["যাব।","যাবে।","যাই না।","গেলাম না।"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u4-cases","icon":"-র","title":"Case Endings: -র, -কে, -তে / -এ","subtitle":"of, to, and in: as little endings","minutes":16,"goals":["Use {{-র / -এর}} for “of” and “'s”","Use {{-কে}} for people as the object","Use {{-এ / -য় / -তে}} for “in, at, to”"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"English uses little words like “of”, “to” and “in”. Bangla glues small **endings** onto the noun instead. Three endings will take you a long way."},{"type":"rule","name":"-র / -এর = of, 's","color":"blue","desc":"After a vowel add {{-র}}; after a consonant add {{-এর}}. A few words take {{-য়ের}}.","examples":[{"t":"রাফির বই","tr":"rafir boi","mean":"Rafi's book","hl":"রাফির"},{"t":"বাবার গাড়ি","tr":"babar gari","mean":"Dad's car","hl":"বাবার"},{"t":"রহিমের বাড়ি","tr":"rohimer bari","mean":"Rahim's house","hl":"রহিমের"},{"t":"বাংলাদেশের রাজধানী","tr":"bangladesher rajdhani","mean":"the capital of Bangladesh","hl":"বাংলাদেশের"},{"t":"মায়ের রান্না","tr":"mayer ranna","mean":"Mum's cooking","hl":"মায়ের"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{-র}} sounds like the “r” in “her” or “their”. Think: Rafi-**r** book = Rafi's book."},{"type":"rule","name":"-কে = to / for a person (the object)","color":"orange","desc":"When a **person** receives the action, add {{-কে}}. Things usually take no ending.","examples":[{"t":"আমি রাফিকে চিনি।","tr":"ami rafike chini","mean":"I know Rafi.","hl":"রাফিকে"},{"t":"মাকে বলো।","tr":"make bolo","mean":"Tell Mum.","hl":"মাকে"},{"t":"আমাকে একটা কলম দাও।","tr":"amake ekta kolom dao","mean":"Give me a pen.","hl":"আমাকে"},{"t":"আমি বই পড়ি।","tr":"ami boi pori","mean":"I read books. (thing: no ending)"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","+ কে (me, you, him…)"],"rows":[["{{আমি}}","{{আমাকে}} amake"],["{{তুমি}}","{{তোমাকে}} tomake"],["{{আপনি}}","{{আপনাকে}} apnake"],["{{সে}}","{{তাকে}} take"],["{{আমরা}}","{{আমাদেরকে}} amaderke / {{আমাদের}} amader"]],"title":"Me, you, him, her"},{"type":"rule","name":"-এ / -য় / -তে = in, at, to","color":"green","desc":"After a consonant add {{-এ}}; after {{-া}} add {{-য়}}; after other vowels add {{-তে}}.","examples":[{"t":"স্কুলে","tr":"skule","mean":"at / to school","hl":"স্কুলে"},{"t":"লন্ডনে","tr":"londone","mean":"in London","hl":"লন্ডনে"},{"t":"ঢাকায়","tr":"dhakay","mean":"in / to Dhaka","hl":"ঢাকায়"},{"t":"বাড়িতে","tr":"barite","mean":"at home","hl":"বাড়িতে"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Word","of (-র)","in / at (-এ, -য়, -তে)"],"rows":[["{{ঘর}} room","{{ঘরের}}","{{ঘরে}}"],["{{ঢাকা}} Dhaka","{{ঢাকার}}","{{ঢাকায়}}"],["{{বাড়ি}} house","{{বাড়ির}}","{{বাড়িতে}}"],["{{স্কুল}} school","{{স্কুলের}}","{{স্কুলে}}"]],"title":"Side by side"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"You may also hear {{ঢাকাতে}} instead of {{ঢাকায়}}. Both are fine. And for “from”, add the after-word {{থেকে}}: {{ঢাকা থেকে}} (from Dhaka)."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি বোনকে বাবার বইটা দিলাম।","tr":"ami bonke babar boita dilam","mean":"I gave my sister Dad's book.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"বোনকে","mean":"to sister"},{"t":"বাবার","mean":"Dad's"},{"t":"বইটা","mean":"the book"},{"t":"দিলাম","mean":"gave"}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Point to each ending.","lines":["রাফির বই","মাকে বলো।","আমি ঢাকায় থাকি।","সে বাড়িতে আছে।","আমাকে একটা কলম দাও।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “Rafi's book”?","options":["রাফিকে বই","রাফিতে বই","বই রাফি","রাফির বই"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which ending marks a person as the object?","options":["-র","-কে","-তে","-টা"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Where does the speaker live?","say":"আমি ঢাকায় থাকি।","options":["in Dhaka","in London","in a village","near the school"],"answer":0},{"q":"“At home” is…","options":["বাড়ির","বাড়িকে","বাড়িতে","বাড়িটা"],"answer":2},{"q":"Choose: {{___ একটা কলম দাও।}} (me)","options":["আমার","আমি","আমাকে","আমায়ের"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"মাকে বলো।","options":["Mum's cooking.","Tell Mum.","Mum is at home.","Call Mum later."],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say “to school”?","options":["স্কুলের","স্কুলকে","স্কুলটা","স্কুলে"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u4-classifiers","icon":"টা","title":"Classifiers: টা, টি, গুলো, জন","subtitle":"Little counting words","minutes":14,"goals":["Count things with {{টা}} and people with {{জন}}","Say “the” with {{-টা}} / {{-টি}}","Make plurals with {{গুলো}} and {{-রা}}"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"In Bangla you rarely say just “two book”. You add a small **counting word**, a classifier. The same little words also work like “the”!"},{"type":"rule","name":"টা (and টি) after a number","color":"green","desc":"{{টা}} is the everyday classifier. {{টি}} is the neater, more formal version you'll see in books.","examples":[{"t":"একটা আম","tr":"ekta am","mean":"a mango / one mango","hl":"একটা"},{"t":"তিনটা কলম","tr":"tinta kolom","mean":"three pens","hl":"তিনটা"},{"t":"একটি গল্প","tr":"ekti golpo","mean":"a story (more formal)","hl":"একটি"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"টা after a noun = “the”","color":"blue","desc":"Stick {{-টা}} on the end of a noun to point to a particular one.","examples":[{"t":"বইটা","tr":"boita","mean":"the book","hl":"টা"},{"t":"ছেলেটা","tr":"chheleta","mean":"the boy","hl":"টা"},{"t":"বইটা কোথায়?","tr":"boita kothay?","mean":"Where's the book?","hl":"টা"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"{{একটা বই}} = **a** book (any book). {{বইটা}} = **the** book (that one). Same little word, different place!"},{"type":"rule","name":"গুলো and -রা = plural “the …s”","color":"orange","desc":"Add {{-গুলো}} to things (formal: {{-গুলি}}), and usually {{-রা}} to people.","examples":[{"t":"বইগুলো","tr":"boigulo","mean":"the books","hl":"গুলো"},{"t":"আমগুলো","tr":"amgulo","mean":"the mangoes","hl":"গুলো"},{"t":"ছেলেরা","tr":"chhelera","mean":"the boys","hl":"রা"},{"t":"শিক্ষকরা","tr":"shikkhokra","mean":"the teachers","hl":"রা"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"After a number, **no plural ending**: {{পাঁচটা বই}} (five books), never {{পাঁচটা বইগুলো}}."},{"type":"rule","name":"জন = counting people","color":"purple","desc":"Use {{জন}} when counting people. Ask “how many people?” with {{কয়জন}}.","examples":[{"t":"একজন লোক","tr":"ekjon lok","mean":"one person","hl":"একজন"},{"t":"দুইজন ছাত্র","tr":"duijon chhatro","mean":"two students","hl":"দুইজন"},{"t":"কয়জন আসবে?","tr":"koyjon ashbe?","mean":"How many people will come?","hl":"কয়জন"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Noun","a / one","the","the (plural)"],"rows":[["{{বই}} book","{{একটা বই}}","{{বইটা}}","{{বইগুলো}}"],["{{আম}} mango","{{একটা আম}}","{{আমটা}}","{{আমগুলো}}"],["{{ছেলে}} boy","{{একটা ছেলে}}","{{ছেলেটা}}","{{ছেলেরা}}"]]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার একটা প্রশ্ন আছে।","tr":"amar ekta proshno achhe","mean":"I have a question.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"একটা","mean":"a, one"},{"t":"প্রশ্ন","mean":"question"},{"t":"আছে","mean":"exists"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"In West Bengal you'll hear {{-টে}} and {{দুটো}}: {{তিনটে}}, {{দুটো বই}}. In Bangladesh, {{তিনটা}} and {{দুইটা}} are normal."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["একটা আম","আমটা খুব মিষ্টি।","আমগুলো কোথায়?","দুইজন ছাত্র","আমার একটা প্রশ্ন আছে।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"How do you say “the book”?","options":["একটা বই","বইগুলো","বইটা","বইজন"],"answer":2},{"q":"How do you say “five books”?","options":["পাঁচ বইগুলো","পাঁচটা বইগুলো","পাঁচজন বই","পাঁচটা বই"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which classifier do you use to count people?","options":["টা","জন","গুলো","টি"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আমগুলো","options":["the mangoes","one mango","the mango","five mangoes"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{টি}} is…","options":["a plural ending","only for people","a more formal টা","a question word"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is being asked?","say":"কয়জন আসবে?","options":["When will they come?","Who will come today?","Will you come too?","How many people will come?"],"answer":3},{"q":"“The boys” is usually…","options":["ছেলেরা","ছেলেটা","একটা ছেলে","দুইজন"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u4-adjectives","icon":"বড়","title":"Adjectives & Comparisons","subtitle":"big, bigger, biggest","minutes":14,"goals":["Use adjectives before nouns and after them","Compare with {{চেয়ে}} or {{থেকে}}","Say “the most” with {{সবচেয়ে}}"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangla adjectives are wonderfully lazy: they **never change**. No “-er”, no “-est”, no agreement. Just learn the word and use it!"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"বড়","tr":"boro","mean":"big; older"},{"t":"ছোট","tr":"chhoto","mean":"small; younger"},{"t":"ভালো","tr":"bhalo","mean":"good"},{"t":"খারাপ","tr":"kharap","mean":"bad"},{"t":"নতুন","tr":"notun","mean":"new"},{"t":"পুরানো","tr":"purano","mean":"old (things)"},{"t":"গরম","tr":"gorom","mean":"hot"},{"t":"ঠান্ডা","tr":"thanda","mean":"cold"},{"t":"সুন্দর","tr":"shundor","mean":"beautiful"},{"t":"লম্বা","tr":"lomba","mean":"tall, long"},{"t":"দামি","tr":"dami","mean":"expensive"},{"t":"সস্তা","tr":"shosta","mean":"cheap"}],"title":"Useful adjectives"},{"type":"rule","name":"Before the noun, or at the end","color":"green","desc":"Before a noun it describes it; at the end it works like “is …” (no verb needed).","examples":[{"t":"বড় বাড়ি","tr":"boro bari","mean":"a big house","hl":"বড়"},{"t":"বাড়িটা বড়।","tr":"barita boro","mean":"The house is big.","hl":"বড়"},{"t":"খুব ঠান্ডা পানি","tr":"khub thanda pani","mean":"very cold water","hl":"খুব"}]},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"খুব","tr":"khub","mean":"very"},{"t":"একটু","tr":"ektu","mean":"a little"},{"t":"অনেক","tr":"onek","mean":"a lot, much"},{"t":"আরও","tr":"aro","mean":"more, even more"}],"title":"Little helpers"},{"type":"rule","name":"Comparing: X Y-এর চেয়ে …","color":"blue","desc":"Put the thing you compare with in the {{-র}} form, then {{চেয়ে}} (than). You can also use {{থেকে}} without {{-র}}.","examples":[{"t":"রাফি সারার চেয়ে লম্বা।","tr":"rafi sharar cheye lomba","mean":"Rafi is taller than Sara.","hl":"চেয়ে"},{"t":"ঢাকা সিলেট থেকে বড়।","tr":"dhaka shilet theke boro","mean":"Dhaka is bigger than Sylhet.","hl":"থেকে"},{"t":"আজ কালকের চেয়ে গরম।","tr":"aj kalker cheye gorom","mean":"Today is hotter than yesterday.","hl":"চেয়ে"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার ভাই আমার চেয়ে লম্বা।","tr":"amar bhai amar cheye lomba","mean":"My brother is taller than me.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"ভাই","mean":"brother"},{"t":"আমার","mean":"of me"},{"t":"চেয়ে","mean":"than"},{"t":"লম্বা","mean":"tall"}],"note":"Literally: “my brother, than me, tall”. The adjective {{লম্বা}} doesn't change."},{"type":"rule","name":"The most: সবচেয়ে","color":"purple","desc":"{{সবচেয়ে}} = “than all”, so “the most”.","examples":[{"t":"ঢাকা বাংলাদেশের সবচেয়ে বড় শহর।","tr":"dhaka bangladesher shobcheye boro shohor","mean":"Dhaka is the biggest city in Bangladesh.","hl":"সবচেয়ে"},{"t":"আম আমার সবচেয়ে প্রিয় ফল।","tr":"am amar shobcheye priyo fol","mean":"Mango is my favourite fruit.","hl":"সবচেয়ে"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"English: big → bigger → biggest. Bangla: {{বড়}} → {{চেয়ে বড়}} (than … big) → {{সবচেয়ে বড়}} (than all, big). The adjective stays the same; only the helper word changes."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{বড়}} and {{ছোট}} also mean older and younger: {{বড় ভাই}} (older brother), {{ছোট বোন}} (younger sister)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Compare things around you.","lines":["বাড়িটা বড়।","রাফি সারার চেয়ে লম্বা।","আজ খুব গরম।","আম আমার সবচেয়ে প্রিয় ফল।","এটা আরও ভালো।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"{{নতুন}} means…","options":["old","new","cheap","good"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say “Rafi is taller than Sara”?","options":["রাফি সারা লম্বা।","রাফি সারার চেয়ে লম্বা।","রাফির সারা চেয়ে লম্বা।","রাফি সবচেয়ে সারা।"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which word means “the most”?","options":["চেয়ে","একটু","খুব","সবচেয়ে"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আজ খুব গরম।","options":["Today is very hot.","Today is a bit cold.","Yesterday was hot.","The water is hot."],"answer":0},{"q":"{{বড় ভাই}} is…","options":["tall man","younger brother","older brother","uncle"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. Which is bigger?","say":"ঢাকা সিলেট থেকে বড়।","options":["Sylhet","they're the same","Dhaka","it doesn't say"],"answer":2},{"q":"Do Bangla adjectives change for plural nouns?","options":["Yes, add -গুলো","Yes, add -রা","No, never","Only for people"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u4-possessives","icon":"আমার","title":"Possessives: My, Your, Their","subtitle":"আমার, তোমার, আপনার, তার…","minutes":12,"goals":["Say my, your, his, her, our, their","Ask “whose?” with {{কার}}","Say “mine”, “yours” and “I have”"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"You already know {{আমার}} (my). All the other possessives follow the same pattern: the {{-র}} ending again!"},{"type":"table","head":["Pronoun","Possessive","Say it","Meaning"],"rows":[["{{আমি}}","{{আমার}}","amar","my, mine"],["{{তুই}}","{{তোর}}","tor","your (intimate)"],["{{তুমি}}","{{তোমার}}","tomar","your (friendly)"],["{{আপনি}}","{{আপনার}}","apnar","your (polite)"],["{{সে}}","{{তার}}","tar","his, her"],["{{তিনি}} / {{উনি}}","{{তাঁর}} / {{ওনার}}","tar / onar","his, her (respectful)"],["{{আমরা}}","{{আমাদের}}","amader","our"],["{{তোমরা}}","{{তোমাদের}}","tomader","your (plural)"],["{{তারা}}","{{তাদের}}","tader","their"]],"title":"Possessive words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Singular adds {{-র}} ({{আমার}}, {{তোমার}}); plural adds {{-দের}} ({{আমাদের}}, {{তোমাদের}}). Same pattern for nouns: {{ছেলেদের স্কুল}} (the boys' school)."},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"{{তার}} means “his” **and** “her”. No gender again! The little moon sign in {{তাঁর}} (chandrabindu) shows respect, though it sounds almost the same."},{"type":"rule","name":"Same word for “my” and “mine”","color":"green","desc":"Put the possessive at the end and it means “mine / yours…”.","examples":[{"t":"এটা আমার বই।","tr":"eta amar boi","mean":"This is my book.","hl":"আমার"},{"t":"বইটা আমার।","tr":"boita amar","mean":"The book is mine.","hl":"আমার"},{"t":"ব্যাগটা কি তোমার?","tr":"byagta ki tomar?","mean":"Is the bag yours?","hl":"তোমার"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"Whose? কার?","color":"blue","desc":"{{কার}} = whose. Answer with a possessive.","examples":[{"t":"এটা কার ফোন?","tr":"eta kar fon?","mean":"Whose phone is this?","hl":"কার"},{"t":"এটা সারার।","tr":"eta sharar","mean":"It's Sara's.","hl":"সারার"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমাদের বাড়িতে একটা বিড়াল আছে।","tr":"amader barite ekta biral achhe","mean":"There's a cat in our house.","words":[{"t":"আমাদের","mean":"our"},{"t":"বাড়িতে","mean":"in house"},{"t":"একটা","mean":"a"},{"t":"বিড়াল","mean":"cat"},{"t":"আছে","mean":"is (there)"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Remember “have”: {{আমার একটা বিড়াল আছে}} = I have a cat (“my one cat exists”). With a polite “you”: {{আপনার কি গাড়ি আছে?}} (Do you have a car?)"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Teacher","t":"এই কলমটা কার?","tr":"ei kolomta kar?","mean":"Whose pen is this?"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"ওটা আমার না। মনে হয় তানিয়ার।","tr":"ota amar na. mone hoy taniar","mean":"That's not mine. I think it's Tania's."},{"who":"Tania","t":"জি, আমার। ধন্যবাদ!","tr":"ji, amar. dhonnobad!","mean":"Yes, it's mine. Thank you!"}],"title":"Whose pen?"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["এটা আমার বই।","বইটা আমার।","এটা কার ফোন?","তাদের বাড়ি ঢাকায়।","আমাদের একটা বিড়াল আছে।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"{{আমাদের}} means…","options":["my","their","your","our"],"answer":3},{"q":"How do you say “your” to a teacher?","options":["আপনার","তোর","তোমার","তার"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What is being asked?","say":"এটা কার ফোন?","options":["Whose phone is this?","Where is my phone?","Is this a new phone?","Who is on the phone?"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{তার}} can mean…","options":["only his","his or her","their","only her"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say “The book is mine”?","options":["আমি বইটা।","বইটা আমার।","আমার বইগুলো।","বইটা আমাকে।"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আমার একটা বিড়াল আছে।","options":["I like cats.","The cat is in the garden.","We don't have a cat.","I have a cat."],"answer":3},{"q":"“Their” is…","options":["তাদের","তার","তোমাদের","আমাদের"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u4-requests","icon":"দিন","title":"Polite Requests & Commands","subtitle":"Sit, come, please give…","minutes":15,"goals":["Give commands at all three levels","Make soft, polite requests","Say “don't” and “let's”"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"“Come in!”, “Sit down!”, “Could you help me?”. Commands also follow the three levels of respect. Let's learn to ask nicely, Bangla style."},{"type":"table","head":["Verb","তুই","তুমি","আপনি (spoken)","আপনি (formal)"],"rows":[["{{করা}} do","{{কর}}","{{করো}}","{{করেন}}","{{করুন}}"],["{{বসা}} sit","{{বস}}","{{বসো}}","{{বসেন}}","{{বসুন}}"],["{{দেখা}} look","{{দেখ}}","{{দেখো}}","{{দেখেন}}","{{দেখুন}}"],["{{খাওয়া}} eat","{{খা}}","{{খাও}}","{{খান}}","{{খান}}"],["{{যাওয়া}} go","{{যা}}","{{যাও}}","{{যান}}","{{যান}}"],["{{আসা}} come","{{আয়}}","{{এসো}} / {{আসো}}","{{আসেন}}","{{আসুন}}"],["{{দেওয়া}} give","{{দে}}","{{দাও}}","{{দেন}}","{{দিন}}"]],"title":"Commands at three levels"},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"In Bangladesh, everyday polite speech uses the {{-েন}} forms ({{বসেন}}, {{আসেন}}). Signs, announcements and careful speech use {{-ুন}} ({{বসুন}}, {{আসুন}}). Both are polite with {{আপনি}}."},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"The {{তুই}} command is the bare root: {{কর}}, {{বস}}, {{খা}}. Short and sharp, so only use it with very close friends!"},{"type":"rule","name":"Softening words","color":"green","desc":"Add {{একটু}} (a little) to almost any request. It works like “please”.","examples":[{"t":"একটু বসেন।","tr":"ektu boshen","mean":"Please sit down.","hl":"একটু"},{"t":"দয়া করে অপেক্ষা করুন।","tr":"doya kore opekkha korun","mean":"Please wait. (formal)","hl":"দয়া করে"},{"t":"একটু পানি দাও।","tr":"ektu pani dao","mean":"Give me some water, please.","hl":"একটু"}]},{"type":"rule","name":"The most polite: ask a future question","color":"blue","desc":"With {{আপনি}}, a future-tense question is the gentlest way to ask.","examples":[{"t":"একটু সাহায্য করবেন?","tr":"ektu shahajjo korben?","mean":"Could you help me a little?","hl":"করবেন"},{"t":"দরজাটা খুলবেন?","tr":"dorjata khulben?","mean":"Would you open the door?","hl":"খুলবেন"},{"t":"আবার আসবেন।","tr":"abar ashben","mean":"Please come again.","hl":"আসবেন"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Level","Don't go","Don't do it"],"rows":[["{{তুই}}","{{যাস না}}","{{করিস না}}"],["{{তুমি}}","{{যেও না}}","{{কোরো না}}"],["{{আপনি}}","{{যাবেন না}}","{{করবেন না}}"]],"title":"“Don't…”"},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"For “don't”, the verb changes a little: {{তুমি}} uses {{যেও না}}, {{কোরো না}}, and {{আপনি}} uses the future form + {{না}}: {{যাবেন না}}."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"চলো যাই।","tr":"cholo jai","mean":"Let's go.","hl":"চলো"},{"t":"চলেন খাই।","tr":"cholen khai","mean":"Let's eat. (polite)","hl":"চলেন"},{"t":"চলো খেলি।","tr":"cholo kheli","mean":"Let's play.","hl":"চলো"}],"title":"Let's…"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Host","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম! আসেন, ভেতরে আসেন।","tr":"assalamu alaikum! ashen, bhetore ashen","mean":"Hello! Come, come inside."},{"who":"Guest","t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম।","tr":"walaikum assalam","mean":"Hello."},{"who":"Host","t":"বসেন। চা খাবেন?","tr":"boshen. cha khaben?","mean":"Sit down. Would you like tea?"},{"who":"Guest","t":"জি, ধন্যবাদ। একটু পানিও দেবেন?","tr":"ji, dhonnobad. ektu panio deben?","mean":"Yes, thanks. Could I have some water too?"},{"who":"Host","t":"অবশ্যই। একটু অপেক্ষা করেন।","tr":"obosshoi. ektu opekkha koren","mean":"Of course. Wait just a moment."}],"title":"A guest arrives"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Guests are honoured in Bangladesh. Hosts will keep offering food: {{আরেকটু নেন!}} (Take a bit more!). It's polite to accept a little."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud at all three levels.","lines":["বস। বসো। বসেন।","একটু সাহায্য করবেন?","আবার আসবেন।","যেও না!","চলো যাই।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Which is a polite command to a guest?","options":["বস।","বসিস।","বসলাম।","বসেন।"],"answer":3},{"q":"What is the most polite way to ask for help?","options":["সাহায্য কর।","সাহায্য করো।","একটু সাহায্য করবেন?","সাহায্য করিস না।"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What does it mean?","say":"আবার আসবেন।","options":["Please come in.","Don't come here.","Please come again.","Let's go now."],"answer":2},{"q":"“Don't go” to a friend (তুমি) is…","options":["যাব না","যেও না","যাইনি","যান"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{চলো যাই}} means…","options":["I'm going.","Let's go.","Did you go?","Go away."],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is the host offering?","say":"চা খাবেন?","options":["water","rice","a chair","tea"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which softening word works like “please”?","options":["একটু","খুব","না","আরও"],"answer":0},{"q":"The formal written form of {{দেন}} (give) is…","options":["দাও","দিন","দে","দিলাম"],"answer":1}]}]}]});
LC.units.push({"id":"talk","order":5,"icon":"কথা","color":"rose","title":"Everyday Conversations","subtitle":"Real-life Bangla for the bazaar, the road, the table, the phone and festivals","lessons":[{"id":"u5-bazaar","icon":"দাম","title":"At the Bazaar","subtitle":"Buy vegetables, ask prices and bargain politely","minutes":15,"goals":["Ask how much something costs","Bargain in a friendly way","Use kilo, half-kilo and hali"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Open-air bazaars are the heart of daily shopping in Bangladesh. In many stalls the price is not fixed, so a little friendly bargaining ({{দরদাম}}) is normal. Let's go shopping!"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"বাজার","tr":"bajar","mean":"market, bazaar","example":{"t":"আমি বাজারে যাচ্ছি।","tr":"ami bajare jachchhi","mean":"I'm going to the market."}},{"t":"দাম","tr":"dam","mean":"price","example":{"t":"দাম কত?","tr":"dam koto?","mean":"What's the price?"}},{"t":"কত","tr":"koto","mean":"how much, how many"},{"t":"টাকা","tr":"taka","mean":"taka (Bangladesh's money)"},{"t":"কেজি","tr":"keji","mean":"kilo"},{"t":"কম","tr":"kom","mean":"less, lower"},{"t":"বেশি","tr":"beshi","mean":"more, too much"},{"t":"তাজা","tr":"taja","mean":"fresh"},{"t":"সবজি","tr":"shobji","mean":"vegetables"},{"t":"দোকানদার","tr":"dokandar","mean":"shopkeeper"}],"title":"Market words"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Rafi","t":"মামা, আলুর কেজি কত?","tr":"mama, alur keji koto?","mean":"Uncle, how much is a kilo of potatoes?"},{"who":"Seller","t":"পঞ্চাশ টাকা কেজি।","tr":"ponchash taka keji.","mean":"Fifty taka a kilo."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"এত দাম কেন? একটু কম রাখুন।","tr":"eto dam keno? ektu kom rakhun.","mean":"Why so expensive? Make it a bit less, please."},{"who":"Seller","t":"ঠিক আছে, পঁয়তাল্লিশ টাকা দিন।","tr":"thik achhe, poytallish taka din.","mean":"Okay, give me forty-five taka."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"চল্লিশ টাকা হলে দুই কেজি নেব।","tr":"chollish taka hole dui keji nebo.","mean":"If it's forty, I'll take two kilos."},{"who":"Seller","t":"আচ্ছা, নিয়ে যান।","tr":"achchha, niye jan.","mean":"All right, take them."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"টমেটো তাজা তো?","tr":"tometo taja to?","mean":"The tomatoes are fresh, right?"},{"who":"Seller","t":"একদম তাজা, আজকেই এসেছে।","tr":"ekdom taja, ajkei eshechhe.","mean":"Totally fresh, they came in today."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"আধা কেজি টমেটোও দিন। মোট কত হলো?","tr":"adha keji tometo-o din. mot koto holo?","mean":"Give me half a kilo of tomatoes too. How much is the total?"},{"who":"Seller","t":"একশো বিশ টাকা।","tr":"eksho bish taka.","mean":"One hundred and twenty taka."}],"title":"Buying potatoes"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Shoppers often call a male seller {{মামা}} (uncle, literally mother's brother) and a female seller {{খালা}} (aunt). It sounds warm and friendly, and people of all ages use it in cities like Dhaka."},{"type":"sentence","t":"এই মাছের দাম কত?","tr":"ei machher dam koto?","mean":"How much is this fish?","words":[{"t":"এই","mean":"this"},{"t":"মাছের","mean":"of the fish"},{"t":"দাম","mean":"price"},{"t":"কত","mean":"how much"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"একটু কম রাখুন।","tr":"ektu kom rakhun.","mean":"Please make it a bit cheaper.","words":[{"t":"একটু","mean":"a little"},{"t":"কম","mean":"less"},{"t":"রাখুন","mean":"keep (it), please"}],"note":"This is the classic polite bargaining line. Smile when you say it!"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমাকে এক হালি ডিম দিন।","tr":"amake ek hali dim din.","mean":"Give me four eggs, please.","words":[{"t":"আমাকে","mean":"to me"},{"t":"এক","mean":"one"},{"t":"হালি","mean":"set of four"},{"t":"ডিম","mean":"eggs"},{"t":"দিন","mean":"please give"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Bangla","Say","Amount"],"rows":[["{{এক কেজি}}","ek keji","1 kilo"],["{{আধা কেজি}}","adha keji","half a kilo"],["{{এক পোয়া}}","ek poa","a quarter kilo (250 g)"],["{{এক হালি}}","ek hali","four (eggs, bananas, lemons)"],["{{এক ডজন}}","ek dojon","a dozen"]],"title":"How much do you want?"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Eggs, bananas and lemons are often sold by the {{হালি}} (four), not one by one. Bargaining is common in open bazaars, but supermarkets and many shops have fixed prices ({{একদাম}}, 'one price'). Bargain with a smile; it is a friendly game, not a fight."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Greet the seller","t":"মামা, ভালো আছেন?","tr":"mama, bhalo achhen?","mean":"Uncle, how are you?","desc":"A friendly start helps you get a better price."},{"title":"Ask the price","t":"পেঁয়াজের কেজি কত?","tr":"peyajer keji koto?","mean":"How much is a kilo of onions?"},{"title":"Bargain","t":"একটু কম রাখুন।","tr":"ektu kom rakhun.","mean":"Make it a bit cheaper."},{"title":"Say how much you want","t":"দুই কেজি দিন।","tr":"dui keji din.","mean":"Give me two kilos."},{"title":"Ask the total and pay","t":"মোট কত হলো?","tr":"mot koto holo?","mean":"How much is the total?"}],"title":"Role-play: your turn to shop"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read each line aloud, then act it out with a friend as seller and buyer.","lines":["মামা, আলুর কেজি কত?","এত দাম কেন?","একটু কম রাখুন।","দুই কেজি দিন।","মোট কত হলো?"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. What is the shopper asking?","say":"আলুর কেজি কত?","options":["Where the bus stop is","The price of a kilo","If the fish is big","The seller's name"],"answer":1},{"q":"What does {{তাজা}} mean?","options":["expensive","less","a kilo","fresh"],"answer":3},{"q":"How do you politely ask for a lower price?","options":["একটু কম রাখুন।","একটু বেশি দিন।","আমি যাচ্ছি।","মোট কত হলো?"],"answer":0},{"q":"How many eggs are in {{এক হালি}}?","options":["two","six","four","twelve"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. How much does the seller want?","say":"পঞ্চাশ টাকা।","options":["15 taka","40 taka","50 taka","45 taka"],"answer":2},{"q":"A friendly word for a male shopkeeper is…","options":["মামা","আপা","খালা","নানি"],"answer":0},{"q":"Which shops usually do NOT bargain?","options":["Vegetable and fruit stalls in the open bazaar","Fish stalls","Open bazaars","Fixed-price shops and supermarkets"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u5-rickshaw","icon":"রিকশা","title":"Rickshaw & CNG","subtitle":"Agree a fare, give directions and get off","minutes":15,"goals":["Ask a driver if he will go somewhere","Agree the fare before you ride","Say left, right, straight and stop"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Cycle rickshaws and green CNG auto-rickshaws are everywhere in Bangladesh. The golden rule: **agree the fare before you get in**. Here's how."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"রিকশা","tr":"riksha","mean":"cycle rickshaw"},{"t":"সিএনজি","tr":"si-en-ji","mean":"CNG auto-rickshaw (three-wheeler)"},{"t":"ভাড়া","tr":"bhara","mean":"fare, rent","example":{"t":"ভাড়া কত?","tr":"bhara koto?","mean":"How much is the fare?"}},{"t":"যাবেন?","tr":"jaben?","mean":"will you go?"},{"t":"ডানে","tr":"dane","mean":"to the right"},{"t":"বামে","tr":"bame","mean":"to the left"},{"t":"সোজা","tr":"shoja","mean":"straight ahead"},{"t":"থামুন","tr":"thamun","mean":"stop (polite)"},{"t":"আস্তে","tr":"aste","mean":"slowly"},{"t":"মোড়","tr":"mor","mean":"corner, junction"},{"t":"জ্যাম","tr":"jyam","mean":"traffic jam"}],"title":"On the road"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Nila","t":"মামা, যাবেন?","tr":"mama, jaben?","mean":"Uncle, will you go?"},{"who":"Driver","t":"কোথায় যাবেন?","tr":"kothay jaben?","mean":"Where do you want to go?"},{"who":"Nila","t":"ধানমন্ডি সাতাশ। ভাড়া কত?","tr":"dhanmondi satash. bhara koto?","mean":"Dhanmondi 27. How much is the fare?"},{"who":"Driver","t":"আশি টাকা।","tr":"ashi taka.","mean":"Eighty taka."},{"who":"Nila","t":"আশি বেশি হয়ে যায়। ষাট টাকা দেব।","tr":"ashi beshi hoye jay. shat taka debo.","mean":"Eighty is too much. I'll pay sixty."},{"who":"Driver","t":"সত্তর দেবেন, আপা।","tr":"shottor deben, apa.","mean":"Make it seventy, sister."},{"who":"Nila","t":"ঠিক আছে, চলুন।","tr":"thik achhe, cholun.","mean":"Okay, let's go."},{"who":"Nila","t":"সামনের মোড়ে বামে যান।","tr":"shamner more bame jan.","mean":"Turn left at the next corner."},{"who":"Nila","t":"এখানে থামুন। এই নিন, সত্তর টাকা।","tr":"ekhane thamun. ei nin, shottor taka.","mean":"Stop here. Here you are, seventy taka."}],"title":"Taking a rickshaw"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Rickshaw pullers and drivers are often called {{মামা}}, and a young woman may be called {{আপা}} (elder sister). Using {{আপনি}} (polite 'you') with drivers is always respectful."},{"type":"sentence","t":"মামা, নিউ মার্কেট যাবেন?","tr":"mama, niu market jaben?","mean":"Uncle, will you go to New Market?","words":[{"t":"মামা","mean":"uncle"},{"t":"নিউ","mean":"New"},{"t":"মার্কেট","mean":"Market"},{"t":"যাবেন","mean":"will you go"}],"note":"Put the place first, then {{যাবেন?}} at the end."},{"type":"sentence","t":"একটু আস্তে চালান।","tr":"ektu aste chalan.","mean":"Please drive a little slower.","words":[{"t":"একটু","mean":"a little"},{"t":"আস্তে","mean":"slowly"},{"t":"চালান","mean":"drive (polite)"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি এখানে নামব।","tr":"ami ekhane nambo.","mean":"I'll get off here.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"এখানে","mean":"here"},{"t":"নামব","mean":"will get off"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"CNGs are named after the compressed natural gas they run on. Drivers may ask {{মিটারে, না চুক্তিতে?}} ('by meter or by agreement?'). Most rides are by agreement, so settle the price first. Ride-hailing apps are also popular in big cities."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Call the driver","t":"মামা, যাবেন?","tr":"mama, jaben?","mean":"Uncle, will you go?"},{"title":"Say where","t":"গুলশান এক।","tr":"gulshan ek.","mean":"Gulshan 1."},{"title":"Ask and agree the fare","t":"ভাড়া কত?","tr":"bhara koto?","mean":"How much?","desc":"If it is high, offer a lower number and meet in the middle."},{"title":"Guide the way","t":"সোজা যান, তারপর ডানে।","tr":"shoja jan, tarpor dane.","mean":"Go straight, then right."},{"title":"Stop and pay","t":"এখানে থামুন।","tr":"ekhane thamun.","mean":"Stop here."}],"title":"Role-play: take a ride"},{"type":"practice","text":"Say these out loud like you are sitting in a rickshaw.","lines":["মামা, যাবেন?","ভাড়া কত?","সোজা যান।","সামনের মোড়ে ডানে যান।","এখানে থামুন।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. What does the passenger want?","say":"এখানে থামুন।","options":["To go faster","To stop here","To turn left","To pay later"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{ভাড়া}} means…","options":["fare","road","left","corner"],"answer":0},{"q":"What should you do BEFORE getting into a rickshaw?","options":["Pay double","Give a tip","Agree the fare","Show your ID card"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. Which way should the driver go?","say":"বামে যান।","options":["Right","Left","Straight","Back"],"answer":1},{"q":"How do you say 'Please drive a little slower'?","options":["একটু কম রাখুন।","এখানে থামুন।","সোজা যান।","একটু আস্তে চালান।"],"answer":3},{"q":"A CNG is…","options":["a big city bus with two floors","a three-wheeled auto-rickshaw","a ferry boat","a train"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u5-restaurant","icon":"চা","title":"Restaurant & Tea Stall","subtitle":"Order tea, food and ask for the bill","minutes":15,"goals":["Order tea the way you like it","Order a simple meal","Ask for less spice and for the bill"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Tea stalls ({{চায়ের দোকান}}) are where friends meet and chat for hours. Restaurants serve rice, curry and lentils. Let's order like a local."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"চা","tr":"cha","mean":"tea"},{"t":"দুধ চা","tr":"dudh cha","mean":"milk tea"},{"t":"রং চা","tr":"rong cha","mean":"black tea (literally 'coloured tea')"},{"t":"চিনি","tr":"chini","mean":"sugar"},{"t":"পানি","tr":"pani","mean":"water"},{"t":"ভাত","tr":"bhat","mean":"cooked rice"},{"t":"ডাল","tr":"dal","mean":"lentil soup"},{"t":"মুরগি","tr":"murgi","mean":"chicken"},{"t":"ঝাল","tr":"jhal","mean":"spicy (hot)"},{"t":"বিল","tr":"bil","mean":"bill"},{"t":"লাগবে","tr":"lagbe","mean":"will be needed","example":{"t":"আর কিছু লাগবে?","tr":"ar kichhu lagbe?","mean":"Anything else?"}}],"title":"Food and drink"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Tanvir","t":"মামা, দুই কাপ চা দিন।","tr":"mama, dui kap cha din.","mean":"Uncle, two cups of tea, please."},{"who":"Tea seller","t":"দুধ চা, না রং চা?","tr":"dudh cha, na rong cha?","mean":"Milk tea or black tea?"},{"who":"Tanvir","t":"একটা দুধ চা, একটা রং চা। চিনি কম।","tr":"ekta dudh cha, ekta rong cha. chini kom.","mean":"One milk tea, one black tea. Less sugar."},{"who":"Tea seller","t":"বিস্কুট লাগবে?","tr":"biskut lagbe?","mean":"Do you want biscuits?"},{"who":"Tanvir","t":"না, শুধু চা।","tr":"na, shudhu cha.","mean":"No, just tea."}],"title":"At the tea stall"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Waiter","t":"কী খাবেন, স্যার?","tr":"ki khaben, syar?","mean":"What would you like to eat, sir?"},{"who":"Tanvir","t":"ভাত, মুরগির ঝোল আর ডাল দিন।","tr":"bhat, murgir jhol ar dal din.","mean":"Rice, chicken curry and lentils, please."},{"who":"Waiter","t":"ঝাল কেমন খাবেন?","tr":"jhal kemon khaben?","mean":"How spicy do you like it?"},{"who":"Tanvir","t":"ঝাল একটু কম দেবেন।","tr":"jhal ektu kom deben.","mean":"Please make it a little less spicy."},{"who":"Waiter","t":"আর কিছু লাগবে?","tr":"ar kichhu lagbe?","mean":"Anything else?"},{"who":"Tanvir","t":"এক বোতল পানি।","tr":"ek botol pani.","mean":"A bottle of water."},{"who":"Tanvir","t":"খাবার খুব মজা হয়েছে। বিলটা দিন।","tr":"khabar khub moja hoyechhe. bilta din.","mean":"The food was delicious. The bill, please."},{"who":"Waiter","t":"জি, এখনই আনছি।","tr":"ji, ekhoni anchhi.","mean":"Yes, bringing it right now."}],"title":"At the restaurant"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Most people in Bangladesh say {{পানি}} for water. Many Hindu families and people in West Bengal say {{জল}}. Both are correct Bangla, and everyone understands both."},{"type":"sentence","t":"ঝাল একটু কম দেবেন।","tr":"jhal ektu kom deben.","mean":"Please make it a little less spicy.","words":[{"t":"ঝাল","mean":"spice, heat"},{"t":"একটু","mean":"a little"},{"t":"কম","mean":"less"},{"t":"দেবেন","mean":"will you give (polite)"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"খাবার খুব মজা হয়েছে।","tr":"khabar khub moja hoyechhe.","mean":"The food was delicious.","words":[{"t":"খাবার","mean":"food"},{"t":"খুব","mean":"very"},{"t":"মজা","mean":"tasty"},{"t":"হয়েছে","mean":"has been"}],"note":"A lovely compliment for any cook or restaurant."},{"type":"sentence","t":"বিলটা দিন।","tr":"bilta din.","mean":"The bill, please.","words":[{"t":"বিলটা","mean":"the bill"},{"t":"দিন","mean":"please give"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Many people eat rice and curry with their right hand. Restaurants have a wash basin so you can wash your hands before and after the meal. Spoons are always fine too."},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Order tea","t":"এক কাপ দুধ চা দিন।","tr":"ek kap dudh cha din.","mean":"One cup of milk tea, please."},{"title":"Ask about sugar","t":"চিনি ছাড়া।","tr":"chini chhara.","mean":"Without sugar.","desc":"Or say {{চিনি কম}} for less sugar."},{"title":"Order a meal","t":"ভাত আর মাছ দিন।","tr":"bhat ar machh din.","mean":"Rice and fish, please."},{"title":"Control the spice","t":"ঝাল কম দেবেন।","tr":"jhal kom deben.","mean":"Not too spicy."},{"title":"Finish politely","t":"বিলটা দিন।","tr":"bilta din.","mean":"The bill, please."}],"title":"Role-play: order a meal"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Then change the words: try {{মাছ}}, {{ডিম}} or {{সবজি}} instead of {{মুরগি}}.","lines":["দুধ চা, না রং চা?","চিনি কম।","ভাত, মুরগির ঝোল আর ডাল দিন।","ঝাল একটু কম দেবেন।","খাবার খুব মজা হয়েছে।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"{{রং চা}} is…","options":["green tea","milk tea","iced coffee","black tea"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. What does the customer want?","say":"চিনি কম।","options":["Less sugar","More milk","No tea at all","A biscuit"],"answer":0},{"q":"How do you ask for the bill?","options":["পানি দিন।","কী খাবেন?","বিলটা দিন।","আর কিছু লাগবে?"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{ঝাল}} means…","options":["sweet","cold","spicy","salty and sour"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is the waiter asking?","say":"আর কিছু লাগবে?","options":["Anything else?","Are you full?","Where are you from?","Tea or coffee?"],"answer":0},{"q":"Most people in Bangladesh call water…","options":["দুধ","চিনি","ডাল","পানি"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which sentence is a compliment to the cook?","options":["ঝাল কম দেবেন।","খাবার খুব মজা হয়েছে।","শুধু চা।","বিলটা দিন।"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u5-family","icon":"পরিবার","title":"Meeting People & Family Talk","subtitle":"Introduce yourself and talk about your family","minutes":15,"goals":["Answer 'Who are you?' and 'Where are you from?'","Name family members on both sides","Talk about brothers and sisters"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"When you meet people in Bangladesh, the first questions are often about your family. Knowing family words makes you instantly part of the conversation."},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Sara","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম, আন্টি।","tr":"assalamu alaikum, anti.","mean":"Peace be upon you (hello), Auntie."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম। তুমি কে, মা?","tr":"walaikum assalam. tumi ke, ma?","mean":"And peace be upon you. Who are you, dear?"},{"who":"Sara","t":"আমি সারা। আমি লন্ডন থেকে এসেছি।","tr":"ami sara. ami london theke eshechhi.","mean":"I'm Sara. I've come from London."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"ও, তুমি রুমার মেয়ে?","tr":"o, tumi rumar meye?","mean":"Oh, are you Ruma's daughter?"},{"who":"Sara","t":"জি, আন্টি। আমার আম্মুর নাম রুমা।","tr":"ji, anti. amar ammur nam ruma.","mean":"Yes, Auntie. My mum's name is Ruma."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"অনেক বড় হয়ে গেছ! তোমরা কয় ভাইবোন?","tr":"onek boro hoye gechho! tomra koy bhaibon?","mean":"You've grown so much! How many brothers and sisters are you?"},{"who":"Sara","t":"আমরা তিন ভাইবোন। ভাইয়া আমার চেয়ে বড়।","tr":"amra tin bhaibon. bhaiya amar cheye boro.","mean":"We are three siblings. My brother is older than me."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"তুমি কোন ক্লাসে পড়ো?","tr":"tumi kon klashe poro?","mean":"Which class are you in?"},{"who":"Sara","t":"আমি ক্লাস নাইনে পড়ি।","tr":"ami klash naine pori.","mean":"I'm in class nine."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"খুব ভালো। আমাদের বাসায় এসো কিন্তু!","tr":"khub bhalo. amader bashay esho kintu!","mean":"Very good. Do come to our home!"}],"title":"Meeting a neighbour"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Elders often call a girl {{মা}} (mother) and a boy {{বাবা}} (father) as a sign of affection. It simply means 'dear'. {{জি}} is a respectful 'yes' used with elders."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"আম্মু / মা","tr":"ammu / ma","mean":"mum / mother"},{"t":"আব্বু / বাবা","tr":"abbu / baba","mean":"dad / father"},{"t":"ভাই","tr":"bhai","mean":"brother"},{"t":"বোন","tr":"bon","mean":"sister"},{"t":"ভাইয়া","tr":"bhaiya","mean":"elder brother (what you call him)"},{"t":"আপু","tr":"apu","mean":"elder sister (what you call her)"},{"t":"ভাইবোন","tr":"bhaibon","mean":"brothers and sisters, siblings"},{"t":"স্বামী","tr":"shami","mean":"husband"},{"t":"স্ত্রী","tr":"stri","mean":"wife"},{"t":"ছেলে","tr":"chhele","mean":"son, boy"},{"t":"মেয়ে","tr":"meye","mean":"daughter, girl"}],"title":"Close family"},{"type":"table","head":["","Father's side","Mother's side"],"rows":[["grandfather","{{দাদা}}","{{নানা}}"],["grandmother","{{দাদি}}","{{নানি}}"],["uncle (parent's brother)","{{চাচা}}","{{মামা}}"],["aunt (parent's sister)","{{ফুপু}}","{{খালা}}"]],"title":"Two sides of the family"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Bangla has a different word for each relative. The table shows words most Muslim families in Bangladesh use. Many Hindu families say {{ঠাকুরদা}} (grandfather), {{কাকা}} (father's brother), {{পিসি}} (father's sister) and {{মাসি}} (mother's sister), and for them {{দাদা}} means 'elder brother'. Listen to how each family speaks and copy them."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার এক ভাই আর এক বোন আছে।","tr":"amar ek bhai ar ek bon achhe.","mean":"I have one brother and one sister.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my / I have"},{"t":"এক","mean":"one"},{"t":"ভাই","mean":"brother"},{"t":"আর","mean":"and"},{"t":"এক","mean":"one"},{"t":"বোন","mean":"sister"},{"t":"আছে","mean":"there is"}],"note":"Bangla says 'my brother is' ({{আমার … আছে}}) instead of 'I have'."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আপনি কী করেন?","tr":"apni ki koren?","mean":"What do you do (for work)?","words":[{"t":"আপনি","mean":"you (polite)"},{"t":"কী","mean":"what"},{"t":"করেন","mean":"do"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার বাবা একজন শিক্ষক।","tr":"amar baba ekjon shikkhok.","mean":"My father is a teacher.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"বাবা","mean":"father"},{"t":"একজন","mean":"a (person)"},{"t":"শিক্ষক","mean":"teacher"}]},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Greet","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম। / নমস্কার।","tr":"assalamu alaikum. / nomoshkar.","mean":"Hello (Muslim / Hindu greeting).","desc":"Use the greeting the other person uses."},{"title":"Say your name","t":"আমার নাম …","tr":"amar nam …","mean":"My name is …"},{"title":"Say where you're from","t":"আমি … থেকে এসেছি।","tr":"ami … theke eshechhi.","mean":"I've come from …"},{"title":"Talk about family","t":"আমরা দুই ভাইবোন।","tr":"amra dui bhaibon.","mean":"We are two siblings."},{"title":"Ask back","t":"আপনার বাসা কোথায়?","tr":"apnar basha kothay?","mean":"Where is your home?"}],"title":"Role-play: meet a new auntie"},{"type":"practice","text":"Say these about YOUR family. Change the numbers and words to make them true.","lines":["আমার নাম সারা।","আমি লন্ডন থেকে এসেছি।","আমরা তিন ভাইবোন।","আমার এক ভাই আর এক বোন আছে।","আমার বাবা একজন শিক্ষক।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Your mother's sister is your…","options":["খালা","চাচা","ফুপু","দাদি"],"answer":0},{"q":"Your father's father (in most Muslim families) is your…","options":["নানা","মামা","দাদা","ভাইয়া"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is the person saying?","say":"আমি লন্ডন থেকে এসেছি।","options":["I live in Dhaka","I've come from London","My name is London","I'm going to London"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{ভাইবোন}} means…","options":["cousins","parents","neighbours","siblings"],"answer":3},{"q":"A respectful 'yes' to an elder is…","options":["না","জি","কী","ও"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is being asked?","say":"আপনি কী করেন?","options":["How old are you?","Where is your home?","What is your name?","What do you do?"],"answer":3},{"q":"When an auntie calls a girl {{মা}}, she means…","options":["dear","mother","come here","go away"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u5-phone","icon":"ফোন","title":"Phone Calls","subtitle":"Answer, ask who's calling and end a call","minutes":12,"goals":["Start and end a phone call","Say you can't hear well","Promise to call back"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Phone calls are fast and you can't see faces, so short fixed phrases help a lot. Learn these and you'll sound natural on the phone."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"হ্যালো","tr":"hyalo","mean":"hello (on the phone)"},{"t":"কে বলছেন?","tr":"ke bolchhen?","mean":"who's speaking?"},{"t":"ফোন দেওয়া","tr":"phon deoa","mean":"to call (literally 'give a phone')","example":{"t":"পরে ফোন দেব।","tr":"pore phon debo.","mean":"I'll call later."}},{"t":"ব্যস্ত","tr":"byasto","mean":"busy"},{"t":"নেটওয়ার্ক","tr":"netoyark","mean":"network, signal"},{"t":"শুনতে পাচ্ছি না","tr":"shunte pachchhi na","mean":"I can't hear"},{"t":"জোরে","tr":"jore","mean":"loudly"},{"t":"আবার","tr":"abar","mean":"again"},{"t":"মেসেজ","tr":"mesej","mean":"message, text"},{"t":"রাখি","tr":"rakhi","mean":"I'll hang up now (literally 'I'll put it down')"}],"title":"Phone words"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Rafi","t":"হ্যালো, আসসালামু আলাইকুম। কে বলছেন?","tr":"hyalo, assalamu alaikum. ke bolchhen?","mean":"Hello, peace be upon you. Who's speaking?"},{"who":"Mitu","t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম। রাফি ভাই, আমি মিতু।","tr":"walaikum assalam. rafi bhai, ami mitu.","mean":"And peace be upon you. Rafi bhai, it's Mitu."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"ও মিতু! কেমন আছ?","tr":"o mitu! kemon achho?","mean":"Oh, Mitu! How are you?"},{"who":"Mitu","t":"ভালো আছি। আপনি কি এখন ব্যস্ত?","tr":"bhalo achhi. apni ki ekhon byasto?","mean":"I'm fine. Are you busy right now?"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"একটু ব্যস্ত। কী বলবে, তাড়াতাড়ি বলো।","tr":"ektu byasto. ki bolbe, taratari bolo.","mean":"A bit busy. Tell me quickly what it is."},{"who":"Mitu","t":"কালকের মিটিং সকাল দশটায়।","tr":"kalker miting shokal doshtay.","mean":"Tomorrow's meeting is at ten in the morning."},{"who":"Rafi","t":"তোমার কথা কেটে কেটে আসছে। আবার বলো তো?","tr":"tomar kotha kete kete ashchhe. abar bolo to?","mean":"Your voice is breaking up. Can you say it again?"},{"who":"Mitu","t":"কাল সকাল দশটায় মিটিং!","tr":"kal shokal doshtay miting!","mean":"Meeting tomorrow at ten a.m.!"},{"who":"Rafi","t":"আচ্ছা, বুঝেছি। পরে কথা হবে। রাখি।","tr":"achchha, bujhechhi. pore kotha hobe. rakhi.","mean":"Okay, got it. Talk later. Bye for now."},{"who":"Mitu","t":"আচ্ছা, আল্লাহ হাফেজ।","tr":"achchha, allah hafej.","mean":"Okay, goodbye."}],"title":"A quick call"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Notice the respect levels: Mitu is younger, so she calls Rafi {{ভাই}} and uses {{আপনি}}. Rafi is older, so he uses friendly {{তুমি}} with her. People often add {{ভাই}} or {{আপা}} after a name to show respect."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{আল্লাহ হাফেজ}} or {{খোদা হাফেজ}} ('may God protect you') is a common Muslim goodbye. A neutral goodbye anyone can use is {{ভালো থাকবেন}} ('stay well'). On the phone, {{আচ্ছা, রাখি}} is the everyday way to say 'I'm hanging up now'."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি আপনার কথা শুনতে পাচ্ছি না।","tr":"ami apnar kotha shunte pachchhi na.","mean":"I can't hear you.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"আপনার","mean":"your"},{"t":"কথা","mean":"words, voice"},{"t":"শুনতে","mean":"to hear"},{"t":"পাচ্ছি","mean":"am able"},{"t":"না","mean":"not"}],"note":"{{না}} (not) comes at the end of the sentence."},{"type":"sentence","t":"একটু জোরে বলুন।","tr":"ektu jore bolun.","mean":"Please speak a bit louder.","words":[{"t":"একটু","mean":"a little"},{"t":"জোরে","mean":"loudly"},{"t":"বলুন","mean":"speak (polite)"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি দশ মিনিট পরে ফোন দেব।","tr":"ami dosh minit pore phon debo.","mean":"I'll call you in ten minutes.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"দশ","mean":"ten"},{"t":"মিনিট","mean":"minutes"},{"t":"পরে","mean":"after"},{"t":"ফোন","mean":"phone"},{"t":"দেব","mean":"will give"}]},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Answer","t":"হ্যালো, কে বলছেন?","tr":"hyalo, ke bolchhen?","mean":"Hello, who's speaking?"},{"title":"Say who you are","t":"আমি নাবিল বলছি।","tr":"ami nabil bolchhi.","mean":"This is Nabil speaking."},{"title":"Bad line?","t":"একটু জোরে বলুন।","tr":"ektu jore bolun.","mean":"Please speak a bit louder."},{"title":"Busy?","t":"পরে ফোন দেব।","tr":"pore phon debo.","mean":"I'll call later."},{"title":"End the call","t":"আচ্ছা, রাখি। ভালো থাকবেন।","tr":"achchha, rakhi. bhalo thakben.","mean":"Okay, bye for now. Take care."}],"title":"Role-play: a phone call"},{"type":"practice","text":"Hold your phone and practise these lines aloud.","lines":["হ্যালো, কে বলছেন?","আমি সারা বলছি।","আমি আপনার কথা শুনতে পাচ্ছি না।","একটু জোরে বলুন।","আচ্ছা, রাখি।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. What does the caller ask?","say":"কে বলছেন?","options":["Are you busy?","Where are you?","Who's speaking?","What time is it?"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{ব্যস্ত}} means…","options":["free","late","busy","tired"],"answer":2},{"q":"How do you say 'Please speak a bit louder'?","options":["একটু জোরে বলুন।","একটু আস্তে চালান।","আবার আসবেন।","পরে ফোন দেব।"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does the person mean?","say":"আচ্ছা, রাখি।","options":["Please call me back later","I'm on my way","Wait a minute","I'm hanging up now"],"answer":3},{"q":"Which goodbye can anyone use, whatever their religion?","options":["আল্লাহ হাফেজ","ভালো থাকবেন","আসসালামু আলাইকুম","ঈদ মোবারক"],"answer":1},{"q":"In {{আমি শুনতে পাচ্ছি না}}, where is the word for 'not'?","options":["At the end","At the start","After {{আমি}}","It is not there"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u5-doctor","icon":"ডাক্তার","title":"At the Doctor","subtitle":"Describe how you feel and understand the advice","minutes":15,"goals":["Say what hurts","Say how long you've been ill","Understand how to take medicine"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Feeling unwell abroad is stressful. A few clear phrases help the doctor understand you quickly. In Bangla, you say a body part 'is hurting'."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"ডাক্তার","tr":"daktar","mean":"doctor"},{"t":"জ্বর","tr":"jor","mean":"fever"},{"t":"ব্যথা","tr":"byatha","mean":"pain, ache"},{"t":"মাথাব্যথা","tr":"mathabyatha","mean":"headache"},{"t":"কাশি","tr":"kashi","mean":"cough"},{"t":"সর্দি","tr":"shordi","mean":"a cold, runny nose"},{"t":"ওষুধ","tr":"oshudh","mean":"medicine"},{"t":"ফার্মেসি","tr":"pharmeshi","mean":"pharmacy"},{"t":"হাসপাতাল","tr":"haspatal","mean":"hospital"},{"t":"অসুস্থ","tr":"oshustho","mean":"ill, unwell"}],"title":"Health words"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Doctor","t":"বসুন। কী সমস্যা?","tr":"boshun. ki shomossha?","mean":"Please sit down. What's the problem?"},{"who":"Karim","t":"দুই দিন ধরে আমার জ্বর আর মাথাব্যথা।","tr":"dui din dhore amar jor ar mathabyatha.","mean":"I've had a fever and headache for two days."},{"who":"Doctor","t":"কাশি আছে?","tr":"kashi achhe?","mean":"Do you have a cough?"},{"who":"Karim","t":"হ্যাঁ, একটু কাশি আছে। গলাও ব্যথা।","tr":"hya, ektu kashi achhe. golao byatha.","mean":"Yes, a little cough. My throat hurts too."},{"who":"Doctor","t":"জ্বর কত ছিল?","tr":"jor koto chhilo?","mean":"How high was the fever?"},{"who":"Karim","t":"কাল রাতে একশো দুই।","tr":"kal rate eksho dui.","mean":"A hundred and two last night."},{"who":"Doctor","t":"ভয়ের কিছু নেই। মনে হচ্ছে ভাইরাল জ্বর।","tr":"bhoyer kichhu nei. mone hochchhe bhairal jor.","mean":"Nothing to worry about. It seems to be a viral fever."},{"who":"Doctor","t":"এই ওষুধটা দিনে তিনবার খাবেন, খাওয়ার পরে। আর বেশি করে পানি খাবেন।","tr":"ei oshudhta dine tinbar khaben, khaoar pore. ar beshi kore pani khaben.","mean":"Take this medicine three times a day, after meals. And drink plenty of water."},{"who":"Karim","t":"ধন্যবাদ, ডাক্তার সাহেব।","tr":"dhonnobad, daktar shaheb.","mean":"Thank you, doctor."}],"title":"At the clinic"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"In Bangla you 'eat' medicine and you 'eat' water: {{ওষুধ খাওয়া}}, {{পানি খাওয়া}}. The same verb {{খাওয়া}} covers eat, drink and take medicine."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Body temperature in Bangladesh is usually given in Fahrenheit, so {{একশো দুই}} (102) means a fairly high fever. The national emergency number in Bangladesh is **999**."},{"type":"table","head":["Body part","Bangla","It hurts!"],"rows":[["head","{{মাথা}}","{{আমার মাথা ব্যথা করছে।}}"],["stomach","{{পেট}}","{{আমার পেট ব্যথা করছে।}}"],["throat","{{গলা}}","{{আমার গলা ব্যথা করছে।}}"],["tooth","{{দাঁত}}","{{আমার দাঁত ব্যথা করছে।}}"],["leg / foot","{{পা}}","{{আমার পা ব্যথা করছে।}}"]],"title":"Where does it hurt?"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার মাথা ব্যথা করছে।","tr":"amar matha byatha korchhe.","mean":"I have a headache.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"মাথা","mean":"head"},{"t":"ব্যথা","mean":"pain"},{"t":"করছে","mean":"is doing"}],"note":"Swap {{মাথা}} for any body part from the table."},{"type":"sentence","t":"দুই দিন ধরে জ্বর।","tr":"dui din dhore jor.","mean":"I've had a fever for two days.","words":[{"t":"দুই","mean":"two"},{"t":"দিন","mean":"days"},{"t":"ধরে","mean":"for (time)"},{"t":"জ্বর","mean":"fever"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"দিনে তিনবার খাবেন।","tr":"dine tinbar khaben.","mean":"Take it three times a day.","words":[{"t":"দিনে","mean":"per day"},{"t":"তিনবার","mean":"three times"},{"t":"খাবেন","mean":"you will take (polite)"}]},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Say what is wrong","t":"আমার পেট ব্যথা করছে।","tr":"amar pet byatha korchhe.","mean":"My stomach hurts."},{"title":"Say since when","t":"গতকাল থেকে।","tr":"gotokal theke.","mean":"Since yesterday."},{"title":"Mention other symptoms","t":"জ্বরও আছে।","tr":"joro achhe.","mean":"I have a fever too."},{"title":"Check the dose","t":"কয়বার খাব?","tr":"koybar khabo?","mean":"How many times should I take it?"},{"title":"Thank the doctor","t":"অনেক ধন্যবাদ।","tr":"onek dhonnobad.","mean":"Thank you very much."}],"title":"Role-play: see the doctor"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Then point to your head, stomach and throat and say the matching line.","lines":["আমার মাথা ব্যথা করছে।","আমার পেট ব্যথা করছে।","দুই দিন ধরে জ্বর।","কাশি আছে।","কয়বার খাব?"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. What is wrong?","say":"আমার মাথা ব্যথা করছে।","options":["A stomach ache","A cough","A headache","A toothache"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{ওষুধ}} means…","options":["doctor","medicine","hospital","fever"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. How often should you take the medicine?","say":"দিনে তিনবার খাবেন।","options":["Once a day","Twice a day","Every hour","Three times a day"],"answer":3},{"q":"How do you say 'I've had a fever for two days'?","options":["দিনে দুইবার খাবেন।","দুই দিন ধরে জ্বর।","দুই কেজি দিন।","আমার পা ব্যথা।"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which verb do you use for taking medicine?","options":["দেওয়া (give)","করা (do)","যাওয়া (go)","খাওয়া (eat)"],"answer":3},{"q":"What is the emergency number in Bangladesh?","options":["999","911","112","100"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{গলা}} is the…","options":["stomach","leg","throat","tooth"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u5-directions","icon":"পথ","title":"Asking Directions","subtitle":"Find places using landmarks","minutes":12,"goals":["Politely stop someone to ask","Understand left, right, near, far","Follow directions with landmarks"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"In Bangladesh, people give directions using landmarks (a mosque, a school, a big shop) more than street names. Learn the position words and you'll find your way."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"কোথায়","tr":"kothay","mean":"where"},{"t":"কাছে","tr":"kachhe","mean":"near"},{"t":"দূরে","tr":"dure","mean":"far"},{"t":"পাশে","tr":"pashe","mean":"next to, beside"},{"t":"সামনে","tr":"shamne","mean":"in front of, ahead"},{"t":"পেছনে","tr":"pechhone","mean":"behind"},{"t":"উল্টো দিকে","tr":"ulto dike","mean":"opposite"},{"t":"রাস্তা","tr":"rasta","mean":"road, way"},{"t":"হেঁটে","tr":"hente","mean":"on foot"},{"t":"দিক","tr":"dik","mean":"direction, side"}],"title":"Position words"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Ayesha","t":"ভাই, একটু শুনবেন?","tr":"bhai, ektu shunben?","mean":"Excuse me, brother?"},{"who":"Man","t":"জি, বলুন।","tr":"ji, bolun.","mean":"Yes, go ahead."},{"who":"Ayesha","t":"এখানে কাছে কোনো ফার্মেসি আছে?","tr":"ekhane kachhe kono pharmeshi achhe?","mean":"Is there a pharmacy near here?"},{"who":"Man","t":"হ্যাঁ, আছে। সোজা গিয়ে প্রথম মোড়ে ডানে যান।","tr":"hya, achhe. shoja giye prothom more dane jan.","mean":"Yes. Go straight and turn right at the first corner."},{"who":"Ayesha","t":"কতদূর?","tr":"kotodur?","mean":"How far is it?"},{"who":"Man","t":"বেশি দূর না, হেঁটে পাঁচ মিনিট।","tr":"beshi dur na, hente panch minit.","mean":"Not far, five minutes on foot."},{"who":"Ayesha","t":"মসজিদের পাশে?","tr":"moshjider pashe?","mean":"Next to the mosque?"},{"who":"Man","t":"না, মসজিদের উল্টো দিকে। একটা স্কুলের সামনে।","tr":"na, moshjider ulto dike. ekta skuler shamne.","mean":"No, opposite the mosque. In front of a school."},{"who":"Ayesha","t":"বুঝেছি। অনেক ধন্যবাদ।","tr":"bujhechhi. onek dhonnobad.","mean":"Got it. Thanks a lot."}],"title":"Finding a pharmacy"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{ভাই, একটু শুনবেন?}} ('Brother, will you listen a moment?') is a natural, polite way to stop someone. For a woman, say {{আপা}}. People are usually very happy to help, and it is normal to check with a second person on the way."},{"type":"sentence","t":"বাসস্ট্যান্ডটা কোন দিকে?","tr":"bashstyandta kon dike?","mean":"Which way is the bus stand?","words":[{"t":"বাসস্ট্যান্ডটা","mean":"the bus stand"},{"t":"কোন","mean":"which"},{"t":"দিকে","mean":"direction"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"সোজা গিয়ে ডানে যান।","tr":"shoja giye dane jan.","mean":"Go straight, then turn right.","words":[{"t":"সোজা","mean":"straight"},{"t":"গিয়ে","mean":"having gone"},{"t":"ডানে","mean":"to the right"},{"t":"যান","mean":"go (polite)"}],"note":"{{গিয়ে}} links two actions: 'go straight and then…'"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি রাস্তা হারিয়ে ফেলেছি।","tr":"ami rasta hariye phelechhi.","mean":"I've lost my way.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"রাস্তা","mean":"way, road"},{"t":"হারিয়ে","mean":"losing"},{"t":"ফেলেছি","mean":"have ended up"}]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"মসজিদের পাশে","tr":"moshjider pashe","mean":"next to the mosque"},{"t":"স্কুলের সামনে","tr":"skuler shamne","mean":"in front of the school"},{"t":"ব্যাংকের পেছনে","tr":"byanker pechhone","mean":"behind the bank"},{"t":"মন্দিরের উল্টো দিকে","tr":"mondirer ulto dike","mean":"opposite the temple","note":"Landmark + {{-এর}} ('of') + position word."}],"title":"Landmark + position"},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Stop someone politely","t":"আপা, একটু শুনবেন?","tr":"apa, ektu shunben?","mean":"Excuse me, sister?"},{"title":"Ask for a place","t":"হাসপাতালটা কোথায়?","tr":"haspatalta kothay?","mean":"Where is the hospital?"},{"title":"Ask the distance","t":"কতদূর?","tr":"kotodur?","mean":"How far?"},{"title":"Repeat to check","t":"সোজা, তারপর বামে?","tr":"shoja, tarpor bame?","mean":"Straight, then left?","desc":"Repeating the directions back is polite and avoids mistakes."},{"title":"Thank them","t":"অনেক ধন্যবাদ।","tr":"onek dhonnobad.","mean":"Thanks a lot."}],"title":"Role-play: find the hospital"},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud. Then describe the way from your home to a shop near you.","lines":["ভাই, একটু শুনবেন?","এখানে কাছে কোনো ফার্মেসি আছে?","সোজা গিয়ে ডানে যান।","মসজিদের উল্টো দিকে।","আমি রাস্তা হারিয়ে ফেলেছি।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. Where is the place?","say":"মসজিদের উল্টো দিকে।","options":["Behind the big school","Next to the bank","Opposite the mosque","Far away"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{কাছে}} means…","options":["near","far","behind","left"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. How far is it?","say":"হেঁটে পাঁচ মিনিট।","options":["Two hours by bus from here","Ten minutes by car","Very far","Five minutes on foot"],"answer":3},{"q":"How do you say 'I've lost my way'?","options":["আমি এখানে নামব।","আমি রাস্তা হারিয়ে ফেলেছি।","রাস্তা কোথায়?","আমি বাসায় যাচ্ছি।"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{স্কুলের সামনে}} means…","options":["in front of the school","behind the school","inside the school","far away from the school"],"answer":0},{"q":"Bangladeshis usually give directions using…","options":["map numbers","street names only","landmarks","compass points"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u5-festivals","icon":"উৎসব","title":"Festival Greetings","subtitle":"Wish people well on Eid, New Year, Puja and more","minutes":15,"goals":["Greet people correctly at each festival","Know the main festivals of Bangladesh","Respond to festival wishes"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangladesh celebrates many festivals, and people of all faiths share in the joy. A popular saying goes: {{ধর্ম যার যার, উৎসব সবার}}, 'Religion is each person's own, festivals belong to everyone.'"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Nabil","t":"ঈদ মোবারক, চাচা!","tr":"id mobarok, chacha!","mean":"Eid Mubarak, Uncle!"},{"who":"Uncle","t":"ঈদ মোবারক! এসো, এসো। ভেতরে এসো।","tr":"id mobarok! esho, esho. bhetore esho.","mean":"Eid Mubarak! Come in, come in."},{"who":"Nabil","t":"চাচি কোথায়?","tr":"chachi kothay?","mean":"Where is Auntie?"},{"who":"Uncle","t":"রান্নাঘরে। আগে সেমাই খাও।","tr":"rannaghore. age shemai khao.","mean":"In the kitchen. Have some semai first."},{"who":"Nabil","t":"জি, চাচা। খুব মজা হয়েছে!","tr":"ji, chacha. khub moja hoyechhe!","mean":"Yes, Uncle. It's delicious!"},{"who":"Uncle","t":"এই নাও, তোমার ঈদের সালামি।","tr":"ei nao, tomar ider salami.","mean":"Here you are, your Eid salami."},{"who":"Nabil","t":"অনেক ধন্যবাদ, চাচা!","tr":"onek dhonnobad, chacha!","mean":"Thank you so much, Uncle!"}],"title":"Eid morning"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Priya","t":"শুভ নববর্ষ, নাবিল!","tr":"shubho nobobarsho, nabil!","mean":"Happy New Year, Nabil!"},{"who":"Nabil","t":"শুভ নববর্ষ, প্রিয়া! লাল-সাদা শাড়িতে তোমাকে খুব সুন্দর লাগছে।","tr":"shubho nobobarsho, priya! lal-shada sharite tomake khub shundor lagchhe.","mean":"Happy New Year, Priya! You look lovely in the red-and-white sari."},{"who":"Priya","t":"ধন্যবাদ! পূজায় আমাদের বাসায় আসবে কিন্তু।","tr":"dhonnobad! pujay amader bashay ashbe kintu.","mean":"Thanks! Do come to our home for the Puja."},{"who":"Nabil","t":"অবশ্যই আসব! আগে থেকেই পূজার শুভেচ্ছা।","tr":"obosshoi ashbo! age thekei pujar shubhechchha.","mean":"Of course I'll come! Puja greetings in advance."}],"title":"Pohela Boishakh"},{"type":"table","head":["Festival","When","Greeting"],"rows":[["Eid ul-Fitr ({{ঈদুল ফিতর}})","end of Ramadan","{{ঈদ মোবারক}}"],["Eid ul-Adha ({{ঈদুল আজহা}})","about two months later, at Hajj time","{{ঈদ মোবারক}}"],["Bangla New Year ({{পহেলা বৈশাখ}})","14 April","{{শুভ নববর্ষ}}"],["Durga Puja ({{দুর্গাপূজা}})","autumn","{{শারদীয় শুভেচ্ছা}} / {{পূজার শুভেচ্ছা}}"],["Christmas ({{বড়দিন}})","25 December","{{শুভ বড়দিন}}"],["Buddha Purnima ({{বুদ্ধ পূর্ণিমা}})","full moon of Boishakh (April or May)","{{শুভ বুদ্ধ পূর্ণিমা}}"],["Victory Day ({{বিজয় দিবস}})","16 December","{{বিজয় দিবসের শুভেচ্ছা}}"]],"title":"Festivals and greetings"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"ঈদ মোবারক","tr":"id mobarok","mean":"Eid Mubarak (blessed Eid)"},{"t":"শুভ নববর্ষ","tr":"shubho nobobarsho","mean":"Happy New Year"},{"t":"পূজার শুভেচ্ছা","tr":"pujar shubhechchha","mean":"Puja greetings"},{"t":"শুভ বিজয়া","tr":"shubho bijoya","mean":"greeting after Durga Puja ends (Bijoya Dashami)"},{"t":"শুভ বড়দিন","tr":"shubho borodin","mean":"Merry Christmas (literally 'happy big day')"},{"t":"শুভেচ্ছা","tr":"shubhechchha","mean":"good wishes"},{"t":"সালামি","tr":"salami","mean":"Eid money given by elders to younger people"},{"t":"সেমাই","tr":"shemai","mean":"sweet vermicelli made for Eid"},{"t":"উৎসব","tr":"utshob","mean":"festival"}],"title":"Festival words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"On Eid, younger people greet elders respectfully, and elders give them {{সালামি}} (gift money). On Eid ul-Adha, families share meat from the sacrifice with relatives, neighbours and people in need."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"During Durga Puja, beautifully decorated {{মণ্ডপ}} (pavilions) are built for the goddess Durga, and visitors of all backgrounds come to see them. After the last day, Hindu friends greet each other with {{শুভ বিজয়া}}."},{"type":"tip","kind":"warn","text":"Not every special day is a 'happy' one. On 21 February ({{শহিদ দিবস}}, Martyrs' Day) people remember those who died for the Bangla language. It is a day of respect, so do not say 'happy'. You will learn more in Unit 6."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আপনাকে ঈদের শুভেচ্ছা।","tr":"apnake ider shubhechchha.","mean":"Eid greetings to you.","words":[{"t":"আপনাকে","mean":"to you (polite)"},{"t":"ঈদের","mean":"of Eid"},{"t":"শুভেচ্ছা","mean":"good wishes"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"সবাইকে শুভ নববর্ষ।","tr":"shobaike shubho nobobarsho.","mean":"Happy New Year, everyone.","words":[{"t":"সবাইকে","mean":"to everyone"},{"t":"শুভ","mean":"happy, auspicious"},{"t":"নববর্ষ","mean":"new year"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আপনার পরিবারকে পূজার শুভেচ্ছা জানাই।","tr":"apnar poribarke pujar shubhechchha janai.","mean":"I send Puja greetings to your family.","words":[{"t":"আপনার","mean":"your"},{"t":"পরিবারকে","mean":"to the family"},{"t":"পূজার","mean":"of the Puja"},{"t":"শুভেচ্ছা","mean":"good wishes"},{"t":"জানাই","mean":"I convey"}]},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Greet a Muslim neighbour on Eid","t":"ঈদ মোবারক!","tr":"id mobarok!","mean":"Eid Mubarak!","desc":"The reply is the same: {{ঈদ মোবারক}}."},{"title":"Greet anyone on 14 April","t":"শুভ নববর্ষ!","tr":"shubho nobobarsho!","mean":"Happy New Year!"},{"title":"Greet a Hindu friend at Durga Puja","t":"শারদীয় শুভেচ্ছা!","tr":"sharodio shubhechchha!","mean":"Autumn festival greetings!"},{"title":"Greet a Christian friend on 25 December","t":"শুভ বড়দিন!","tr":"shubho borodin!","mean":"Merry Christmas!"},{"title":"Send wishes to the family","t":"পরিবারের সবাইকে শুভেচ্ছা।","tr":"poribarer shobaike shubhechchha.","mean":"Best wishes to all the family."}],"title":"Role-play: a year of greetings"},{"type":"practice","text":"Say each greeting with a big smile.","lines":["ঈদ মোবারক!","শুভ নববর্ষ!","পূজার শুভেচ্ছা!","শুভ বড়দিন!","আপনাকে ঈদের শুভেচ্ছা।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. Which festival is it?","say":"শুভ নববর্ষ!","options":["Eid ul-Adha (Qurbani Eid)","Bangla New Year","Christmas","Durga Puja"],"answer":1},{"q":"Someone says {{ঈদ মোবারক}} to you. You reply…","options":["শুভ বিজয়া","শুভ বড়দিন","নমস্কার","ঈদ মোবারক"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{সালামি}} is…","options":["a sweet dish","Eid gift money from elders","a prayer mat","a new dress"],"answer":1},{"q":"What is Christmas called in Bangla?","options":["নববর্ষ","বৈশাখ","পূজা","বড়দিন"],"answer":3},{"q":"Pohela Boishakh in Bangladesh falls on…","options":["14 April","1 January","16 December","21 February"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. When would you hear this greeting?","say":"শুভ বিজয়া!","options":["On Eid morning","At Christmas","After Durga Puja ends","On a birthday"],"answer":2},{"q":"On 21 February (Martyrs' Day) you should…","options":["say 'Eid Mubarak'","give salami","show respect, not say 'happy'","say 'Happy New Year'"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{ধর্ম যার যার, উৎসব সবার}} means…","options":["Festivals belong to everyone","Only elders can celebrate festivals","Festivals are for children","Religion is a festival"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u5-visiting","icon":"বাড়ি","title":"Visiting Someone's Home","subtitle":"Be a polite guest and enjoy Bangladeshi hospitality","minutes":15,"goals":["Greet your hosts and give a small gift","Accept food and drink politely","Take your leave in a natural way"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Hospitality ({{আপ্যায়ন}}) is a big part of Bangladeshi culture. Guests are treated with great care, and you will almost certainly be offered food. Here's how to be a perfect guest."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"মেহমান / অতিথি","tr":"mehman / otithi","mean":"guest"},{"t":"বাসা","tr":"basha","mean":"home, flat (in town)"},{"t":"বাড়ি","tr":"bari","mean":"house, family home"},{"t":"ভেতরে","tr":"bhetore","mean":"inside"},{"t":"বসুন","tr":"boshun","mean":"please sit"},{"t":"জুতা","tr":"juta","mean":"shoes"},{"t":"মিষ্টি","tr":"mishti","mean":"sweets"},{"t":"শরবত","tr":"shorbot","mean":"cold sweet drink"},{"t":"আপ্যায়ন","tr":"appayon","mean":"hospitality"},{"t":"উঠি","tr":"uthi","mean":"I'll get going (literally 'I'll get up')"}],"title":"Guest words"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Auntie","t":"আরে, এসো এসো! ভেতরে এসো।","tr":"are, esho esho! bhetore esho.","mean":"Oh, come in, come in! Come inside."},{"who":"Sami","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম, খালা। আপনার জন্য একটু মিষ্টি এনেছি।","tr":"assalamu alaikum, khala. apnar jonno ektu mishti enechhi.","mean":"Hello, Auntie. I brought a few sweets for you."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"এসবের কী দরকার ছিল! বসো, বসো।","tr":"eshober ki dorkar chhilo! bosho, bosho.","mean":"There was no need for that! Sit, sit."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"কী খাবে? চা, না শরবত?","tr":"ki khabe? cha, na shorbot?","mean":"What will you have? Tea or a cold drink?"},{"who":"Sami","t":"কিছু লাগবে না, খালা।","tr":"kichhu lagbe na, khala.","mean":"I don't need anything, Auntie."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"তা কি হয়? একটু কিছু খেতেই হবে।","tr":"ta ki hoy? ektu kichhu khetei hobe.","mean":"How can that be? You must have a little something."},{"who":"Sami","t":"আচ্ছা, তাহলে এক কাপ চা।","tr":"achchha, tahole ek kap cha.","mean":"Okay then, a cup of tea."},{"who":"Sami","t":"আজ তাহলে উঠি, খালা। খুব ভালো লাগল।","tr":"aj tahole uthi, khala. khub bhalo laglo.","mean":"I'd better get going now, Auntie. It was really lovely."},{"who":"Auntie","t":"আবার এসো কিন্তু! আম্মুকে সালাম দিও।","tr":"abar esho kintu! ammuke salam dio.","mean":"Do come again! Give my regards to your mum."}],"title":"A visit to Auntie's"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"It is polite to bring a small gift such as sweets ({{মিষ্টি}}) or fruit. Hosts often refuse a gift at first ('There was no need!'), and guests often refuse food at first. The host insists, and then you accept. This little dance is part of good manners."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Take off your shoes if you see shoes by the door. Greet elders first, and offer and receive things with your right hand. {{আজ তাহলে উঠি}} is the polite, natural way to say you are leaving."},{"type":"sentence","t":"জুতা কি খুলতে হবে?","tr":"juta ki khulte hobe?","mean":"Should I take my shoes off?","words":[{"t":"জুতা","mean":"shoes"},{"t":"কি","mean":"(question word)"},{"t":"খুলতে","mean":"to take off"},{"t":"হবে","mean":"will be needed"}],"note":"{{কি}} (short i) turns a sentence into a yes/no question. {{কী}} (long ি) means 'what'."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আপনার বাসাটা খুব সুন্দর।","tr":"apnar bashata khub shundor.","mean":"Your home is very beautiful.","words":[{"t":"আপনার","mean":"your"},{"t":"বাসাটা","mean":"the home"},{"t":"খুব","mean":"very"},{"t":"সুন্দর","mean":"beautiful"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আজ তাহলে উঠি।","tr":"aj tahole uthi.","mean":"I'd better get going now.","words":[{"t":"আজ","mean":"today"},{"t":"তাহলে","mean":"then, so"},{"t":"উঠি","mean":"I get up"}]},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Greet the host","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম। / নমস্কার।","tr":"assalamu alaikum. / nomoshkar.","mean":"Hello."},{"title":"Give your gift","t":"আপনার জন্য একটু মিষ্টি।","tr":"apnar jonno ektu mishti.","mean":"A few sweets for you."},{"title":"Compliment the home","t":"আপনার বাসাটা খুব সুন্দর।","tr":"apnar bashata khub shundor.","mean":"Your home is lovely."},{"title":"Accept food politely","t":"আচ্ছা, একটু দিন।","tr":"achchha, ektu din.","mean":"Okay, just a little, please."},{"title":"Take your leave","t":"আজ তাহলে উঠি। খুব ভালো লাগল।","tr":"aj tahole uthi. khub bhalo laglo.","mean":"I'll get going now. It was lovely."}],"title":"Role-play: be the guest"},{"type":"practice","text":"Practise being a polite guest. Read aloud.","lines":["আপনার জন্য একটু মিষ্টি এনেছি।","কিছু লাগবে না।","আচ্ছা, তাহলে এক কাপ চা।","আপনার বাসাটা খুব সুন্দর।","আজ তাহলে উঠি।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. What is the host saying?","say":"ভেতরে এসো।","options":["Sit outside","Go home","Take a gift","Come inside"],"answer":3},{"q":"What is a good small gift to bring?","options":["Nothing at all","Sweets or fruit","A bag of rice","Money in an envelope"],"answer":1},{"q":"The host insists you eat. What usually happens?","options":["You accept a little","You leave at once","You keep refusing","You ask for the menu"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{আজ তাহলে উঠি}} means…","options":["Please stand up","Wake up today","I'd better get going now","Let's eat now"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{মেহমান}} means…","options":["host","guest","neighbour","sweets"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is the guest asking?","say":"জুতা কি খুলতে হবে?","options":["Where is the kitchen, please?","Can I sit here?","Is this tea sweet?","Should I take off my shoes?"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u5-weather","icon":"বৃষ্টি","title":"Small Talk & the Weather","subtitle":"Chat about heat, rain and the six seasons","minutes":15,"goals":["Make small talk about the weather","Talk about rain and the monsoon","Name the six seasons of Bengal"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Weather is the easiest small talk anywhere. In Bangladesh, the heat and the monsoon rain ({{বর্ষা}}) are favourite topics. Rain is also loved in songs, poems and food."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"আবহাওয়া","tr":"abhaoa","mean":"weather"},{"t":"গরম","tr":"gorom","mean":"hot, heat"},{"t":"ঠান্ডা","tr":"thanda","mean":"cold, cool"},{"t":"শীত","tr":"shit","mean":"winter, cold weather"},{"t":"বৃষ্টি","tr":"brishti","mean":"rain"},{"t":"মেঘ","tr":"megh","mean":"cloud"},{"t":"রোদ","tr":"rod","mean":"sunshine"},{"t":"ঝড়","tr":"jhor","mean":"storm"},{"t":"ছাতা","tr":"chhata","mean":"umbrella"},{"t":"বর্ষা","tr":"borsha","mean":"monsoon, rainy season"},{"t":"ভ্যাপসা","tr":"bhyapsha","mean":"muggy, humid"}],"title":"Weather words"},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Rina","t":"আজ কী গরম, তাই না?","tr":"aj ki gorom, tai na?","mean":"Isn't it hot today?"},{"who":"Jamal","t":"হ্যাঁ, খুব ভ্যাপসা গরম। ঘামে ভিজে গেছি।","tr":"hya, khub bhyapsha gorom. ghame bhije gechhi.","mean":"Yes, really muggy. I'm soaked with sweat."},{"who":"Rina","t":"আকাশে মেঘ করেছে। মনে হয় বৃষ্টি আসবে।","tr":"akashe megh korechhe. mone hoy brishti ashbe.","mean":"It's clouded over. I think rain is coming."},{"who":"Jamal","t":"এলে ভালোই হবে, একটু ঠান্ডা হবে।","tr":"ele bhaloi hobe, ektu thanda hobe.","mean":"That would be good. It'll cool down a bit."},{"who":"Rina","t":"ছাতা এনেছেন?","tr":"chhata enechhen?","mean":"Did you bring an umbrella?"},{"who":"Jamal","t":"না, ভুলে গেছি!","tr":"na, bhule gechhi!","mean":"No, I forgot!"},{"who":"Rina","t":"বর্ষাকালে সবসময় ছাতা সাথে রাখবেন।","tr":"borshakale shobshomoy chhata shathe rakhben.","mean":"In the rainy season, always keep an umbrella with you."},{"who":"Jamal","t":"ঠিক বলেছেন। বৃষ্টির দিনে খিচুড়ি খেতে মন চায়।","tr":"thik bolechhen. brishtir dine khichuri khete mon chay.","mean":"You're right. On rainy days I feel like eating khichuri."},{"who":"Rina","t":"আমারও! সাথে ইলিশ মাছ ভাজা।","tr":"amaro! shathe ilish machh bhaja.","mean":"Me too! With fried hilsa fish."}],"title":"A cloudy afternoon"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Khichuri (rice and lentils cooked together) with fried hilsa ({{ইলিশ}}) is the classic rainy-day meal in Bangladesh. Many families make it as soon as the monsoon rain starts."},{"type":"table","head":["Season","Bangla","Bangla months","Roughly"],"rows":[["summer","{{গ্রীষ্ম}}","{{বৈশাখ}}, {{জ্যৈষ্ঠ}}","mid-April to mid-June"],["rainy season","{{বর্ষা}}","{{আষাঢ়}}, {{শ্রাবণ}}","mid-June to mid-August"],["early autumn","{{শরৎ}}","{{ভাদ্র}}, {{আশ্বিন}}","mid-August to mid-October"],["late autumn","{{হেমন্ত}}","{{কার্তিক}}, {{অগ্রহায়ণ}}","mid-October to mid-December"],["winter","{{শীত}}","{{পৌষ}}, {{মাঘ}}","mid-December to mid-February"],["spring","{{বসন্ত}}","{{ফাল্গুন}}, {{চৈত্র}}","mid-February to mid-April"]],"title":"The six seasons (ছয় ঋতু)"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"Bengal is called the land of six seasons ({{ষড়ঋতুর দেশ}}). Each season lasts two Bangla months. In spring and early summer, sudden evening storms called {{কালবৈশাখী}} can blow in with strong wind and rain."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আজ খুব গরম পড়েছে।","tr":"aj khub gorom porechhe.","mean":"It's very hot today.","words":[{"t":"আজ","mean":"today"},{"t":"খুব","mean":"very"},{"t":"গরম","mean":"heat"},{"t":"পড়েছে","mean":"has fallen"}],"note":"Heat and cold 'fall' in Bangla: {{গরম পড়েছে}}, {{শীত পড়েছে}}."},{"type":"sentence","t":"বাইরে ঝুম বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","tr":"baire jhum brishti hochchhe.","mean":"It's pouring outside.","words":[{"t":"বাইরে","mean":"outside"},{"t":"ঝুম","mean":"heavy, pouring"},{"t":"বৃষ্টি","mean":"rain"},{"t":"হচ্ছে","mean":"is happening"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"কাল কি বৃষ্টি হবে?","tr":"kal ki brishti hobe?","mean":"Will it rain tomorrow?","words":[{"t":"কাল","mean":"tomorrow"},{"t":"কি","mean":"(question word)"},{"t":"বৃষ্টি","mean":"rain"},{"t":"হবে","mean":"will happen"}],"note":"{{কাল}} can mean 'tomorrow' or 'yesterday'. The verb tells you which!"},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Open with the weather","t":"আজ কী গরম, তাই না?","tr":"aj ki gorom, tai na?","mean":"Isn't it hot today?","desc":"{{তাই না?}} works like 'isn't it?' and invites the other person to agree."},{"title":"Agree","t":"হ্যাঁ, খুব গরম।","tr":"hya, khub gorom.","mean":"Yes, very hot."},{"title":"Talk about rain","t":"মনে হয় বৃষ্টি আসবে।","tr":"mone hoy brishti ashbe.","mean":"I think it's going to rain."},{"title":"Share a favourite","t":"আমার বর্ষাকাল খুব ভালো লাগে।","tr":"amar borshakal khub bhalo lage.","mean":"I really like the rainy season."},{"title":"Ask a question back","t":"আপনার কোন ঋতু ভালো লাগে?","tr":"apnar kon ritu bhalo lage?","mean":"Which season do you like?"}],"title":"Role-play: weather chat"},{"type":"practice","text":"Look out of the window and describe today's weather using these lines.","lines":["আজ কী গরম, তাই না?","আকাশে মেঘ করেছে।","বাইরে ঝুম বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","আজ খুব শীত পড়েছে।","কাল কি বৃষ্টি হবে?"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. What is the weather like?","say":"বাইরে ঝুম বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","options":["It's very sunny","It's pouring with rain","It's freezing cold","There's no wind"],"answer":1},{"q":"{{ছাতা}} means…","options":["cloud","storm","sunshine","umbrella"],"answer":3},{"q":"The monsoon season in Bangla is…","options":["বর্ষা","শীত","বসন্ত","শরৎ"],"answer":0},{"q":"What is a classic rainy-day meal?","options":["Ice cream with cold mango juice","Cold salad","Khichuri with fried hilsa","Plain bread"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What is the speaker saying?","say":"আজ কী গরম, তাই না?","options":["Is it cold today?","Will it rain today?","Isn't it hot today?","Is it windy?"],"answer":2},{"q":"How many seasons does Bengal traditionally have?","options":["six","four","two","twelve"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{শীত}} is…","options":["summer","spring","the rainy season","winter"],"answer":3}]}]}]});
LC.units.push({"id":"read","order":6,"icon":"পড়া","color":"violet","title":"Reading & Culture","subtitle":"Graded stories, the national anthem, proverbs and the culture behind the language","lessons":[{"id":"u6-story-cat","icon":"গল্প","title":"Story 1: Mina's Cat","subtitle":"A short, easy story to read line by line","minutes":12,"goals":["Read a short story sentence by sentence","Learn words for a home and a pet","Answer questions about the story"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Time to read a real story! Read each line, tap the words you don't know, then read the whole story again without help. This one is **Level 1**: short sentences, everyday words."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"বিড়াল","tr":"biral","mean":"cat"},{"t":"ছোট","tr":"chhoto","mean":"small"},{"t":"সাদা","tr":"shada","mean":"white"},{"t":"নরম","tr":"norom","mean":"soft"},{"t":"দুধ","tr":"dudh","mean":"milk"},{"t":"খোঁজা","tr":"khonja","mean":"to search"},{"t":"আলমারি","tr":"almari","mean":"cupboard, wardrobe"},{"t":"ঘুমানো","tr":"ghumano","mean":"to sleep"},{"t":"দুষ্টু","tr":"dushtu","mean":"naughty"}],"title":"Story words"},{"type":"sentence","t":"মিনার একটা ছোট বিড়াল আছে।","tr":"minar ekta chhoto biral achhe.","mean":"Mina has a small cat.","words":[{"t":"মিনার","mean":"Mina's"},{"t":"একটা","mean":"a, one"},{"t":"ছোট","mean":"small"},{"t":"বিড়াল","mean":"cat"},{"t":"আছে","mean":"there is"}],"title":"মিনার বিড়াল (Mina's Cat)"},{"type":"sentence","t":"বিড়ালটার নাম মিনি।","tr":"biraltar nam mini.","mean":"The cat's name is Mini.","words":[{"t":"বিড়ালটার","mean":"the cat's"},{"t":"নাম","mean":"name"},{"t":"মিনি","mean":"Mini"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"মিনি সাদা আর খুব নরম।","tr":"mini shada ar khub norom.","mean":"Mini is white and very soft.","words":[{"t":"মিনি","mean":"Mini"},{"t":"সাদা","mean":"white"},{"t":"আর","mean":"and"},{"t":"খুব","mean":"very"},{"t":"নরম","mean":"soft"}],"note":"Bangla often has no word for 'is': {{মিনি সাদা}} = 'Mini (is) white'."},{"type":"sentence","t":"প্রতিদিন সকালে মিনি দুধ খায়।","tr":"protidin shokale mini dudh khay.","mean":"Every morning Mini drinks milk.","words":[{"t":"প্রতিদিন","mean":"every day"},{"t":"সকালে","mean":"in the morning"},{"t":"মিনি","mean":"Mini"},{"t":"দুধ","mean":"milk"},{"t":"খায়","mean":"eats, drinks"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"একদিন মিনিকে কোথাও পাওয়া গেল না।","tr":"ekdin minike kothao paoa gelo na.","mean":"One day Mini was nowhere to be found.","words":[{"t":"একদিন","mean":"one day"},{"t":"মিনিকে","mean":"Mini"},{"t":"কোথাও","mean":"anywhere"},{"t":"পাওয়া","mean":"found"},{"t":"গেল","mean":"could be"},{"t":"না","mean":"not"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"মিনা সারা বাড়ি খুঁজল।","tr":"mina shara bari khunjlo.","mean":"Mina searched the whole house.","words":[{"t":"মিনা","mean":"Mina"},{"t":"সারা","mean":"whole"},{"t":"বাড়ি","mean":"house"},{"t":"খুঁজল","mean":"searched"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"শেষে দেখা গেল, মিনি আলমারির ভেতরে ঘুমাচ্ছে!","tr":"sheshe dekha gelo, mini almarir bhetore ghumachchhe!","mean":"In the end she found Mini sleeping inside the cupboard!","words":[{"t":"শেষে","mean":"in the end"},{"t":"দেখা","mean":"seen"},{"t":"গেল","mean":"it was"},{"t":"মিনি","mean":"Mini"},{"t":"আলমারির","mean":"of the cupboard"},{"t":"ভেতরে","mean":"inside"},{"t":"ঘুমাচ্ছে","mean":"is sleeping"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"মিনা হেসে বলল, \"দুষ্টু বিড়াল!\"","tr":"mina heshe bollo, \"dushtu biral!\"","mean":"Mina laughed and said, \"Naughty cat!\"","words":[{"t":"মিনা","mean":"Mina"},{"t":"হেসে","mean":"laughing"},{"t":"বলল","mean":"said"},{"t":"দুষ্টু","mean":"naughty"},{"t":"বিড়াল","mean":"cat"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Look at {{-এর}} / {{-র}}: it means 'of' or 's. {{মিনা}} → {{মিনার}} (Mina's), {{আলমারি}} → {{আলমারির}} (of the cupboard)."},{"type":"practice","text":"Now read the whole story aloud without looking at the meanings.","lines":["মিনার একটা ছোট বিড়াল আছে।","বিড়ালটার নাম মিনি।","মিনি সাদা আর খুব নরম।","প্রতিদিন সকালে মিনি দুধ খায়।","একদিন মিনিকে কোথাও পাওয়া গেল না।","মিনা সারা বাড়ি খুঁজল।","শেষে দেখা গেল, মিনি আলমারির ভেতরে ঘুমাচ্ছে!","মিনা হেসে বলল, \"দুষ্টু বিড়াল!\""]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Did you understand?","items":[{"q":"What colour is Mini?","options":["white","black","brown","grey and black"],"answer":0},{"q":"What does Mini have every morning?","options":["rice","fish","water and bread","milk"],"answer":3},{"q":"Where did Mina find Mini?","options":["Under the bed","In the cupboard","On the roof","In the garden by the pond"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. Which line from the story is this?","say":"মিনা সারা বাড়ি খুঁজল।","options":["Mina searched the whole house.","Mini drinks milk every morning.","Mina has a cat.","The cat is soft."],"answer":0},{"q":"{{দুষ্টু}} means…","options":["sleepy","hungry","naughty","beautiful"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{মিনার}} means…","options":["to Mina","Mina's","Mina is","with Mina"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u6-story-rain","icon":"বর্ষা","title":"Story 2: On a Rainy Day","subtitle":"A monsoon morning that turns out well","minutes":15,"goals":["Read a longer story in the past tense","Learn monsoon words","Notice respectful verb forms"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a **Level 2** story. The sentences are a little longer and tell what happened in the past. It is set in {{আষাঢ়}}, the first month of the rainy season."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"আষাঢ়","tr":"asharh","mean":"Asharh (first month of the rainy season)"},{"t":"রওনা দেওয়া","tr":"rowna deoa","mean":"to set off"},{"t":"হাঁটুসমান","tr":"hantushoman","mean":"knee-deep"},{"t":"হঠাৎ","tr":"hothat","mean":"suddenly"},{"t":"বাতাস","tr":"batash","mean":"wind, breeze"},{"t":"উল্টে দেওয়া","tr":"ulte deoa","mean":"to turn over, flip"},{"t":"ভিজে যাওয়া","tr":"bhije jaoa","mean":"to get wet"},{"t":"বন্ধ","tr":"bondho","mean":"closed"},{"t":"খিচুড়ি","tr":"khichuri","mean":"rice and lentils cooked together"}],"title":"Story words"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আষাঢ় মাসের এক সকালে খুব বৃষ্টি হচ্ছিল।","tr":"asharh masher ek shokale khub brishti hochchhilo.","mean":"One morning in the month of Asharh, it was raining hard.","words":[{"t":"আষাঢ়","mean":"Asharh"},{"t":"মাসের","mean":"of the month"},{"t":"এক","mean":"one"},{"t":"সকালে","mean":"morning"},{"t":"খুব","mean":"very, hard"},{"t":"বৃষ্টি","mean":"rain"},{"t":"হচ্ছিল","mean":"was happening"}],"title":"বৃষ্টির দিনে (On a Rainy Day)"},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাফি ছাতা নিয়ে স্কুলে রওনা দিল।","tr":"rafi chhata niye skule rowna dilo.","mean":"Rafi set off for school with an umbrella.","words":[{"t":"রাফি","mean":"Rafi"},{"t":"ছাতা","mean":"umbrella"},{"t":"নিয়ে","mean":"taking"},{"t":"স্কুলে","mean":"to school"},{"t":"রওনা","mean":"departure"},{"t":"দিল","mean":"gave (= set off)"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাস্তায় হাঁটুসমান পানি জমে গিয়েছিল।","tr":"rastay hantushoman pani jome giyechhilo.","mean":"Knee-deep water had collected on the road.","words":[{"t":"রাস্তায়","mean":"on the road"},{"t":"হাঁটুসমান","mean":"knee-deep"},{"t":"পানি","mean":"water"},{"t":"জমে","mean":"collecting"},{"t":"গিয়েছিল","mean":"had become"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"হঠাৎ জোরে বাতাস এসে ছাতাটা উল্টে দিল।","tr":"hothat jore batash eshe chhatata ulte dilo.","mean":"Suddenly a strong wind came and turned the umbrella inside out.","words":[{"t":"হঠাৎ","mean":"suddenly"},{"t":"জোরে","mean":"strongly"},{"t":"বাতাস","mean":"wind"},{"t":"এসে","mean":"coming"},{"t":"ছাতাটা","mean":"the umbrella"},{"t":"উল্টে","mean":"flipping"},{"t":"দিল","mean":"did"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাফি পুরো ভিজে গেল, কিন্তু সে হাসতে লাগল।","tr":"rafi puro bhije gelo, kintu she hashte laglo.","mean":"Rafi got soaking wet, but he started to laugh.","words":[{"t":"রাফি","mean":"Rafi"},{"t":"পুরো","mean":"completely"},{"t":"ভিজে","mean":"wet"},{"t":"গেল","mean":"got"},{"t":"কিন্তু","mean":"but"},{"t":"সে","mean":"he"},{"t":"হাসতে","mean":"to laugh"},{"t":"লাগল","mean":"began"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"স্কুলে গিয়ে সে দেখল, আজ স্কুল বন্ধ!","tr":"skule giye she dekhlo, aj skul bondho!","mean":"When he got to school, he saw that school was closed today!","words":[{"t":"স্কুলে","mean":"to school"},{"t":"গিয়ে","mean":"having gone"},{"t":"সে","mean":"he"},{"t":"দেখল","mean":"saw"},{"t":"আজ","mean":"today"},{"t":"স্কুল","mean":"school"},{"t":"বন্ধ","mean":"closed"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"বাসায় ফেরার পর মা তাকে গরম খিচুড়ি খেতে দিলেন।","tr":"bashay pherar por ma take gorom khichuri khete dilen.","mean":"After he got home, Mum gave him hot khichuri to eat.","words":[{"t":"বাসায়","mean":"home"},{"t":"ফেরার","mean":"returning"},{"t":"পর","mean":"after"},{"t":"মা","mean":"Mum"},{"t":"তাকে","mean":"him"},{"t":"গরম","mean":"hot"},{"t":"খিচুড়ি","mean":"khichuri"},{"t":"খেতে","mean":"to eat"},{"t":"দিলেন","mean":"gave (respectful)"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাফি ভাবল, বৃষ্টির দিনটা আসলে খারাপ না।","tr":"rafi bhablo, brishtir dinta ashole kharap na.","mean":"Rafi thought the rainy day wasn't so bad after all.","words":[{"t":"রাফি","mean":"Rafi"},{"t":"ভাবল","mean":"thought"},{"t":"বৃষ্টির","mean":"rainy"},{"t":"দিনটা","mean":"the day"},{"t":"আসলে","mean":"actually"},{"t":"খারাপ","mean":"bad"},{"t":"না","mean":"not"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Verbs change to show respect. For Rafi (a child) the story says {{দিল}} and {{দেখল}}. For his mother it says {{দিলেন}}: the {{-এন}} ending is the respectful form, used for elders and anyone you call {{আপনি}}."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"During the monsoon, heavy rain can quickly flood city streets. Children love jumping in the puddles, while parents worry about the mud! Khichuri on a rainy day is a favourite family tradition."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the story aloud. Try to read it twice: once slowly, once at a natural speed.","lines":["আষাঢ় মাসের এক সকালে খুব বৃষ্টি হচ্ছিল।","রাফি ছাতা নিয়ে স্কুলে রওনা দিল।","রাস্তায় হাঁটুসমান পানি জমে গিয়েছিল।","হঠাৎ জোরে বাতাস এসে ছাতাটা উল্টে দিল।","রাফি পুরো ভিজে গেল, কিন্তু সে হাসতে লাগল।","স্কুলে গিয়ে সে দেখল, আজ স্কুল বন্ধ!","বাসায় ফেরার পর মা তাকে গরম খিচুড়ি খেতে দিলেন।","রাফি ভাবল, বৃষ্টির দিনটা আসলে খারাপ না।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Did you understand?","items":[{"q":"Where was Rafi going?","options":["To the bazaar","To the river","To his grandmother's house","To school"],"answer":3},{"q":"What happened to his umbrella?","options":["He lost it","The wind flipped it","He gave it away","It was too small for him"],"answer":1},{"q":"How did Rafi feel when he got wet?","options":["He cried","He got angry","He went straight home sad","He laughed"],"answer":3},{"q":"Why didn't Rafi have class?","options":["School was closed","He was ill","He was late","His teacher went away on holiday"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What did Mum give Rafi?","say":"মা তাকে গরম খিচুড়ি খেতে দিলেন।","options":["Cold milk","A new umbrella","Hot khichuri","Sweets"],"answer":2},{"q":"Why does the story say {{দিলেন}} for Mum, not {{দিল}}?","options":["Because it's the future","Because there are two mums","To show respect","It's a spelling mistake"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{হঠাৎ}} means…","options":["suddenly","slowly","every day","after school"],"answer":0}]}]},{"id":"u6-story-village","icon":"গ্রাম","title":"Story 3: A Day at Nanu's","subtitle":"A London boy visits his grandmother's village","minutes":15,"goals":["Read a Level 3 story with dialogue","Learn village and cousin words","Feel confident to speak Bangla with family"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"This **Level 3** story is about Ayan, a boy from London who visits his grandmother's village in Bangladesh for the first time. Maybe you know that feeling!"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"নানুবাড়ি","tr":"nanubari","mean":"maternal grandmother's home"},{"t":"গ্রাম","tr":"gram","mean":"village"},{"t":"ধানক্ষেত","tr":"dhankhet","mean":"rice field"},{"t":"ভোর","tr":"bhor","mean":"dawn"},{"t":"মোরগ","tr":"morog","mean":"rooster"},{"t":"পিঠা","tr":"pitha","mean":"traditional rice cake"},{"t":"লজ্জা","tr":"lojja","mean":"shyness, embarrassment"},{"t":"ভুল","tr":"bhul","mean":"mistake"},{"t":"নৌকা","tr":"nouka","mean":"boat"},{"t":"মামাতো ভাই","tr":"mamato bhai","mean":"cousin (mother's brother's son)"}],"title":"Story words"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আয়ান লন্ডন থেকে প্রথমবার নানুবাড়িতে এসেছে।","tr":"ayan london theke prothombar nanubarite eshechhe.","mean":"Ayan has come from London to his grandmother's home for the first time.","words":[{"t":"আয়ান","mean":"Ayan"},{"t":"লন্ডন","mean":"London"},{"t":"থেকে","mean":"from"},{"t":"প্রথমবার","mean":"for the first time"},{"t":"নানুবাড়িতে","mean":"to Nanu's home"},{"t":"এসেছে","mean":"has come"}],"title":"নানুবাড়িতে একদিন (A Day at Nanu's)"},{"type":"sentence","t":"গ্রামটা সিলেটে, চারপাশে সবুজ ধানক্ষেত।","tr":"gramta shilete, charpashe shobuj dhankhet.","mean":"The village is in Sylhet, with green rice fields all around.","words":[{"t":"গ্রামটা","mean":"the village"},{"t":"সিলেটে","mean":"in Sylhet"},{"t":"চারপাশে","mean":"all around"},{"t":"সবুজ","mean":"green"},{"t":"ধানক্ষেত","mean":"rice fields"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"ভোরে মোরগের ডাকে তার ঘুম ভাঙল।","tr":"bhore moroger dake tar ghum bhanglo.","mean":"At dawn, the rooster's crow woke him up.","words":[{"t":"ভোরে","mean":"at dawn"},{"t":"মোরগের","mean":"the rooster's"},{"t":"ডাকে","mean":"by the call"},{"t":"তার","mean":"his"},{"t":"ঘুম","mean":"sleep"},{"t":"ভাঙল","mean":"broke"}],"note":"Bangla says 'his sleep broke' ({{ঘুম ভাঙল}}) for 'he woke up'."},{"type":"sentence","t":"নানু তাকে শীতের সকালে গরম ভাপা পিঠা খাওয়ালেন।","tr":"nanu take shiter shokale gorom bhapa pitha khaoalen.","mean":"On the winter morning, Nanu fed him warm steamed rice cakes.","words":[{"t":"নানু","mean":"Nanu (Grandma)"},{"t":"তাকে","mean":"him"},{"t":"শীতের","mean":"winter's"},{"t":"সকালে","mean":"in the morning"},{"t":"গরম","mean":"warm"},{"t":"ভাপা","mean":"steamed"},{"t":"পিঠা","mean":"rice cakes"},{"t":"খাওয়ালেন","mean":"fed (respectful)"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"প্রথমে আয়ান বাংলা বলতে লজ্জা পাচ্ছিল।","tr":"prothome ayan bangla bolte lojja pachchhilo.","mean":"At first, Ayan felt shy about speaking Bangla.","words":[{"t":"প্রথমে","mean":"at first"},{"t":"আয়ান","mean":"Ayan"},{"t":"বাংলা","mean":"Bangla"},{"t":"বলতে","mean":"to speak"},{"t":"লজ্জা","mean":"shyness"},{"t":"পাচ্ছিল","mean":"was feeling"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"নানু বললেন, \"ভুল হলে সমস্যা নেই, বলতে থাকো।\"","tr":"nanu bollen, \"bhul hole shomossha nei, bolte thako.\"","mean":"Nanu said, \"Mistakes are no problem. Keep talking.\"","words":[{"t":"নানু","mean":"Nanu"},{"t":"বললেন","mean":"said (respectful)"},{"t":"ভুল","mean":"mistake"},{"t":"হলে","mean":"if it happens"},{"t":"সমস্যা","mean":"problem"},{"t":"নেই","mean":"there is no"},{"t":"বলতে","mean":"speaking"},{"t":"থাকো","mean":"keep on"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"বিকেলে সে মামাতো ভাইদের সাথে নৌকায় চড়ল।","tr":"bikele she mamato bhaider shathe noukay chorlo.","mean":"In the afternoon he went on a boat with his cousins.","words":[{"t":"বিকেলে","mean":"in the afternoon"},{"t":"সে","mean":"he"},{"t":"মামাতো","mean":"maternal-uncle's"},{"t":"ভাইদের","mean":"brothers (cousins)"},{"t":"সাথে","mean":"with"},{"t":"নৌকায়","mean":"on a boat"},{"t":"চড়ল","mean":"rode"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাতে আয়ান বলল, \"নানু, আমি আবার আসব!\"","tr":"rate ayan bollo, \"nanu, ami abar ashbo!\"","mean":"At night Ayan said, \"Nanu, I'll come again!\"","words":[{"t":"রাতে","mean":"at night"},{"t":"আয়ান","mean":"Ayan"},{"t":"বলল","mean":"said"},{"t":"নানু","mean":"Nanu"},{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"আবার","mean":"again"},{"t":"আসব","mean":"will come"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Cousin word","Child of your…"],"rows":[["{{চাচাতো ভাই / বোন}}","father's brother ({{চাচা}})"],["{{ফুপাতো ভাই / বোন}}","father's sister ({{ফুপু}})"],["{{মামাতো ভাই / বোন}}","mother's brother ({{মামা}})"],["{{খালাতো ভাই / বোন}}","mother's sister ({{খালা}})"]],"title":"Cousins are 'brothers' and 'sisters'"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Many British Bangladeshi families have roots in Sylhet. Older relatives there may speak Sylheti, a regional way of speaking that sounds quite different. Standard Bangla, which you are learning, is understood all over Bangladesh."},{"type":"tip","kind":"tip","text":"Like Ayan, you will make mistakes, and that's fine! Family members are usually delighted when you try. Every sentence you say makes the next one easier."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the story aloud, then retell it in English to someone at home.","lines":["আয়ান লন্ডন থেকে প্রথমবার নানুবাড়িতে এসেছে।","গ্রামটা সিলেটে, চারপাশে সবুজ ধানক্ষেত।","ভোরে মোরগের ডাকে তার ঘুম ভাঙল।","নানু তাকে শীতের সকালে গরম ভাপা পিঠা খাওয়ালেন।","প্রথমে আয়ান বাংলা বলতে লজ্জা পাচ্ছিল।","নানু বললেন, \"ভুল হলে সমস্যা নেই, বলতে থাকো।\"","বিকেলে সে মামাতো ভাইদের সাথে নৌকায় চড়ল।","রাতে আয়ান বলল, \"নানু, আমি আবার আসব!\""]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Did you understand?","items":[{"q":"Where does Ayan usually live?","options":["Dhaka","Sylhet","New York City","London"],"answer":3},{"q":"What woke Ayan up?","options":["His alarm clock","A rooster","The rain","His cousin shouting"],"answer":1},{"q":"What did Nanu give him in the morning?","options":["Steamed rice cakes","Rice and fish curry","Biscuits","Tea"],"answer":0},{"q":"Why was Ayan quiet at first?","options":["He was too tired from the flight","He was angry","He was shy about his Bangla","He didn't like the food"],"answer":2},{"q":"Listen. What did Nanu tell him?","say":"ভুল হলে সমস্যা নেই, বলতে থাকো।","options":["Go to sleep now","Mistakes are fine, keep talking","Eat your pitha","Don't go down to the river on your own"],"answer":1},{"q":"Your mother's sister's son is your…","options":["চাচাতো ভাই","মামাতো ভাই","ফুপাতো ভাই","খালাতো ভাই"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{ঘুম ভাঙল}} means…","options":["fell asleep","woke up","had a dream","was tired"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u6-anthem","icon":"গান","title":"Amar Sonar Bangla","subtitle":"The opening lines of the national anthem of Bangladesh","minutes":15,"goals":["Read the opening lines of the anthem","Understand each word and image","Know who wrote it and when"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"{{আমার সোনার বাংলা}} ('My Golden Bengal') is the national anthem of Bangladesh. It was written by the great poet **Rabindranath Tagore**. Its words are a love song to the land of Bengal: its sky, its breeze and its mango groves."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Tagore (1861–1941) wrote this song in 1905, when the British split Bengal in two and many Bengalis protested. After Bangladesh became independent in 1971, the first ten lines of the song became the national anthem. Tagore was the first non-European to win the Nobel Prize in Literature (1913).","title":"About the song"},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"সোনার","tr":"shonar","mean":"golden (literally 'of gold')"},{"t":"তোমায়","tr":"tomay","mean":"you (old, poetic form of {{তোমাকে}})"},{"t":"ভালোবাসি","tr":"bhalobashi","mean":"I love"},{"t":"চিরদিন","tr":"chirodin","mean":"forever, always"},{"t":"আকাশ","tr":"akash","mean":"sky"},{"t":"বাতাস","tr":"batash","mean":"breeze, air"},{"t":"প্রাণ","tr":"pran","mean":"life, heart, soul"},{"t":"বাঁশি","tr":"banshi","mean":"bamboo flute"},{"t":"ফাগুন","tr":"phagun","mean":"Falgun, a spring month (= {{ফাল্গুন}})"},{"t":"ঘ্রাণ","tr":"ghran","mean":"fragrance, scent"}],"title":"Words in the song"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমার সোনার বাংলা, আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি।","tr":"amar shonar bangla, ami tomay bhalobashi.","mean":"My golden Bengal, I love you.","words":[{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"সোনার","mean":"golden"},{"t":"বাংলা","mean":"Bengal"},{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"তোমায়","mean":"you"},{"t":"ভালোবাসি","mean":"love"}],"title":"Line 1"},{"type":"sentence","t":"চিরদিন তোমার আকাশ, তোমার বাতাস, আমার প্রাণে","tr":"chirodin tomar akash, tomar batash, amar prane","mean":"Forever your sky, your breeze, in my heart…","words":[{"t":"চিরদিন","mean":"forever"},{"t":"তোমার","mean":"your"},{"t":"আকাশ","mean":"sky"},{"t":"তোমার","mean":"your"},{"t":"বাতাস","mean":"breeze"},{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"প্রাণে","mean":"in the heart"}],"title":"Line 2"},{"type":"sentence","t":"ও মা, আমার প্রাণে বাজায় বাঁশি।","tr":"o ma, amar prane bajay banshi.","mean":"…O Mother, play a flute in my heart.","words":[{"t":"ও","mean":"O"},{"t":"মা","mean":"Mother"},{"t":"আমার","mean":"my"},{"t":"প্রাণে","mean":"in the heart"},{"t":"বাজায়","mean":"plays"},{"t":"বাঁশি","mean":"flute"}],"note":"The poet speaks to Bengal as {{মা}}, a mother. Lines 2 and 3 together mean: 'Your sky and your breeze always play a flute in my heart.'","title":"Line 3"},{"type":"sentence","t":"ও মা, ফাগুনে তোর আমের বনে ঘ্রাণে পাগল করে,","tr":"o ma, phagune tor amer bone ghrane pagol kore,","mean":"O Mother, in spring the scent of your mango groves drives me wild with joy,","words":[{"t":"ও","mean":"O"},{"t":"মা","mean":"Mother"},{"t":"ফাগুনে","mean":"in Falgun (spring)"},{"t":"তোর","mean":"your (very close)"},{"t":"আমের","mean":"mango"},{"t":"বনে","mean":"in the groves"},{"t":"ঘ্রাণে","mean":"with the scent"},{"t":"পাগল","mean":"mad, wild"},{"t":"করে","mean":"makes"}],"title":"Line 4"},{"type":"sentence","t":"মরি হায়, হায় রে","tr":"mori hay, hay re","mean":"Ah, how wonderful, how wonderful!","words":[{"t":"মরি","mean":"I could die (of joy)"},{"t":"হায়","mean":"ah"},{"t":"হায়","mean":"ah"},{"t":"রে","mean":"oh"}],"note":"These are cries of deep feeling, like 'Oh, my heart!'","title":"Line 5"},{"type":"tip","kind":"memory","text":"Notice the poet first says {{তোমার}} (your) and then {{তোর}} (your, very close). {{তোর}} is how you talk to someone extremely dear, like your own mother. The love grows warmer as the song goes on."},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"When the national anthem is played, people stand up quietly to show respect. Schools in Bangladesh sing it at morning assembly."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read the opening lines slowly, like a poem. Then try to say them from memory.","lines":["আমার সোনার বাংলা, আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি।","চিরদিন তোমার আকাশ, তোমার বাতাস, আমার প্রাণে","ও মা, আমার প্রাণে বাজায় বাঁশি।","ও মা, ফাগুনে তোর আমের বনে ঘ্রাণে পাগল করে,","মরি হায়, হায় রে"]},{"type":"write","level":"line","items":["আমার সোনার বাংলা, আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি।"],"note":"Copy the first line neatly. Take care with the vowel signs in {{সোনার}} and {{ভালোবাসি}}."},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Who wrote {{আমার সোনার বাংলা}}?","options":["A modern pop singer","An unknown village singer","A British officer","Rabindranath Tagore"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{সোনার}} means…","options":["golden","silver","green","beautiful river"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does this line mean?","say":"আমার সোনার বাংলা, আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি।","options":["I love the sky","Mother, come home","My golden Bengal, I love you","Your mango groves are very big"],"answer":2},{"q":"In the song, Bengal is spoken to as…","options":["a friend","a queen","a mother","a child"],"answer":2},{"q":"What plays a flute in the poet's heart?","options":["The sky and breeze of Bengal","The rain","A shepherd boy out in the fields","The poet's mother"],"answer":0},{"q":"What fills the air with scent in spring?","options":["Rose gardens","Rice cooking","The sea","Mango groves"],"answer":3},{"q":"When the anthem plays, people…","options":["clap loudly","stand quietly","sit down","leave the room"],"answer":1}]}]},{"id":"u6-proverbs","icon":"প্রবাদ","title":"Proverbs & Idioms","subtitle":"Wise old sayings and colourful expressions","minutes":15,"goals":["Understand common Bangla proverbs","Use a few idioms in conversation","Compare them with English sayings"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bangla speakers love proverbs ({{প্রবাদ}}) and idioms ({{বাগধারা}}). Grandparents use them, and so do newspapers. Dropping one into a conversation always gets a smile!"},{"type":"examples","items":[{"t":"যেমন কর্ম তেমন ফল।","tr":"jemon kormo temon phol","mean":"As the deed, so the fruit.","note":"English: You reap what you sow."},{"t":"দশের লাঠি একের বোঝা।","tr":"dosher lathi eker bojha","mean":"Ten people's sticks are one person's load.","note":"English: Many hands make light work."},{"t":"চকচক করলেই সোনা হয় না।","tr":"chokchok korlei shona hoy na","mean":"Shining doesn't make it gold.","note":"English: All that glitters is not gold."},{"t":"যত গর্জে তত বর্ষে না।","tr":"joto gorje toto borshe na","mean":"It doesn't rain as much as it thunders.","note":"English: Barking dogs seldom bite. Big talk, little action."},{"t":"সময়ের এক ফোঁড়, অসময়ের দশ ফোঁড়।","tr":"shomoyer ek phor, oshomoyer dosh phor","mean":"One stitch on time, ten stitches too late.","note":"English: A stitch in time saves nine."},{"t":"নাচতে না জানলে উঠান বাঁকা।","tr":"nachte na janle uthan banka","mean":"If you can't dance, the courtyard is crooked.","note":"English: A bad worker blames his tools."},{"t":"অতি লোভে তাঁতি নষ্ট।","tr":"oti lobhe tanti noshto","mean":"Too much greed ruined the weaver.","note":"Greed leads to loss."},{"t":"অল্প বিদ্যা ভয়ংকরী।","tr":"olpo bidda bhoyonkori","mean":"A little learning is dangerous.","note":"Knowing only a little can make you overconfident."}],"title":"Everyday proverbs"},{"type":"sentence","t":"যত গর্জে তত বর্ষে না।","tr":"joto gorje toto borshe na.","mean":"It doesn't rain as much as it thunders.","words":[{"t":"যত","mean":"as much as"},{"t":"গর্জে","mean":"it thunders"},{"t":"তত","mean":"that much"},{"t":"বর্ষে","mean":"it rains"},{"t":"না","mean":"not"}],"note":"Say this about someone who makes big promises but does little."},{"type":"sentence","t":"দশের লাঠি একের বোঝা।","tr":"dosher lathi eker bojha.","mean":"Ten people's sticks are one person's load.","words":[{"t":"দশের","mean":"of ten (people)"},{"t":"লাঠি","mean":"sticks"},{"t":"একের","mean":"of one"},{"t":"বোঝা","mean":"burden"}],"note":"A heavy job is easy when everyone helps, but too much for one person."},{"type":"sentence","t":"চকচক করলেই সোনা হয় না।","tr":"chokchok korlei shona hoy na.","mean":"All that glitters is not gold.","words":[{"t":"চকচক","mean":"shiny"},{"t":"করলেই","mean":"just by doing (shining)"},{"t":"সোনা","mean":"gold"},{"t":"হয়","mean":"becomes"},{"t":"না","mean":"not"}]},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"মাথা গরম করা","tr":"matha gorom kora","mean":"to lose your temper (literally 'to heat the head')","example":{"t":"মাথা গরম কোরো না।","tr":"matha gorom koro na.","mean":"Don't lose your temper."}},{"t":"আকাশ থেকে পড়া","tr":"akash theke pora","mean":"to be stunned (literally 'to fall from the sky')","example":{"t":"খবরটা শুনে সে আকাশ থেকে পড়ল।","tr":"khoborta shune she akash theke porlo.","mean":"She was stunned when she heard the news."}},{"t":"চোখের মণি","tr":"chokher moni","mean":"the apple of someone's eye","example":{"t":"ছোট মেয়েটা সবার চোখের মণি।","tr":"chhoto meyeta shobar chokher moni.","mean":"The little girl is everyone's darling."}},{"t":"ডুমুরের ফুল","tr":"dumurer phul","mean":"someone you hardly ever see (literally 'a fig flower')","example":{"t":"তুমি তো ডুমুরের ফুল হয়ে গেছ!","tr":"tumi to dumurer phul hoye gechho!","mean":"We never see you any more!"}},{"t":"হাত লাগানো","tr":"hat lagano","mean":"to lend a hand","example":{"t":"সবাই মিলে হাত লাগাও।","tr":"shobai mile hat lagao.","mean":"Everyone, lend a hand together."}},{"t":"মুখে খই ফোটা","tr":"mukhe khoi phota","mean":"to talk non-stop (literally 'popcorn popping in the mouth')","example":{"t":"ওর মুখে খই ফোটে।","tr":"or mukhe khoi phote.","mean":"She never stops talking."}}],"title":"Colourful idioms"},{"type":"tip","kind":"fun","text":"Fig trees hide their flowers inside the fruit, so you never see a fig flower. That's why someone who rarely visits is called {{ডুমুরের ফুল}}. Aunties love saying this to relatives who don't visit often!"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Many proverbs come from village life: weavers, rain, courtyards and rice. They show how close Bengali culture is to the land and the seasons."},{"type":"practice","text":"Read each proverb aloud. Then think of a time in your life when one of them was true.","lines":["যেমন কর্ম তেমন ফল।","দশের লাঠি একের বোঝা।","চকচক করলেই সোনা হয় না।","যত গর্জে তত বর্ষে না।","সময়ের এক ফোঁড়, অসময়ের দশ ফোঁড়।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"Which proverb matches 'All that glitters is not gold'?","options":["চকচক করলেই সোনা হয় না।","যেমন কর্ম তেমন ফল।","অতি লোভে তাঁতি নষ্ট।","দশের লাঠি একের বোঝা।"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{মাথা গরম করা}} means…","options":["to have a fever","to wash your hair","to lose your temper","to think very hard about it"],"answer":2},{"q":"Your cousin never visits. Your aunt says he is a…","options":["চোখের মণি","ডুমুরের ফুল","মাথা গরম","সোনার বাংলা"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is the lesson of this proverb?","say":"দশের লাঠি একের বোঝা।","options":["Greed is bad","Gold is heavy to carry alone","Do it on time","Many hands make light work"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{আকাশ থেকে পড়া}} means…","options":["to fall over","to be stunned","to fly a kite","to look at the stars at night"],"answer":1},{"q":"Which proverb warns against greed?","options":["যত গর্জে তত বর্ষে না।","অল্প বিদ্যা ভয়ংকরী।","যেমন কর্ম তেমন ফল।","অতি লোভে তাঁতি নষ্ট।"],"answer":3},{"q":"Listen. Someone talks big but does little. Which proverb fits?","say":"যত গর্জে তত বর্ষে না।","options":["Too much thunder, little rain","A stitch in time","Fruit comes from your own deeds","Popcorn in the mouth"],"answer":0},{"q":"A Bangla word for 'idiom' is…","options":["প্রবাদ","উৎসব","বাগধারা","গল্প"],"answer":2}]}]},{"id":"u6-culture","icon":"সংস্কৃতি","title":"Festivals, Language & Food","subtitle":"Pohela Boishakh, 21 February, food culture and hospitality","minutes":18,"goals":["Know how Pohela Boishakh is celebrated","Understand why 21 February matters","Learn the manners of the Bangladeshi table"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Culture is the heart of a language. In this lesson you'll learn about the Bangla New Year, the Language Movement that gave the world Mother Language Day, and the food and hospitality Bangladesh is famous for."},{"type":"vocab","items":[{"t":"পহেলা বৈশাখ","tr":"pohela boishakh","mean":"first day of Boishakh (Bangla New Year)"},{"t":"মেলা","tr":"mela","mean":"fair"},{"t":"হালখাতা","tr":"halkhata","mean":"new account book opened by shops at New Year"},{"t":"পান্তা ভাত","tr":"panta bhat","mean":"rice soaked overnight in water"},{"t":"শোভাযাত্রা","tr":"shobhajatra","mean":"procession, parade"},{"t":"ভাষা","tr":"bhasha","mean":"language"},{"t":"মাতৃভাষা","tr":"matribhasha","mean":"mother tongue"},{"t":"শহিদ মিনার","tr":"shohid minar","mean":"Martyrs' Monument"},{"t":"প্রভাতফেরি","tr":"probhatpheri","mean":"dawn walk to the Shaheed Minar on 21 February"},{"t":"অতিথি","tr":"otithi","mean":"guest"}],"title":"Culture words"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"{{পহেলা বৈশাখ}} is the first day of the Bangla year, celebrated on 14 April in Bangladesh by people of every faith. People wear red and white, enjoy music at sunrise, visit fairs ({{মেলা}}) and join colourful processions with masks and giant figures. The Dhaka New Year procession was listed by UNESCO as intangible cultural heritage in 2016. Many families eat {{পান্তা ভাত}} with fried hilsa and spicy mashes ({{ভর্তা}}), and shopkeepers open a new account book ({{হালখাতা}}) and offer sweets to customers.","title":"Pohela Boishakh: Bangla New Year"},{"type":"sentence","t":"সবাইকে নববর্ষের শুভেচ্ছা।","tr":"shobaike nobobarsher shubhechchha.","mean":"New Year greetings to everyone.","words":[{"t":"সবাইকে","mean":"to everyone"},{"t":"নববর্ষের","mean":"of the New Year"},{"t":"শুভেচ্ছা","mean":"good wishes"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"In 1948, Pakistan's leaders announced that Urdu alone would be the state language, although most people in East Bengal (now Bangladesh) spoke Bangla. Students and citizens protested. On **21 February 1952**, police fired on protesters in Dhaka, and several were killed, among them Salam, Barkat, Rafiq and Jabbar. Bangla was finally recognised as a state language in 1956. In 1999 UNESCO declared 21 February **International Mother Language Day**, now observed around the world.","title":"21 February and the Language Movement"},{"type":"sentence","t":"রাষ্ট্রভাষা বাংলা চাই।","tr":"rashtrobhasha bangla chai.","mean":"We want Bangla as the state language.","words":[{"t":"রাষ্ট্রভাষা","mean":"state language"},{"t":"বাংলা","mean":"Bangla"},{"t":"চাই","mean":"we want"}],"note":"This was the famous slogan of the Language Movement."},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Ayan","t":"দাদু, আমরা একুশে ফেব্রুয়ারি কেন পালন করি?","tr":"dadu, amra ekushe phebruari keno palon kori?","mean":"Grandpa, why do we observe 21 February?"},{"who":"Dadu","t":"১৯৫২ সালের এই দিনে ছাত্ররা বাংলা ভাষার জন্য জীবন দিয়েছিল।","tr":"unish sho bayanno saler ei dine chhatrora bangla bhashar jonno jibon diyechhilo.","mean":"On this day in 1952, students gave their lives for the Bangla language."},{"who":"Ayan","t":"তারা কী চেয়েছিল?","tr":"tara ki cheyechhilo?","mean":"What did they want?"},{"who":"Dadu","t":"তারা চেয়েছিল, বাংলা হবে রাষ্ট্রভাষা।","tr":"tara cheyechhilo, bangla hobe rashtrobhasha.","mean":"They wanted Bangla to be a state language."},{"who":"Ayan","t":"তাই কি আমরা শহিদ মিনারে ফুল দিই?","tr":"tai ki amra shohid minare phul dii?","mean":"Is that why we lay flowers at the Shaheed Minar?"},{"who":"Dadu","t":"হ্যাঁ। এখন সারা পৃথিবী দিনটাকে মাতৃভাষা দিবস হিসেবে পালন করে।","tr":"hya. ekhon shara prithibi dintake matribhasha dibosh hishebe palon kore.","mean":"Yes. Now the whole world observes the day as Mother Language Day."},{"who":"Ayan","t":"তাহলে আমি ভালো করে বাংলা শিখে তাঁদের সম্মান জানাব!","tr":"tahole ami bhalo kore bangla shikhe tander shomman janabo!","mean":"Then I'll honour them by learning Bangla well!"}],"title":"Why we remember 21 February"},{"type":"steps","items":[{"title":"Midnight","desc":"Just after midnight, national leaders and the public begin laying flowers at the Central Shaheed Minar in Dhaka."},{"title":"Dawn walk","t":"প্রভাতফেরি","tr":"probhatpheri","mean":"dawn procession","desc":"At dawn, people walk barefoot to their local Shaheed Minar, often singing songs of the Language Movement."},{"title":"Flowers","t":"ফুল দেওয়া","tr":"phul deoa","mean":"laying flowers","desc":"Wreaths and flowers are placed at the foot of the monument."},{"title":"Remembering","t":"শহিদ দিবস","tr":"shohid dibosh","mean":"Martyrs' Day","desc":"Many people wear black badges. It is a public holiday and a day of quiet respect."}],"title":"How 21 February is observed"},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"There is a famous saying: {{মাছে-ভাতে বাঙালি}}, 'Fish and rice make a Bengali.' Rice is eaten at almost every meal, and the hilsa ({{ইলিশ}}) is the national fish. Winter brings many kinds of {{পিঠা}} (rice cakes), and good news is always shared with sweets ({{মিষ্টিমুখ}}).","title":"Food culture"},{"type":"sentence","t":"মাছে-ভাতে বাঙালি।","tr":"machhe-bhate bangali.","mean":"Fish and rice make a Bengali.","words":[{"t":"মাছে-ভাতে","mean":"with fish and rice"},{"t":"বাঙালি","mean":"Bengali (person)"}]},{"type":"tip","kind":"culture","text":"Guests are treated with great honour. The host serves guests first, offers the best pieces, and keeps putting more food on your plate. When you are truly full, say so politely, with a smile and a compliment for the food.","title":"Hospitality"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আরেকটু নিন।","tr":"arektu nin.","mean":"Have a little more.","words":[{"t":"আরেকটু","mean":"a little more"},{"t":"নিন","mean":"take (polite)"}],"note":"You will hear this many times as a guest!"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আর না, পেট ভরে গেছে।","tr":"ar na, pet bhore gechhe.","mean":"No more, thank you. I'm full.","words":[{"t":"আর","mean":"more"},{"t":"না","mean":"no"},{"t":"পেট","mean":"stomach"},{"t":"ভরে","mean":"filled"},{"t":"গেছে","mean":"has become"}]},{"type":"practice","text":"Read aloud.","lines":["শুভ নববর্ষ!","রাষ্ট্রভাষা বাংলা চাই।","মাছে-ভাতে বাঙালি।","আরেকটু নিন।","আর না, পেট ভরে গেছে।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Quick quiz","items":[{"q":"On which date is Pohela Boishakh celebrated in Bangladesh?","options":["21 February","16 December","14 April","1 January"],"answer":2},{"q":"What colours do people traditionally wear for Pohela Boishakh?","options":["Red and white","Black and grey","Blue and yellow","Green only"],"answer":0},{"q":"Why is 21 February remembered?","options":["For Bangla New Year","For the end of Ramadan","For the start of the monsoon","For the Language Movement of 1952"],"answer":3},{"q":"UNESCO made 21 February…","options":["World Food Day","International Mother Language Day","The first day of the Bangla New Year","Victory Day"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is this slogan asking for?","say":"রাষ্ট্রভাষা বাংলা চাই।","options":["Bangla as the state language","More rice and fish","A new year","A holiday"],"answer":0},{"q":"{{প্রভাতফেরি}} is…","options":["a New Year fair with music and food","a boat race","a dawn walk to the Shaheed Minar","a sweet shop"],"answer":2},{"q":"The national fish of Bangladesh is the…","options":["rui (a river carp)","hilsa (ইলিশ)","shrimp","catfish"],"answer":1},{"q":"Listen. What is the guest saying?","say":"আর না, পেট ভরে গেছে।","options":["More, please","It's too spicy","Where's the water?","I'm full"],"answer":3}]}]},{"id":"u6-review","icon":"শেষ","title":"Final Review Lab","subtitle":"Put everything together: speak, read, listen and write","minutes":20,"goals":["Follow a longer real-life conversation","Build and read sentences confidently","Check what you can do now"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Congratulations on reaching the final lesson! This lab mixes everything: greetings, family, food, weather, directions and culture. Take your time and enjoy how much you can understand now."},{"type":"dialogue","lines":[{"who":"Nadia","t":"আসসালামু আলাইকুম। আপনি কি এখানে নতুন?","tr":"assalamu alaikum. apni ki ekhane notun?","mean":"Hello. Are you new here?"},{"who":"Tom","t":"ওয়ালাইকুম আসসালাম। জি, আমি টম। আমি বাংলা শিখছি।","tr":"walaikum assalam. ji, ami tom. ami bangla shikhchhi.","mean":"Hello. Yes, I'm Tom. I'm learning Bangla."},{"who":"Nadia","t":"বাহ্, আপনি তো সুন্দর বাংলা বলেন!","tr":"bah, apni to shundor bangla bolen!","mean":"Wow, you speak Bangla beautifully!"},{"who":"Tom","t":"ধন্যবাদ! একটু একটু পারি।","tr":"dhonnobad! ektu ektu pari.","mean":"Thanks! I can manage a little."},{"who":"Nadia","t":"চা খাবেন? এখানে কাছেই একটা ভালো চায়ের দোকান আছে।","tr":"cha khaben? ekhane kachhei ekta bhalo chayer dokan achhe.","mean":"Would you like some tea? There's a good tea stall close by."},{"who":"Tom","t":"অবশ্যই! আজ খুব গরম, তাই না?","tr":"obosshoi! aj khub gorom, tai na?","mean":"Of course! It's very hot today, isn't it?"},{"who":"Nadia","t":"হ্যাঁ। বিকেলে বৃষ্টি আসতে পারে।","tr":"hya. bikele brishti ashte pare.","mean":"Yes. It might rain this afternoon."},{"who":"Tom","t":"তাহলে চা আর বৃষ্টি, দুটোই উপভোগ করব!","tr":"tahole cha ar brishti, dutoi upobhog korbo!","mean":"Then I'll enjoy both the tea and the rain!"},{"who":"Nadia","t":"আপনার সাথে কথা বলে খুব ভালো লাগল।","tr":"apnar shathe kotha bole khub bhalo laglo.","mean":"It was really nice talking to you."},{"who":"Tom","t":"আমারও। আবার দেখা হবে!","tr":"amaro. abar dekha hobe!","mean":"Me too. See you again!"}],"title":"A new friend"},{"type":"sentence","t":"আমি বাংলা শিখছি।","tr":"ami bangla shikhchhi.","mean":"I am learning Bangla.","words":[{"t":"আমি","mean":"I"},{"t":"বাংলা","mean":"Bangla"},{"t":"শিখছি","mean":"am learning"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"একটু একটু পারি।","tr":"ektu ektu pari.","mean":"I can manage a little.","words":[{"t":"একটু","mean":"a little"},{"t":"একটু","mean":"a little"},{"t":"পারি","mean":"I can"}],"note":"A modest and very useful answer when someone praises your Bangla."},{"type":"sentence","t":"আপনার সাথে কথা বলে খুব ভালো লাগল।","tr":"apnar shathe kotha bole khub bhalo laglo.","mean":"It was really nice talking to you.","words":[{"t":"আপনার","mean":"your"},{"t":"সাথে","mean":"with"},{"t":"কথা","mean":"talk"},{"t":"বলে","mean":"having spoken"},{"t":"খুব","mean":"very"},{"t":"ভালো","mean":"good"},{"t":"লাগল","mean":"felt"}]},{"type":"sentence","t":"আবার দেখা হবে।","tr":"abar dekha hobe.","mean":"See you again.","words":[{"t":"আবার","mean":"again"},{"t":"দেখা","mean":"meeting"},{"t":"হবে","mean":"will happen"}]},{"type":"table","head":["Situation","Key phrase","Meaning"],"rows":[["Bazaar","{{একটু কম রাখুন।}}","Make it a bit cheaper."],["Rickshaw","{{মামা, যাবেন?}}","Uncle, will you go?"],["Tea stall","{{এক কাপ চা দিন।}}","A cup of tea, please."],["Phone","{{আচ্ছা, রাখি।}}","Okay, bye for now."],["Doctor","{{আমার মাথা ব্যথা করছে।}}","I have a headache."],["Directions","{{এখানে কাছে কোনো ফার্মেসি আছে?}}","Is there a pharmacy near here?"],["Visiting","{{আজ তাহলে উঠি।}}","I'd better get going now."],["Festival","{{ঈদ মোবারক! / শুভ নববর্ষ!}}","Eid Mubarak! / Happy New Year!"]],"title":"Your survival phrases"},{"type":"dictation","items":[{"t":"এক কাপ চা দিন।","tr":"ek kap cha din.","mean":"A cup of tea, please."},{"t":"ভাড়া কত?","tr":"bhara koto?","mean":"How much is the fare?"},{"t":"আজ খুব গরম।","tr":"aj khub gorom.","mean":"It's very hot today."},{"t":"আমি বাংলা শিখছি।","tr":"ami bangla shikhchhi.","mean":"I am learning Bangla."},{"t":"আবার দেখা হবে।","tr":"abar dekha hobe.","mean":"See you again."}],"title":"Listen and write"},{"type":"write","level":"line","items":["আমি বাংলা শিখছি।","আপনার সাথে কথা বলে খুব ভালো লাগল।"],"note":"Copy each line twice. Read it aloud as you write."},{"type":"selfcheck","items":["I can buy things at a bazaar and bargain politely.","I can take a rickshaw or CNG and give simple directions.","I can order tea and food and ask for the bill.","I can introduce myself and talk about my family.","I can make and end a short phone call.","I can tell a doctor what hurts.","I can greet people correctly at Eid, New Year and Puja.","I can read a short story in Bangla script.","I know the opening lines of {{আমার সোনার বাংলা}} and what they mean.","I can explain why 21 February is important."],"title":"What can you do now?"},{"type":"practice","text":"Final challenge: read these aloud as smoothly as you can.","lines":["আসসালামু আলাইকুম। আমি বাংলা শিখছি।","মামা, আলুর কেজি কত?","সোজা গিয়ে ডানে যান।","বাইরে ঝুম বৃষ্টি হচ্ছে।","আমার সোনার বাংলা, আমি তোমায় ভালোবাসি।","আপনার সাথে কথা বলে খুব ভালো লাগল।"]},{"type":"quiz","title":"Final quiz","items":[{"q":"Listen. Where would you hear this?","say":"মামা, যাবেন?","options":["At the doctor's","In a rickshaw","On the phone","At a wedding"],"answer":1},{"q":"Someone praises your Bangla. A modest reply is…","options":["আমি বাংলা জানি না।","বিলটা দিন।","আজ তাহলে উঠি।","একটু একটু পারি।"],"answer":3},{"q":"{{আবার দেখা হবে}} means…","options":["See you again","Look again","Come back now","I don't see it"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What is the problem?","say":"আমার পেট ব্যথা করছে।","options":["A headache","A very sore throat","A stomach ache","A broken leg"],"answer":2},{"q":"Which greeting is right for Durga Puja?","options":["ঈদ মোবারক","শুভ বড়দিন","শারদীয় শুভেচ্ছা","আল্লাহ হাফেজ"],"answer":2},{"q":"{{তাই না?}} at the end of a sentence means…","options":["isn't it?","why not?","that's all","not that one"],"answer":0},{"q":"Listen. What does the speaker want?","say":"এক কাপ চা দিন।","options":["A bottle of water","Two kilos of rice","The bill","A cup of tea"],"answer":3},{"q":"What did students demand on 21 February 1952?","options":["A new national anthem","Bangla as a state language","Free rickshaws","A New Year holiday"],"answer":1}]}]}]});
